  '<p class="gd-p">Your booking is confirmed. A few things are left: your licence photos, a selfie and proof of coverage, a signature from each additional driver, and the deposit.</p><section class="gd-task" id="before-pickup-what-we-still-need-from-you" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">What we still need from you</h2><p class="gd-p">While a request or booking is not complete, everything it still needs is in one list, <b class="gd-ui">To do</b>, under the steps on <b class="gd-ui">Trips</b> and on the booking: one line for each thing, with its state and a small button. The red button of <b class="gd-ui">Do this next</b> is always the first thing to do.</p><div class="gd-tablewrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Table"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">State</th><th scope="col">What it means</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Needed</td><td>Send it: press the button on the line</td></tr><tr><td>Not accepted</td><td>We could not accept what you sent: the reason is on the line, send it again</td></tr><tr><td>Under review</td><td>We have it and a person on our team is checking it</td></tr><tr><td>Done</td><td>Nothing more to do</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class="gd-p">The lines are what this booking needs: your licence (front and back) and a selfie for each driver, proof of coverage (not with the Protection Plan), signing and paying, the deposit, each additional driver accepting the terms, your date of birth and your home address. On the booking, the details the agreement needs are filled in right there, under <b class="gd-ui">Your details for the agreement</b>. Our reminders name the same things.</p><p class="gd-p">Each line says exactly what is missing. With your own insurance (OPCF 27) you send two pages: the <b class="gd-ui">pink slip</b> (the insurance card for your own car) and the <b class="gd-ui">OPCF 27 endorsement page</b> of your policy. If one is missing, the line says which one (&quot;We have your OPCF 27 endorsement page. Still needed: your pink slip&quot;), and its button opens that upload with the page chosen. Next to each upload is an example picture of the page with the parts that must show circled: your name, the policy number, the dates, the insurer and, on the endorsement page, the OPCF 27 line. Find it in your insurer&#39;s app or website, in your email, or in your car&#39;s glovebox. Put it flat, get all four corners in the photo, and avoid glare.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="before-pickup-your-booking-page" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Your booking page</h2><p class="gd-p">Every booking opens with a large photo of your car, its name, the status and a clock: &quot;Pickup in 2 days 4 h&quot;, or &quot;Return by Sun 7 PM&quot; while you have the car.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Trips</b>, then your booking. The status is on the photo, for example Confirmed, with your booking number.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Under the photo: when and where you pick up and return the car (tap a place to open it in Maps), the kilometres included, the fuel rule and the deposit.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Do this next</b>, at the top, tells you the one thing still needed, with its red button, for example <b class="gd-ui">Upload documents</b>, and the time left before pickup. Under it, your steps: done, now (<b class="gd-ui">Your turn</b>) and later. When nothing is needed it says when and where to pick up the car, with <b class="gd-ui">Add to calendar</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Manage your trip holds <b class="gd-ui">Licence and coverage</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Extend</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Ask to change dates</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Message us</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Call us</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Add a driver</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Documents</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Cancel booking</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/account/bookings/CC-10003</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/972"><img src="/guides/img/renter-08-booking-confirmed-desktop-b5603da5.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="972"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:10.4%;top:54.9%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:9.4%;top:78.9%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:92.4%;top:76.9%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div><p class="gd-p">Money, on the right (below on a phone), shows what you paid and what is owing, part by part, with a <b class="gd-ui">Pay</b> button when something is open and your receipts. <b class="gd-ui">Price details</b> opens every line of the price. The steps under <b class="gd-ui">Do this next</b> show how far along you are: approve the offer, sign and pay, licence and insurance, pick up, return, final statement. A step finished since your last visit ticks over as the bar moves.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="before-pickup-your-rental-step-by-step" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Your rental, step by step</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Your rental, step by step</b> on your booking opens the walkthrough: the whole rental in four stages, Before pickup, At pickup, On the road and The return.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Start the walkthrough</b> (<b class="gd-ui">Continue</b> once you have begun). The top shows how many steps are done and which stage you are at.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The step to do now is in black at the top. A task opens its page, for example <b class="gd-ui">Add your licence</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Sign the agreement</b>, and is ticked once it is done. A step to read (what to bring, where we meet, your own photos, the road rules, what to do if something goes wrong, how to bring the car back) has <b class="gd-ui">Got it</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">At pickup, the walk-around: we photograph the car with you and you sign the condition report on your phone. Once done, <b class="gd-ui">See the photo report</b> opens every photo.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Every stage is listed below with its steps, so you can read ahead.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="before-pickup-upload-your-licence-selfie-and-coverage" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Upload your licence, selfie and coverage</h2><p class="gd-p">Do this at least 24 hours before pickup. It takes a few minutes with your phone.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On your booking, press <b class="gd-ui">Upload documents</b> (or <b class="gd-ui">Licence and coverage</b>).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Licence, front: lay the licence on a dark surface with all four corners visible. Press <b class="gd-ui">Take a photo</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Choose from my photos</b> for a photo already on your phone.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Licence, back: do the same for the back.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Selfie with your licence: hold the licence beside your face, then press <b class="gd-ui">Take selfie</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Coverage for damage to the car: add what your option asks for, then press <b class="gd-ui">Take a photo</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Choose from my photos</b> (a PDF works too). Not sure your credit card covers rentals? Use the card coverage checker first.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">While your booking still needs them, <b class="gd-ui">Your trips</b> shows <b class="gd-ui">Upload your licence</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Upload proof of insurance</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Check if your credit card covers rentals</b>, and our request and offer emails link straight to the licence upload.</p><div class="gd-figblock"><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/account/bookings/CC-10003/verify</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/1232"><img src="/guides/img/renter-09-verify-desktop-d20f668d.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="1232"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:18.5%;top:65.3%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:50%;top:63.6%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:81.2%;top:63.6%" aria-hidden="true">4</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:50%;top:95.3%" aria-hidden="true">5</span></div></div></figure></div><div class="gd-tablewrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Table"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Your option</th><th scope="col">What we need</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Option 1, OPCF 27 on your own policy</td><td>Your insurer, the policy number and its expiry (after your return date), then two pages: your <b class="gd-ui">pink slip</b> (the liability insurance card) and the <b class="gd-ui">OPCF 27 endorsement page</b>, each a PDF or a photo. Send both before you pay: the payment opens once they are in.</td></tr><tr><td>Option 2, your credit card&#39;s rental coverage</td><td>Pay with that card: it must be a credit card (debit and prepaid cards are refused) in your name. Search for your card (the bank and the card&#39;s name) and pick it: the page tells you at once whether it covers this car (the card&#39;s value limit, the kinds of car it leaves out, the most days). Then tick and confirm. Not on the list? Tick <b class="gd-ui">My card is not on the list</b> and type its name: our team checks it. The card&#39;s benefits document is optional.</td></tr><tr><td>Option 3, the CarmaCars Protection Plan</td><td>Ask for it on your booking; we confirm it once it is active.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Which cards include rental car coverage? <span class="gd-url">carmacars.ca/credit-card-rental-coverage</span> lists them, with each card&#39;s car value limit (MSRP), its longest rental and a link to its guide. Most cards stop at a car priced $65,000 or $85,000, and some of our cars are priced higher. Only your card&#39;s issuer decides a claim: call the number on the back of your card before you rent.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>A person checks your proof and approves it, or tells you what to fix. The car is handed over only once it is approved. Changing your option replaces the earlier proof. We remind you 48 and 24 hours before pickup while it is missing. We delete licence and face photos 90 days after your rental ends.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="before-pickup-additional-drivers" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Additional drivers</h2><p class="gd-p">Each additional driver signs the agreement with their own link.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">When the agreement is ready, each driver with an email gets their own signing link.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">On your booking, press <b class="gd-ui">Copy their signing link</b> to send it yourself, or <b class="gd-ui">Send a new link</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Each driver adds their own licence photos and selfie, like you did.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>Signing links expire after 72 hours. A new link ends the older one, so always send the newest.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="before-pickup-add-something-to-your-trip" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Add something to your trip</h2><p class="gd-p">Until 24 hours before pickup (or the notice an add-on needs), add add-ons from your booking.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On your booking, under Add-ons, press <b class="gd-ui">Add something to your trip</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Tick the add-on you want. Its price shows below.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Add and pay</b>. It is charged at once on the card you paid with, and shows on your booking and receipt.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A chauffeur needs our confirmation: press <b class="gd-ui">Ask for it</b>. We confirm it and charge your card then.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">No card on file for this booking? The add-on is added and waits for payment: press <b class="gd-ui">Pay for your add-ons</b> under Add-ons, enter a card and press <b class="gd-ui">Pay</b>. It is charged at once; that card is not kept.</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>If you cancel, add-ons are refunded like the rest of your booking. Flowers and a chauffeur are not refunded once their notice before pickup has started.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="before-pickup-what-to-bring-to-pickup" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">What to bring to pickup</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Your original licence. A photo is not enough.</li><li>The card you paid with. The deposit is taken on it about an hour before pickup.</li><li>A few minutes to walk around the car with us. We photograph it together.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="before-pickup-check-in-yourself-release-28" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Check in yourself (release 28)</h2><p class="gd-p">From 24 hours before pickup, <b class="gd-ui">Check in yourself</b> on your booking: take the photos of the car as you get it (pick them all at once from your camera roll: all sides, odometer, fuel gauge, inside, any damage), the odometer and the fuel. If your booking is ready, you are checked in at once; otherwise a team member confirms it. If you do not take the photos, we take them.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Confirm it is you</b> is an optional step on the same page: take a photo of your licence and a selfie at that moment. We compare them with the ones on your booking, so the car goes to you and nobody else. You can skip it, and it never holds up your check-in. The photos are deleted with your other licence and face photos, 90 days after your rental ends.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="before-pickup-if-we-change-your-coverage-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">If we change your coverage (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">If your card does not cover the car, or you ask for the CarmaCars Protection Plan, our team can switch your booking for you. You get an email with what changed and the new total. On an offer you approve the new price. On a booking you have paid, any extra is sent to you as a secure payment link, or you pay it from your booking page. You then do not need to send a card coverage document. If you go back to your card, the booking page asks you to confirm it again.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="before-pickup-your-accident-card" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Your accident card</h2><p class="gd-p">Your booking shows your <b class="gd-ui">Accident card</b>: what to do after an accident, and the coverage of this booking.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>With your own auto policy (OPCF 27): your insurer and policy number, as on the proof you uploaded.</li><li>With your credit card coverage: the card and its coverage provider.</li><li>With the Protection Plan: the provider, the policy number, the claims phone and your plan reference.</li></ul><p class="gd-p">Press <b class="gd-ui">Print it</b> to print the card at its size for the glovebox, or keep the page on your phone.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">Your name and date of birth</h3><p class="gd-p">Set them in your profile. Once your licence is verified they must match it: a change is sent as a correction request, shown as waiting until our team checks it against your licence.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="before-pickup-if-your-card-does-not-cover-the-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">If your card does not cover the car</h2><p class="gd-p">The page says why: the card has no rental car damage coverage, the car is worth more than the card&#39;s limit, the card leaves out this kind of car, or the rental is longer than the card allows. Choose <b class="gd-ui">Use OPCF 27 on my policy instead</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Ask for the Protection Plan</b> just below.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="before-pickup-change-my-protection" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Change my protection</h2><p class="gd-p">How damage to the car is covered can be changed on your booking page, under <b class="gd-ui">Protection</b>, once you approve the offer and until you return the car.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Change my protection</b>. You see the three options with their prices: your own insurance (OPCF 27), your credit card&#39;s coverage, or the CarmaCars Protection Plan.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Credit card coverage: choose your card from our list. It counts only if that card covers this car, and you tick that you will pay with it. Otherwise, OPCF 27: tick that you will upload your policy (the pink slip and the endorsement page). Otherwise, the Protection Plan.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The Protection Plan applies at once: pay the difference with <b class="gd-ui">Pay</b> on your booking. Moving off the Protection Plan needs your proof (a photo or PDF); our team checks it and the change applies once approved. You can withdraw the request while it waits.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">During your trip you can add the Protection Plan; your own insurance or card coverage is set before pickup. After damage is reported, the protection stays as it was.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('renter', 'during-your-trip', 'chapter', 'before-pickup', 'Plans change. You can ask for more days, ask to change dates, answer a change we suggest, or cancel, all from your booking.

## Extend your rental

1. On your booking, press **Extend**.
2. Pick how long: **1 hour**, **3 hours**, **1 day**, **3 days**, **1 week** or **1 month**. Each shows the new return and its price, HST included: each added day costs your booking''s price a day (what you paid for it, fees and HST included, divided by its days). An option the car cannot take is greyed out with the reason, and the page says until when the car is free.
3. Press **Pay** to pay with your card on file. When the car is free it is approved at once and the page shows your new return. No card on file, or the card is declined? The secure payment page opens: enter a card there. Otherwise the request goes to our team, and once approved you pay on the same page.
4. For another date, open **Another date and time**, choose it, press **See the price**, then **Request extension**.

![](/guides/img/renter-11-extend-desktop-957274cc.jpg "desktop; size: 960 552; address: carmacars.ca/account/bookings/CC-10003/extend; pins: 2 34.4 62.9, 3 15.1 77.2")

> Tip: A few hours cost the hourly late fee, never more than a day, so extending never costs more than being late, and it keeps your trip covered. Already past your return time and still have the car? You can still extend. It counts from your original return time, and the late charges stay owed until the extension is paid.

## Ask to change dates

1. On your booking, press **Ask to change dates**.
2. Set the new pickup and return, then press **See the difference** to see what you would pay or get back.
3. Press **Ask to change dates** to send it. Nothing changes until you agree to our answer.

![](/guides/img/renter-12-change-desktop-09f6b563.jpg "desktop; size: 960 552; address: carmacars.ca/account/bookings/CC-10003/change; pins: 2 15.1 91.8")

## A change we suggest

Sometimes we need to change your booking, for example another car of the same class. You decide.

1. You get an email, and your booking says "We suggest a change to your booking". Press **Review and answer**.
2. Read what changes (before and after), the reason, the money and the time left to answer.
3. To agree, press **Accept and sign the amendment**, sign, then press **Accept and sign**.
4. Anything more to pay is charged to your Card on File. If the card is declined, press **Pay and apply the change**.
5. To say no, press **Decline this change**. Your booking stays as it was.

> Tip: You have 48 hours to answer, and we send one reminder. CarmaCars signs the amendment at the moment you sign it, and the signed copy is saved under Documents. If the change costs less, the refund goes back to your card within 10 business days after the amendment is signed.

## Cancel a booking

1. On your booking, press **Cancel booking**.
2. Read What you get back. It shows the rule that applies and your refund.
3. Type the booking number to confirm (for example CC-10021), then press **Cancel booking**.

![](/guides/img/renter-13-cancel-desktop-d0bb2c67.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 692; address: carmacars.ca/account/bookings/CC-10003/cancel; pins: 2 36.1 67.2, 3 95.8 45.1")

| Standard booking: when you cancel | Refund of what you paid |
| --- | --- |
| Within 24 hours of booking, and 48 hours or more before pickup | 95% back |
| 48 hours or more before pickup | 75% back |
| 24 to 48 hours before pickup | 50% back |
| Less than 24 hours before pickup | No refund |

A Non-refundable booking gets no refund. The deposit is taken at pickup, so none is held when you cancel before it.

## Messages, tolls and tickets

- On a rental of 2 days or more we check in after the first day: "How is the car?" If anything is off, reply to the email or text, or call us.
- Write to us about a booking at the bottom of its page: type in Your message and press Send.
- Tolls and tickets are yours to pay, including Highway 407 ETR. If one reaches us, we pay it and charge the amount plus our fee to your Card on File, and email you a copy of the notice.
- Running late? Extend in your booking, even after the return time while you still have the car, or call us at 289-312-5991. The late fee is 17.5% of the daily rate for each started hour (at least $25) after a 30 minute grace.
- Before your return we remind you: the day before, about 3 hours before (with an Extend link) and at the return time. If the car is late we send a notice at 15 minutes and a final notice at 2 hours. No late notices between 10 pm and 7 am.
- Already brought the car back but still getting late notices? Tap **I''ve returned the car** in the notice, or press it on your booking. Add photos of the car where you left it (pick several at once from your camera roll), the odometer, the fuel level and the time you returned it: all optional. The late notices stop at once while we check. When we confirm, your trip is complete. If we cannot find the car, we tell you why and the notices start again.
- Something wrong with the car? While you have it, press **Report a problem** on your booking: it calls roadside help, or opens a message to us.
- Someone else will drive too? Press **Add a driver**: write their name in the message and we add them; they sign with their own link.

## Return the car yourself (release 28)

**Return the car yourself** on your booking: photos of the car where you left it, the odometer, the fuel and the time. With all of them your trip is completed at once and any late notices stop; we may still adjust the readings after we see the car.

## Report an accident

While you have the car, the **Accident card** on your booking has **Report an accident**. Anyone hurt? Call 911 first.

1. Say what happened, when (empty means now) and where: type it or press **Use my location**.
2. Add photos and videos from your camera roll: all the cars, the plates, the damage and the scene.
3. Add the other party''s name, phone, plate and their insurer, and the police report number if there is one.
4. Answer **Is anyone hurt?** and **Can the car be driven?**, then press **Send the report**.

Your answers stay on your phone as you type until you send them. Once sent, our team has it at once and calls you; the page shows the next steps, **Call us**, and lets you add more photos or videos.

## Extend at the same rate (release 35)

An extension costs the same a day as your booking, and per-trip fees such as the Protection Plan are charged for the added days at the same rate. Delivery is never charged again. The price shows before you ask.

## Secondary contact and rideshare documents

Open **More** on your booking page:

- **Secondary contact**: someone we may call if we cannot reach you, for this trip or on your profile. Optional.
- **Rideshare or delivery documents**: rideshare and delivery driving are welcome. Driving for Uber, Lyft, DoorDash, Uber Eats, Instacart or another platform? Pick the platforms and print the documents they ask for: your rental agreement, a coverage letter and a vehicle letter.

## Rideshare, a second contact and a mid-trip check (release 35)

- Driving for Uber, Lyft, DoorDash, Uber Eats, Instacart or another platform is allowed: your booking page makes the documents they ask for.
- Add a secondary contact we can call if we cannot reach you, on your profile or for one trip.
- Halfway through a longer trip we send one short message asking how it is going. Reply with any problem and our team picks it up.
- We send no automatic text at night; an answer asked for then arrives in the morning. Common questions are answered at once, and a person answers anything else.

## Deposit still owed (release 48)
If you picked up the car before the deposit hold was placed, your booking page says **Deposit still owed** with the amount. It is a hold on your credit card, not a charge, released after the rental. We try your saved card each morning; if that does not work we send you a secure link by text or email. Tap it to place the hold, or call us.', 'During your trip', 'Extend, change dates, answer a change we suggest, or cancel.',
  'Plans change. You can ask for more days, ask to change dates, answer a change we suggest, or cancel, all from your booking.

## Extend your rental

1. On your booking, press **Extend**.
2. Pick how long: **1 hour**, **3 hours**, **1 day**, **3 days**, **1 week** or **1 month**. Each shows the new return and its price, HST included: each added day costs your booking''s price a day (what you paid for it, fees and HST included, divided by its days). An option the car cannot take is greyed out with the reason, and the page says until when the car is free.
3. Press **Pay** to pay with your card on file. When the car is free it is approved at once and the page shows your new return. No card on file, or the card is declined? The secure payment page opens: enter a card there. Otherwise the request goes to our team, and once approved you pay on the same page.
4. For another date, open **Another date and time**, choose it, press **See the price**, then **Request extension**.

![](/guides/img/renter-11-extend-desktop-957274cc.jpg "desktop; size: 960 552; address: carmacars.ca/account/bookings/CC-10003/extend; pins: 2 34.4 62.9, 3 15.1 77.2")

> Tip: A few hours cost the hourly late fee, never more than a day, so extending never costs more than being late, and it keeps your trip covered. Already past your return time and still have the car? You can still extend. It counts from your original return time, and the late charges stay owed until the extension is paid.

## Ask to change dates

1. On your booking, press **Ask to change dates**.
2. Set the new pickup and return, then press **See the difference** to see what you would pay or get back.
3. Press **Ask to change dates** to send it. Nothing changes until you agree to our answer.

![](/guides/img/renter-12-change-desktop-09f6b563.jpg "desktop; size: 960 552; address: carmacars.ca/account/bookings/CC-10003/change; pins: 2 15.1 91.8")

## A change we suggest

Sometimes we need to change your booking, for example another car of the same class. You decide.

1. You get an email, and your booking says "We suggest a change to your booking". Press **Review and answer**.
2. Read what changes (before and after), the reason, the money and the time left to answer.
3. To agree, press **Accept and sign the amendment**, sign, then press **Accept and sign**.
4. Anything more to pay is charged to your Card on File. If the card is declined, press **Pay and apply the change**.
5. To say no, press **Decline this change**. Your booking stays as it was.

> Tip: You have 48 hours to answer, and we send one reminder. CarmaCars signs the amendment at the moment you sign it, and the signed copy is saved under Documents. If the change costs less, the refund goes back to your card within 10 business days after the amendment is signed.

## Cancel a booking

1. On your booking, press **Cancel booking**.
2. Read What you get back. It shows the rule that applies and your refund.
3. Type the booking number to confirm (for example CC-10021), then press **Cancel booking**.

![](/guides/img/renter-13-cancel-desktop-d0bb2c67.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 692; address: carmacars.ca/account/bookings/CC-10003/cancel; pins: 2 36.1 67.2, 3 95.8 45.1")

| Standard booking: when you cancel | Refund of what you paid |
| --- | --- |
| Within 24 hours of booking, and 48 hours or more before pickup | 95% back |
| 48 hours or more before pickup | 75% back |
| 24 to 48 hours before pickup | 50% back |
| Less than 24 hours before pickup | No refund |

A Non-refundable booking gets no refund. The deposit is taken at pickup, so none is held when you cancel before it.

## Messages, tolls and tickets

- On a rental of 2 days or more we check in after the first day: "How is the car?" If anything is off, reply to the email or text, or call us.
- Write to us about a booking at the bottom of its page: type in Your message and press Send.
- Tolls and tickets are yours to pay, including Highway 407 ETR. If one reaches us, we pay it and charge the amount plus our fee to your Card on File, and email you a copy of the notice.
- Running late? Extend in your booking, even after the return time while you still have the car, or call us at 289-312-5991. The late fee is 17.5% of the daily rate for each started hour (at least $25) after a 30 minute grace.
- Before your return we remind you: the day before, about 3 hours before (with an Extend link) and at the return time. If the car is late we send a notice at 15 minutes and a final notice at 2 hours. No late notices between 10 pm and 7 am.
- Already brought the car back but still getting late notices? Tap **I''ve returned the car** in the notice, or press it on your booking. Add photos of the car where you left it (pick several at once from your camera roll), the odometer, the fuel level and the time you returned it: all optional. The late notices stop at once while we check. When we confirm, your trip is complete. If we cannot find the car, we tell you why and the notices start again.
- Something wrong with the car? While you have it, press **Report a problem** on your booking: it calls roadside help, or opens a message to us.
- Someone else will drive too? Press **Add a driver**: write their name in the message and we add them; they sign with their own link.

## Return the car yourself (release 28)

**Return the car yourself** on your booking: photos of the car where you left it, the odometer, the fuel and the time. With all of them your trip is completed at once and any late notices stop; we may still adjust the readings after we see the car.

## Report an accident

While you have the car, the **Accident card** on your booking has **Report an accident**. Anyone hurt? Call 911 first.

1. Say what happened, when (empty means now) and where: type it or press **Use my location**.
2. Add photos and videos from your camera roll: all the cars, the plates, the damage and the scene.
3. Add the other party''s name, phone, plate and their insurer, and the police report number if there is one.
4. Answer **Is anyone hurt?** and **Can the car be driven?**, then press **Send the report**.

Your answers stay on your phone as you type until you send them. Once sent, our team has it at once and calls you; the page shows the next steps, **Call us**, and lets you add more photos or videos.

## Extend at the same rate (release 35)

An extension costs the same a day as your booking, and per-trip fees such as the Protection Plan are charged for the added days at the same rate. Delivery is never charged again. The price shows before you ask.

## Secondary contact and rideshare documents

Open **More** on your booking page:

- **Secondary contact**: someone we may call if we cannot reach you, for this trip or on your profile. Optional.
- **Rideshare or delivery documents**: rideshare and delivery driving are welcome. Driving for Uber, Lyft, DoorDash, Uber Eats, Instacart or another platform? Pick the platforms and print the documents they ask for: your rental agreement, a coverage letter and a vehicle letter.

## Rideshare, a second contact and a mid-trip check (release 35)

- Driving for Uber, Lyft, DoorDash, Uber Eats, Instacart or another platform is allowed: your booking page makes the documents they ask for.
- Add a secondary contact we can call if we cannot reach you, on your profile or for one trip.
- Halfway through a longer trip we send one short message asking how it is going. Reply with any problem and our team picks it up.
- We send no automatic text at night; an answer asked for then arrives in the morning. Common questions are answered at once, and a person answers anything else.

## Deposit still owed (release 48)
If you picked up the car before the deposit hold was placed, your booking page says **Deposit still owed** with the amount. It is a hold on your credit card, not a charge, released after the rental. We try your saved card each morning; if that does not work we send you a secure link by text or email. Tap it to place the hold, or call us.

## Notices from the car''s Tracker (release 48)

Every car has a Tracker, as your rental agreement says (section 12). If it records something, we tell you at once by email, text or the app: what happened, any charge, and the clause of your agreement.

- **Speeding over 180, 220 or 300 km/h**: a speeding charge applies each time ($500, $1,000 and $2,500 plus HST). It is taken from your deposit first.
- **A speed well over the limit, or hard braking**: a friendly heads-up. No charge.
- **The car outside Ontario, past its return time, or its Tracker unplugged**: please call us.
- **The car at an impound lot**: call us at once so we can get it released. The towing and storage costs are yours.

1. Open the notice, or your booking page.
2. Call us if something is wrong or you have a question. We would rather sort it out with you.

> Note: You can turn the heads-up messages off under **Notifications**. Notices about a charge are always sent.
',
