  'Vehicles is the fleet. Listings turns a car into a page on carmacars.ca in four steps: photos, covered plates, a review, and live on the site.

## Vehicles

**Cars** > **Vehicles**

1. Filter by status; More filters has who supplies the car, retired cars and the mode. Each row shows the plate, class, owner, mode, status, listing and daily rate.
2. Search by plate, model or owner. **Cars** > **Rates for many cars** changes the rates of many cars at once.
3. Open a car for its tabs: Overview, Rates, Fees and coverage, Calendar, Listing, and Owner, documents, tracker. The Tracker card links to Fleet tracking.

![](/guides/img/admin-08-vehicles-desktop-46461f49.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 900; address: carmacars.ca/admin/vehicles; pins: 1 74.3 31.1, 2 37.5 24.3, 3 48.6 52.4")

## Set a car''s rates and kilometres

Open the car, then the **Rates** tab. Everything on it saves together, in one step.

1. Type the four rates. Only the daily rate is needed: an empty weekend rate is the daily rate, an empty weekly rate is 6 days at the daily rate, and an empty monthly rate is 22 days.
2. Kilometres: keep **Use the defaults** (the kilometres a day in Settings, Kilometre choices, and the extra kilometre rate in Fee defaults for the car''s class), or choose **Custom for this car** and type them.
3. Check the deposit (the class default is filled in), and the delivery and pickup fees: each is one way, an empty pickup fee is the delivery fee, and 0 means not offered.
4. Read What renters pay under the fields: real prices for a weekend, a few weekdays, a week and a month, worked out the way bookings are priced. Press **Save the rates**.

| Rate | What it means |
| --- | --- |
| Daily rate | A price per day, for each day that starts on a Sunday, Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday or Thursday |
| Weekend rate | A price per day, not for the whole weekend: each day that starts on a Friday or Saturday. Friday 10 am to Sunday 10 am is 2 days at this rate; Sunday to Monday is a daily day |
| Weekly rate | The price for 7 days. Rentals of 7 to 29 days cost this for each 7 days, counted by the day. A 1 to 6 day rental never costs more |
| Monthly rate | The price for 30 days. A 7 to 29 day rental never costs more |

5. Lead-time pricing for this car, below the rates: **Program settings** (the tiers there), **Off for this car**, or **Its own tiers** (a table like the one in Program settings). Press **Save**.
6. **Price limits**, beside them: the lowest and highest daily rate the owner accepts. **This car** sets the car''s own; the owner''s line sets them for every car of that owner (a car''s own come first, field by field). Empty is no limit. Press **Save price limits**. Owners set the same limits in their portal.

> Good to know: Price limits hold the rental a day (after lead-time pricing, the non-refundable discount, a discount, a promo code or a price typed by hand; never fees, add-ons or tax) between the minimum and the maximum: one line, "Minimum daily rate for this car" or "Maximum daily rate for this car", brings it back. Never on an Owner Booking or a booking billed to an insurer. To price one request outside them, open its review screen, **More options**, tick **Allow a price outside the car''s price limits (Admin only)** and say why: it is kept on the booking and in the audit log. Untick it and the limits apply again.

> Tip: A problem shows on its own field, in words, as you type. When similar cars have rates, a line suggests them with Use these; it is only a hint. The same fields are on **Add a car**, so a car can be added with its rates in one pass.

## Fleet tracking

**Cars** > **Vehicles**, the **Fleet tracking** tab. Fleet staff have the same map as **Fleet map** in their menu; customer service, Sales and Finance open it from **Find a car** (**Car map**) and field staff under **Map**, read only: every staff member sees where the cars are, and only Admins and fleet staff mark alerts as seen. Every car on the same map as the Live map, with who has it. A car''s page and a booking''s page show **Where the car is** (or **No tracker yet**). Each owner sees the location and trips of their own cars in the owner portal, never the renter or the booking.

1. The four numbers: cars on rent, moving, parked, and open alerts.
2. The map shows each car as its photo in a ring: green moving (the arrow is its heading), yellow engine on, blue parked, orange not reporting. The list beside it has every car with its renter, booking, when it is due back (late in red) and its state.
3. Press a car on the map or in the list for its card: last report, odometer, fuel, tracker battery, whether the tracker has the car''s power, and the trip under way.
4. **Alerts**: speeding, left Ontario, left your zone, still driving after the return time, low tracker battery, unplugged and not reporting. Each also comes to the bell and, with phone alerts on, under Urgent alerts. Press **Show** to see where, **Seen** when it is handled, or **Mark all as seen**.
5. **Trips by booking**: each booking''s trips, kilometres and top speed (red at the speeding level). Press the last trip to draw its route on the map.

## Pair a tracker with a car

1. A new tracker that reports shows under **Trackers**, "Reporting, not on a car yet". Press **Pair**, choose the car and the install date.
2. Or press **Pair a tracker** and type its device ID (the IMEI or serial number on the tracker).
3. The install date starts the Tracker Fee on the owner''s invoice when the car has none yet. A replacement tracker keeps the car''s first date; the old tracker is taken off by itself.
4. **Remove** takes a tracker off a car (tick "faulty" for a broken one). The Tracker Fee is not changed.

## Tracking settings

Below the trackers: the speeding level (140 km/h), the minutes of grace after the return time (15), the low battery level (20%), the hours before "not reporting" (6), the Ontario alert, and one optional zone (a name, its centre and a radius in km). History keeps a moving car''s position once a minute for 90 days, trips and alerts for 365 days (at most 365: the privacy policy keeps tracker data 12 months).

1. Demo mode (off): simulated cars drive the GTA''s highways here and on the Live map, for a demonstration. Nothing is saved. Turn it off before the trackers go live.
2. **Make the ingest key**: the relay or tracker service signs every batch of positions with it. It is shown once; making a new one stops the old one at once.

> Tip: The Live map shows the same cars with its Fleet layer (tick Fleet).

## Tracker events, evidence and pound flags (release 48)

Below the map on **Cars > Fleet tracking**. It is off until the trackers are installed: an Admin turns on **Tracker events** under **Tracker event settings**.

On, each event makes one alert per car, kind and 30 minutes (never a flood), an evidence record, and a notice to the renter and to the car''s owner:

- **Speeding over 180, 220 or 300 km/h**: a record per limit, with the speeding charge of Settings > Program ($500, $1,000 and $2,500 plus HST by default). The renter is told what the Tracker recorded, the charge and the clause (rental agreement 10.5).
- **Over the speeding alert level** (140 km/h) and **harsh driving**: a friendly heads-up to the renter, no charge.
- **Left Ontario**, **driving after the return time**, **Tracker unplugged or tampered with**: a notice with the clause. No set charge.
- **Driving at night** (off unless you turn it on): staff and the owner only. The agreement sets no curfew.
- **At a pound**: see Pound flags below.

The **Tracker events** table shows each record: when, the car and booking, the speed and the map point, where it came from, how many readings it keeps, its seal (a SHA-256), the charge and the clause, and who was told.

1. To bill a speeding record, press **Charge** on its row (an Admin or Finance). The charge is added to the booking with the evidence record attached, and it is taken from the deposit first.
2. The record goes into the dispute pack by itself, with the notice the renter got.

**Pound flags**: a car whose tracker parks inside a pound lot''s radius for 20 minutes is flagged. Fleet gets an urgent To do and alert, Fleet and Admins an email, and the renter is told to call.

1. Call the lot (its phone and hours are on the flag), then the renter. Keep the receipts.
2. Press **Record the path**: the non-return charge ($1,000) or the theft recovery charge ($1,500) with the tow, impound and storage costs, **Recovered, nothing to charge**, or **Not a pound**. Write what happened.
3. A charge still waits for its other evidence (the final late notice, the receipt) like every fee.

**Pound lots**: the known Ontario lots, with name, address, phone and hours. It starts with the lots the Toronto and Peel police publish.

1. Press **Find the pins from the addresses** once; a lot with no pin cannot flag a car.
2. **Edit** a lot to add its hours, fix its details or type its pin, and tick **I checked these details with the lot**.
3. **Add a lot** for any other pound you know of.

> Note: The renter''s notice about a charge is always sent. The renter can mute the heads-up, and the owner can mute their alerts, in their own notification settings.

## The listing pipeline

Open **Cars** > **Listings**. A draft waiting for review shows Needs review.

1. Each row shows the car, plate, state, photos and the work done on it so far.
2. Press **Start a listing** to begin one for a car that has none.
3. Open a car to review it.

![](/guides/img/admin-09-listings-desktop-970819b6.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 560; address: carmacars.ca/admin/listings; pins: 1 53.5 37.0, 2 87.2 21.1, 3 32.6 37.0")

## Review a listing

1. Steps to go live shows four numbered steps: **1 Photos** (how many of the required photos are in, 14 for most cars, 13 for a two-seater with no rear seats), **2 Cover plates**, **3 Review** and **4 Live on the site**. Each says what it needs and has one button to where it is done; the step to do now is in red. A step that stopped (a photo edit or the copy) shows under them with **Retry**.
2. Similar cars on file lists possible duplicates. Press **Not a duplicate** or **Same car**. An open flag does not keep the car off the site; only Same car does.
3. The copy is written by itself from the car''s facts and published when it passes the checks: nothing to type. To change a line, press Change; that field is then locked and kept by every new version.
4. Under Photos, each public photo shows its plate state: Plate not checked, Plate covered or No plate visible.

![](/guides/img/admin-10-listing-review-desktop-352745fd.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 1100; address: carmacars.ca/admin/listings/704abf3d-8905-443d-a157-d52769cf7449; pins: 1 20.6 16.6, 2 86.1 47.5, 3 19.9 106.8, 4 74.9 106.8")

## Cover the licence plate

The plates are checked by themselves. Every photo is looked at by the vision model within the day''s free AI share: a plate it finds is blurred so no character can be read (the photo shows Covered automatically, with how sure it was), a photo with no plate is marked No plate visible (No plate seen automatically), and a photo it is not sure of stays Plate not checked for you. While photos wait, the Photos card says how many. A wrong decision: press **Undo** on the photo (the photo as it was comes back, Plate not checked), or **Not a plate: no plate visible** on a cover put where there is no plate.

To cover a plate yourself, press **Cover the plate** on the photo. The editor opens right under it.

1. Check the box over the plate, or press **Suggest the plate**.
2. Drag over a plate to draw a box. Drag a box to move it, or its corner to resize it.
3. The plate is blurred so no character can be read, only over the plate itself, with rounded corners and a soft edge. Nothing is drawn on a plate. A car with no front plate gets no box there. The studio photos Gemini makes have no plate at all: it is taken off cleanly, and a bumper without a plate is left as it is.
4. Press **Save the covered photo**. **Clear the boxes** starts over.
5. No plate in the shot? Press **No plate visible on this photo**.

![](/guides/img/admin-11-plate-editor-desktop-4219ad93.jpg "desktop; size: 690 703; address: carmacars.ca/admin/listings/704abf3d-8905-443d-a157-d52769cf7449; pins: 1 42.5 83.8, 2 49.6 29.9, 3 4.3 77.4, 4 15.5 83.8, 5 18.1 91.2")

> Tip: The covered photo replaces the public one; the original is kept privately. Keyboard: N adds a box, the arrows move it, Shift and the arrows resize it, Delete removes it.

## Publish

1. A real car that is not on the site is a line on To do: press **Set rates and publish**. The daily rate is filled in (the car''s own, or the suggested rate from similar cars or the class); change it if you like and press **Publish now**.
2. On the car itself, the Listing tab has **Publish now**; each open item of its checklist has a button to where it is done.
3. From a listing review: press **Approve and publish**, **Approve, publish later**, or **Send back** with what to fix.

> Watch out: The plate check never holds a car back: a real photo whose plate is not checked stays private (the other photos, or the sample photos, show instead) and goes public by itself once its plate is covered or marked not visible. Listings already live show "Plate not checked" on such photos.

## Photos filed under the wrong shot, and interior windows

1. On the Photos card, each shot lists its photos. A photo filed under the wrong shot: press **Remove** under it, then **Remove it**. The shot is free again: take or pick the right photo. The removed photo is kept privately and the removal is in the history. A live listing''s photos change in the review instead (Reject).
2. Dashboard and seat photos: what shows through the windows is replaced by the studio background when the cut is clean (a quality check: some but not most of the frame seen through, high in the frame, a few clean regions, sharp edges). Otherwise the windows are blurred, and the photo is marked windows blurred. Nothing to do.
3. A car with 2 seats or fewer needs no Rear seats photo.

## A listing without photos yet: sample photos

A car can be listed before its photos are taken. Until then the site shows a sample photo.

1. Submit the listing without photos. The listing copy is still written for you from the car''s details.
2. The car page and the car''s card show a sample photo, captioned "Sample photo", so renters know it is not this car. Staff see "Using sample photos" on the car and in Listings.
3. Publishing does not wait for a plate check: a sample photo has no plate.
4. Add the real photos when they are taken. Once real photos are approved they replace the sample at once; nothing else to do.

## Sample photos

**Settings** > **Sample photos**. The pictures a car shows until its real photos are in.

1. Every body type has a built-in picture (sedan, SUV, truck, van, coupe, hatchback, electric car).
2. Add your own: choose the Body type, and a Make and Model if the photo is of that exact model, pick the Photo, and press **Add the photo**.
3. The most specific photo wins: make and model, then make and body type, then body type. **Turn off** or **Delete** a photo you no longer want.
4. Cars using sample photos lists the cars still waiting for real photos. Each real car showing sample photos is also a line on To do, with **Add photos**.

![](/guides/img/admin-36-sample-photos-desktop-55c64070.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 812; address: carmacars.ca/admin/settings/sample-photos; pins: 4 26.8 28.9")

## Publish now, and new cars published by themselves

Nothing between a new car and the site has to be finished first: the car goes on the site, and what is still open shows on its checklist.

1. **Settings** > **Program**, **Publish new cars automatically** (on by default): a new real car goes on the site by itself as soon as it has its year, make and model and its rates, when it is added with rates, when its rates are saved, when it is added for an owner, or when an owner''s application is approved.
2. Otherwise open the car: its Listing tab says why it is not on the site and has **Publish now**. A car with no rates yet is published with the suggested rates (similar cars, else the class defaults in Program settings); change them later on the Rates tab.
3. Every real car has its listing from the moment it is added, as a draft. It shows in Listings and in Not on the site yet until it is published.
4. An owner''s own application waits for your decision before its car is published by itself; Publish now still works.
5. A car taken off the site by staff, or scheduled for a later date, is never published by itself: press **Publish now**.

## The checklist: what is still open on a listed car

Open items never stop publishing. They show as warnings on the car''s Listing tab and after Publish now.

| Item | What it means |
| --- | --- |
| Paperwork | Ownership permit, registry forms, agreements signed, Forms C and D, upfront payment, registry visit, tracker, safety certificate |
| Insurance | Not on the fleet insurance policy yet: the car can be booked, but not handed over |
| Details | Colour, body, seats, gearbox: the car page leaves out what is missing |
| Photos | No real photos: sample photos stand in. A photo whose plate is not checked stays private until it is |
| No VIN yet | A car added by its plate alone: add the VIN when you have it |
| Possible duplicate | An open flag in Similar cars. Only Same car keeps the car off the site |
| Owner terms | The management fee (Revenue Share) and fees not set: a request uses the owner''s terms or the standard grid |

## The fleet policy rule at handover

A program owner''s car is listed and can be requested, offered and paid for while its paperwork is open. It is never handed over until the insurer confirms in writing that it is on the fleet insurance policy.

- Staff see a warning on a request and an offer for a car not on the policy yet.
- The handover refuses the car until the insurer''s confirmation is recorded (Owners and onboarding). The field app says so on the job.
- Only real states keep a car off the site: retired, left the program, out of service, Turo only, bookings turned off, a self-managed owner in arrears, or a paused listing.

## Cars on sample photos

**Cars**, **Listings** ends with **Cars on sample photos**: each real car whose page still shows sample photos, with its newest handover photos (the check-in and check-out photos field staff take).

1. Where a handover photographed the car, press **Use the handover photos**. They go into the car''s listing as if taken on the capture screen.
2. When every required shot is there, the listing is submitted: Gemini makes each photo from the original, then the listing waits for your review like any other.
3. A car with no handover photos yet gets them at its next handover, or press **Start a listing** and take them.

> Good to know: The listing photos use no Cloudflare image processing: Gemini makes every photo and the site makes the sizes.

## A car''s registration and documents

Open the car, then **Owner & documents**. The **Registration** card:

1. Correct the **VIN** (it is checked: 17 characters, the check digit, not on another car; decoded again for the body style and trim), the **Year** and the **Body style**.
2. Type the **Ontario permit number** and the date the **Plate sticker expires**. Fleet gets a task 30 days and 7 days before; save the new date after the renewal and the task closes.
3. Under **Documents**, choose the kind (**Ownership permit**, Safety Standards Certificate, owner''s insurance, other), pick the photo or PDF and press **Upload**. The ownership permit clears that item of the owner''s checklist.
4. For the **Safety Standards Certificate**, also type its number, the date it was issued and the date it expires. Fleet gets a task 30 days and 7 days before it expires; upload the new certificate with its dates and the task closes. It is a document on the car, not a service record, and nothing is billed to the owner.
5. **Add a car** takes the ownership permit and the Safety Standards Certificate too, under **Documents (optional)**.

## A car added under the wrong owner

Open the car, Overview, **Who supplies the car**, **Move to another owner**. Choose the owner, or **CarmaCars (owner not known yet)**: the car becomes a company car, with no owner schedule or terms.

- The car''s unsigned owner application and vehicle schedule are withdrawn (kept in the history), and its draft owner invoices are deleted. Nobody is notified.
- It is refused once anything for the car is signed, issued, paid or on a statement.

### The VIN from the car, not typed

Every VIN field (Add a car, Add a car for an owner, the car''s **Registration**, **Start a listing**) has **Scan the barcode** and **Photo of the VIN**. Scan the barcode in the driver''s door frame or at the bottom of the windshield: the phone''s camera reads it by itself. Or take a photo of the VIN plate or sticker: the barcode in it is read first, else the photo is read for the printed VIN. The VIN is checked (17 characters, the check digit; I, O and Q become 1 and 0) and decoded as when you type it. Check it against the car before saving.

### Photos in any order

**Add photos** on the listing takes any number of photos at once from the camera roll. Each is sorted to its shot by itself (front three-quarter, sides, rear, dashboard, seats and the rest); a shot that already has its photo sends the new one to the extra photos, so nothing is replaced by accident. The shots are a guide, not a rule: a listing is complete with 10 photos that can go on the site and one outside photo for the cover. Outside photos get the studio background: the car is cropped to its edges and placed big in the frame with its wheels on the floor and a soft shadow under the tyres, and any corner watermark or caption beside the car is left out. Inside and detail photos are kept as taken; when one has a watermark, a logo or caption text on it, the edge with the mark is cut off by itself, and a photo whose mark cannot be cut off (one in the middle) stays off the site until you replace it. **Cover the plate** opens on every outside photo with the plate box suggested; check it and save.

Outside photos made before the newest framing (the car small in the frame, or without the model''s name behind it) are made again with **Frame the outside photos again** above the photos of the listing, then **Yes, frame again**. The cover and the main outside views get the model''s name lettered behind the car, as on the sample photos (for example CLA, C CLASS, AMG GT). The photos leave the site until their plates are checked again: the plate box is suggested on the new photos; check each and cover it. On a published listing each goes back on the site once its plate is checked.

## Showroom photos

Outside photos go in the CarmaCars showroom by themselves. When a real photographed room is stored (dealership or studio photos licensed for commercial use, fetched once from Wikimedia Commons with their author and licence kept), the car stands in it: about 70% of the width, its wheels on the room''s floor, a soft shadow and a faint reflection under it, its light matched to the room, and no sign or lettering on the real wall. Program settings > Listings has the switch (Photographed showroom rooms, on), the car''s width and the cut-out quality floor: a cut-out that is not clean enough (pieces, a blurry or ragged edge) is never placed in a room, the real photo is used instead (its plate covered as usual) and the photo says so. Without a stored room it is the drawn dark showroom: a simple dark dealership with linear lights in the ceiling, a slatted wood wall between two light strips with a big lit CarmaCars sign, and a polished dark floor with the car''s reflection and a shadow under each tyre. Every angle of a car is in the same room, and the cover has the model''s name in metal letters on the wall under the sign. The image model may relight the car or turn it slightly; a photo that shows another car, model or colour is not used. **Settings** > **Program settings** > **Listings** has the switch (Showroom photos, on), the image model that makes the photos look photographed, and its daily limit. Past the limit, or when the image model is not available, the site makes the showroom itself for free, and the photo says why under it.

- A car whose photos were made on the black studio: press **Apply showroom to this car** above its photos, then **Yes, apply**.
- Every car at once: **Listings** > **Showroom photos** > **Apply showroom to every car**, then **Yes, every car**.
- Under a photo in the showroom: **Redo** makes it again, **Back to the original** puts back the version before the showroom.

A car that stays where it was keeps its plate check. When the image model made the photo, check the plate again: the photo is off the site until you do. Photos made in the first showroom are made again in the new one with **Apply showroom to this car** or **Apply showroom to every car**.

## Failed photos

The site makes the photo sizes itself: the image service is asked only to cut the car out (**Settings** > **Program settings** > **Listings**: the switch to let the image service make every photo step is off). When the image service is busy or over its allowance, the photo still goes on the site from the original and is made again later. A listing marked Failed has **Retry failed photos** in its note; **Retry failed photos** at the top does every listing. They are made again a few at a time, and the listing leaves Failed when they are done.

## The primary photo is always the front exterior (release 43)

The first photo of every car on the site, in the cards, the feeds and the Marketplace kit is its exterior at the standard angle (front three-quarter, in the dark showroom). An inside photo is never ahead of an outside one, and the cover mark follows by itself whenever photos are added, made again or reordered.

- **Primary photo is not exterior** is a flag and a filter in **Cars** > **Vehicles**: it marks a car whose first photo is an inside one because its best outside photo is not on the site yet, or it has none. Add or approve an outside photo and the flag clears by itself.
- **Redo photos with Gemini** on the car page makes every photo of the car again from its original with Gemini, and generates its missing angles. A photo Gemini cannot make well stays off the site, flagged. It needs the image model switched on in Program settings, Listings.
- The same press checks the car''s **Other detail** photos again: an outside view filed there is moved to the outside photos (the front three-quarter becomes the first photo) and made in the showroom. This is what clears the flag on a car that showed nothing to redo.
- Every outside photo has the same room behind it: Gemini replaces the whole background from the original photo.
- Every plate is blurred; nothing is drawn on it and there is no text anywhere else. Inside photos stay sharp from front to back.
- **Redo every car with Gemini** (Listings, Showroom photos; Admin and Fleet) is the same as **Redo every car** on the Photo standard card.

## The photo standard: every photo made by Gemini (release 45)

Every listing photo is made by Gemini from the original photo, never from a cut-out. Outside photos get their whole background replaced by the CarmaCars showroom, with nothing of the place they were taken in left. Inside photos are cleaned up (no clutter) and sharp from front to back. Every plate is blurred so no character can be read; no plate is drawn and there is no text anywhere else on the photo.

- **The check.** A second Gemini look compares each new photo with the original and refuses it when the old background shows, the car is warped, another colour or model, has parts added or missing, a plate can be read, or there is text anywhere. The site also checks the edges are the dark showroom. A refused photo is made again, twice; then it stays off the site and is counted as flagged.
- **Missing angles.** Every car shows the standard set: front three-quarter, front, side profile, rear three-quarter, rear, dashboard, front seats, rear seats and trunk. An angle the car has no photo of is generated by Gemini from the car''s own photos, in the same showroom, and marked **AI generated** on the listing (staff only). A real photo of that angle replaces it by itself.
- **The order.** The front three-quarter is always first, then the other outside photos, then the inside ones. A car whose first photo would be an inside one shows no photos and cannot be published until it has an outside one; its front three-quarter is generated first.
- **By itself.** Every 5 minutes the job brings the next cars to the standard, newest listed cars first, until every car is done (about a day for the whole fleet). A photo already at the standard is never made again unless you ask. **Program settings** > **Listings**: the daily Gemini limit (2000 calls), the calls kept for new uploads (50) and the switch.
- **Listings** > **Photo standard** (Admin and Fleet) shows each car: photos at the standard out of all, AI angles, flagged photos and the last run. **Redo this car now** makes all of its photos again at once; **Redo every car** makes every photo of every car again. **Redo photos with Gemini** on a car page does the same as Redo this car now.

## The first photo: plain, with a model, or a flyer

On a listing, under **First photo**, choose what shows first on the site and in the Marketplace kit. Switch any time; the other photos stay as they are.

- **Plain car**: the cover photo as it is (the default).
- **With a model**: a car-show photo made by the image model, with a fully clothed adult model beside the car. It needs the image model; until it is made (or when the image model is not there) the plain cover shows, and the listing says why.
- **Flyer**: the cover photo with a band like a printed flyer: the car, the price a day from its live rates, the call to action, a badge and the logo. When the price, the words or the cover photo change, it is made again by itself within 10 minutes; the plain cover shows meanwhile.

**Make it again** makes the chosen one again. The words of the flyer and the description of the model are in **Settings** > **Program settings** > **Listings** (First photo "flyer" and First photo "with a model"); {car}, {price}, {weekly} and {monthly} are filled for each car.

## Marketing photos in other scenes

For Marketplace and social posts, a car''s outside photos can be made again in other scenes. The website keeps its own photos in the dark showroom: a marketing set never replaces them.

1. On a listing, under **Marketing photos**, choose a scene, or **Mix: a different scene on each photo**, and press **Make the marketing set**.
2. The copies show as they are made. The dark showroom and the plain white studio are made by the site when the image model is not there; the photographic scenes (a bright showroom, a city street at night, the Toronto waterfront, a parking garage, Highway, a scenic road, Brick building) need the image model, and say so on the copy when it is not there.
3. **Download (ZIP)** takes the set; the Marketplace kit''s **With scenes (ZIP)** takes the same set.

**Settings** > **Program settings** > **Marketing scenes** lists the scenes. A scene made in a real place has a photo of that place: Brick building picks its photo by itself: the widest outside photo, as taken, of the shareholders'' own cars. To use another, press **Change the reference photo** and pick one (the shareholders'' cars'' photos come first), or upload one. The scenes'' names and words are in the **Marketing scenes** setting.

## Extra photos

A photo that fits no shot is an extra photo. Under the shots, **Extra outside photos** (put on the studio background) and **Extra inside and detail photos** (touched up) each take any number at once. They count toward the 10 photos, get the same plate check, and come after the standard shots on the car''s page.

1. In the review, **Extra photos, in their order on the car page** lists them.
2. Drag a photo by its handle (⋮⋮), or press **Earlier** or **Later**.
3. Press **Save the order**.

## Fix a cut-out

When the background removal cuts badly (a mirror or a wheel missing, background left beside the car), press **Edit the cut-out** under the outside photo.

1. **Cut-out** shows the car over the photo as taken, shown faintly. Choose **Erase** and brush over what should go, or **Restore** and brush over what the cut-out took off. Set **Brush size** and **Zoom**; when zoomed, **Move the view** pans. **Undo** takes back the last stroke.
2. **On the studio** shows the car on the studio background. Drag the car to move it and use **Size** to make it larger or smaller. **Centre and full size** puts it back.
3. Press **Save as a new version**. The photo is made again in about a minute; the version before and the photo as taken are kept. **Reset to the automatic cut-out** starts again from the automatic one.

> Good to know: If the car did not move, the plate check carries over: a photo marked no plate visible stays so, and a covered plate is covered again on the new photo when the review is open. If the car moved, check the plate again. A photo made before cut-outs were kept shows **Make the cut-out** first; the editor opens by itself when it is ready.

Every photo also gets a light touch-up by itself (exposure, levels, a little contrast and colour, mild sharpening), never enough to change the paint colour or hide a scratch. Turn it off for one photo with **Use original colours** under it (the photo is made again; approve it again), or for every photo in Admin > Settings > **Program settings** (Listings) with **Auto-enhance listing photos**. The photo as uploaded is always kept.
## Import photos from a Google Drive link

The owner often hands over a car''s photos as a public Google Drive folder, or one big folder with a folder per make and then per car. You do not download them: paste the link.

**One car.** On the car''s listing, under the capture, **Import photos from a Google Drive link**. Paste the folder link (shared with Anyone with the link) and press **Import the photos**. Every photo in the folder, and in the folders inside it, is added to this car as if you had pressed Add photos: each is sorted to its shot (else filed as an extra photo, in file-name order), put on the studio background and checked for its plate. The box under the link, **Submit the listing for processing when its photos are in**, is on by default.

**Many cars.** **Cars** > **Import photos from Drive** (a button on Vehicles). Paste the top folder''s link and press **Read the folder**. The page walks every folder and proposes a car for each folder that holds photos, from the year, make, model, colour and plate in the folder names (the make folder above counts; 01 Motors partner cars come first). Check the table: tick or untick **Import**, change the car in the list (the likely cars come first), leave out a folder with **Do not import this folder**. A line marked **Check this one** matched two alike cars. Then press **Import N photos from M folders**.

1. The page follows the import by itself. You can leave it and come back: it runs in the background.
2. The end shows the summary: imported, skipped and failed, and why for each (a file over 15 MB, a file that is not a photo, the same photo already on the car, a folder not shared).
3. **Try the failed photos again** takes only the ones that failed. Pressing Import on the same link again never adds a photo twice: a Drive file already on the car is skipped, and so is the same picture under another name. A photo you took off the car can be imported again.

> Good to know: JPG, PNG, HEIC and WebP only (HEIC and WebP are made JPEG first). At most 15 MB a photo, 600 photos, 400 folders and 4 GB in one import. Drive is asked politely, one photo at a time; a big import takes a while.

> Good to know: Without a key, Drive shows only the first 50 files of a folder on its public page; a folder with more is read in full when Drive allows it. In **Settings**, the **Photo import from Google Drive** box takes a Google API key with the Drive API on (after it is saved only its last 4 characters are shown, and it is never written to the change log): with it, folders of any size are read and photos download without Drive''s warning pages.

## Test bookings and deleting a car

1. On a booking made only to try the site, press **Mark as a test booking** (Admins only; the reason is optional). **Make it a real booking again** undoes it.
2. A car whose bookings are all test bookings can be deleted: the test bookings and their test payments go with it, and a copy is kept in the archive of deleted requests.
3. A car with a real booking cannot be deleted.

## Pickup from owner and return to owner (release 28)

On a car''s page, **Pickup from owner and return to owner** records the car''s condition when CarmaCars picks it up from its owner or gives it back: the date and time, km, fuel, many photos at once with the suggested angles, and notes. **Add photos** adds more to a record later. The owner sees these records read only on the car''s page in their portal. They are the baseline condition for any dispute.

## Incident cards (release 34)
**Cars** > **Vehicles** > **Incident cards** prints the card for each car: what to do in an accident or a breakdown, the support number from Settings, a roadside number when there is one, a QR code to report it in the app, and the fleet insurance slip. Open a car and press **Incident card** to print only that car; on the list, **Print all cars** prints them all, two cards to a Letter page with crop marks, ready to laminate. Under Fleet insurance policy press **Add the policy** (the insurer, the policy number, the dates, the named insured, the roadside number on the slip) and choose the uploaded slip if you have one: it is printed as it is, otherwise the fields are. The card never shows a premium. Fleet staff print the same cards from their portal.

## Field jobs, shifts and who gets a job

**Cars**, then **Field jobs**, is the board Fleet uses, with every action Fleet has. Shifts are published by themselves from the shift template in Program settings (one shift of 10:00 to 17:00 every second day by default, 14 days ahead, only forward from the latest shift), with a shift of its own for any handover or return no shift covers; **Publish shifts** adds more by hand, and a shift you cancel is not published again. Field staff take them. **Missing check-in and check-out**, on the same page, lists every past rental without its photos and readings, with **Give to field staff**. Jobs go on shifts, not on people: each job is put on the shift covering its time (or that day''s), whoever holds the shift does it (several people share the jobs, least busy first), a shift nobody holds keeps its jobs for whoever claims it, and work lands only on days with shifts (work due on a day without shifts moves to the day before, or to the next day with shifts when it comes in on the day; the booking''s own times never change). A booking whose handover or return falls on a day with no shifts shows a warning on the board and on the booking. **To a shift** moves a job to another shift. You can give a job to a field person on a shift that day or to an Admin, take it off with **Unassign** (tick **Tell them** to let them know), and an Admin who holds a job opens it on the field portal. A person who has not passed the academy cannot be given a job or take a shift. A shift with jobs and nobody on it within 24 hours alerts Fleet and the Admins once.

## Every view generated from the car''s photos (release 47)

Every car shows nine generated views: front three-quarter (always first), front, side profile, rear three-quarter, rear, dashboard, front seats, rear seats and trunk. Gemini makes each one from references, so the car is the real car and the room looks like a real showroom.

- **What Gemini is sent.** The car''s own photos (its exact colour, trim and wheels); when it has fewer than three, or none of that side, its newest check-in and check-out photos as well (only as references: they are never shown on the site). Then the sample view of that angle (for the camera position only), the stock photo of the model, and for an outside view the showroom background plate. The words describe each angle: camera height, lens, crop, the car centred, 45 degrees for a three-quarter. Plates blurred, no text, no logos added.
- **The check.** A second Gemini look compares the result with the real photos (same car, colour, wheels and trim, nothing warped, not a render) and with the angle. A refused view is made again, twice, told what was wrong; still refused, it is flagged and the car''s real photo of that angle stays on the site.
- **The real photos.** They stay in the car''s record and on the Admin car page, marked as they were; the site shows the generated view of an angle in place of the real one only once it has passed. Generated views are marked **AI generated** for staff only.
- **By itself.** Every 5 minutes the job takes the front three-quarter of every car first (newest listed first), then the other angles, within the daily Gemini limit (about a day for the whole fleet). **Program settings** > **Listings**: the switch for the generated views.
- **Listings** > **Photo standard** shows each car''s **Generated set** (views made out of nine, being made, flagged, and "from check-in photos" when those were used). **Redo this car now** and **Redo every car** make the generated views again too; the views on the site stay until the new ones pass.
- **Showroom background plates** (**Program settings**, Admin): the room for front, side and rear views. Gemini made them once and a second look confirmed each looks like a real photo. Upload a real photo of a showroom (empty floor in the middle, no people, cars, signs or logos) to replace one or all three; **Make a new one** has Gemini make it again.

## The studio set: every car photographed the same way (release 48)

Every car gets the same nine views, as if all were photographed in one studio on one day: the same angle, camera height, lens and framing for each view, the car facing the same way as the sample covers (the front three-quarter and the side with the nose to the left), plates taken off cleanly, the car itself unchanged.

- The scene: every car stands in the same scene so the covers line up as you scroll: the dark dealership with the CarmaCars sign on the wall by default, with the model''s name on the wall behind the car on the first photo. **Program settings** > **Listings**: the scene for every car. On a car, **Studio photos** > **Scene** picks another for that car only (highway, brick building and the other marketing scenes).
- No photo of an angle? Gemini makes it from the car''s other photos. A car with no photo at all gets its outside views from the stock photo of its model, in its own colour.
- One set everywhere: once a car''s front three-quarter is made, the site shows only its made views, in the standard order, the front three-quarter first: the same photo on the home page, the search cards, the car page, the partner feeds and in the sitemap. The real photos stay in the car''s record.
- The check: Gemini checks each view against the car''s own photos: the same car (model, colour, wheels), the right angle, the nose the right way, the old background gone (the site also measures it), no readable plate. Smaller doubts (framing, a part the photos do not show) stop only the first two tries.
- On a car, **Studio photos** shows each view beside the car''s own photos of that angle, marked **AI**. **Make again** makes one view again; **Take off the site** and **Put on the site**.
- **Listings** > **Photo standard** shows the fleet''s progress: views made out of all, cars with their studio cover, and about how many days are left at Gemini''s daily limit.
- Marketing set: **Make the marketing set** uses the studio views (the same angle and cover as the site) in the scene you choose, plus up to three lifestyle shots: an adult model with the car, styled like a luxury car advert, always fully dressed and tasteful. Each is marked **AI**; tick **In the ZIP** for the photos you want in a post. A lifestyle shot Gemini declines is skipped.
- Background plates (**Program settings**, Admin): one set per scene. Choose the scene, then upload a real photo of the place to replace one or all three.

## Studio renders first (release 48)

- Every car gets the full studio set made from its own photos: same colour, wheels and trim, the same framing for every car.
- On the site the renders come first, in this order: side profile (the nose to the left, the cover), front three-quarter, front, rear three-quarter, rear, dashboard, front seats, rear seats, trunk. The car''s own photos follow, on the same branded background. They are never hidden.
- A render goes live as soon as it passes the photo check. There is no approval step. To change one, open the car, **Studio photos**, then **Make again** or **Take off the site**. Taking the side profile off makes the next render the cover.
- The car page says **Rendered photos** above the gallery, with **See its real photos**.
- New cars get their renders by themselves. To do every published car now: **Listings**, **Photo standard**, **Render every published car**. The line beside it shows how many cars are done. It works within the image model''s daily limit.
- When a car''s set is live, the owner gets an email and an alert ("Your car has new studio photos"), and Fleet gets "Studio photos live" in the next digest. Look the photos over.
- The Cars filter lists one model per family (for example CLA-Class or 3 Series). The trim shows on the car. A car whose model family is not recognised is listed in **Data health**: fix the typo, or ask for the family to be added.',
  '<p class="gd-p">Vehicles is the fleet. Listings turns a car into a page on carmacars.ca in four steps: photos, covered plates, a review, and live on the site.</p><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-vehicles" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Vehicles</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Vehicles</b></p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Filter by status; More filters has who supplies the car, retired cars and the mode. Each row shows the plate, class, owner, mode, status, listing and daily rate.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Search by plate, model or owner. <b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Rates for many cars</b> changes the rates of many cars at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Open a car for its tabs: Overview, Rates, Fees and coverage, Calendar, Listing, and Owner, documents, tracker. The Tracker card links to Fleet tracking.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/vehicles</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/900"><img src="/guides/img/admin-08-vehicles-desktop-46461f49.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="900"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:74.3%;top:31.1%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:37.5%;top:24.3%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:48.6%;top:52.4%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-set-a-car-s-rates-and-kilometres" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Set a car&#39;s rates and kilometres</h2><p class="gd-p">Open the car, then the <b class="gd-ui">Rates</b> tab. Everything on it saves together, in one step.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Type the four rates. Only the daily rate is needed: an empty weekend rate is the daily rate, an empty weekly rate is 6 days at the daily rate, and an empty monthly rate is 22 days.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Kilometres: keep <b class="gd-ui">Use the defaults</b> (the kilometres a day in Settings, Kilometre choices, and the extra kilometre rate in Fee defaults for the car&#39;s class), or choose <b class="gd-ui">Custom for this car</b> and type them.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Check the deposit (the class default is filled in), and the delivery and pickup fees: each is one way, an empty pickup fee is the delivery fee, and 0 means not offered.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Read What renters pay under the fields: real prices for a weekend, a few weekdays, a week and a month, worked out the way bookings are priced. Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the rates</b>.</div></li></ol></div><div class="gd-tablewrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Table"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Rate</th><th scope="col">What it means</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Daily rate</td><td>A price per day, for each day that starts on a Sunday, Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday or Thursday</td></tr><tr><td>Weekend rate</td><td>A price per day, not for the whole weekend: each day that starts on a Friday or Saturday. Friday 10 am to Sunday 10 am is 2 days at this rate; Sunday to Monday is a daily day</td></tr><tr><td>Weekly rate</td><td>The price for 7 days. Rentals of 7 to 29 days cost this for each 7 days, counted by the day. A 1 to 6 day rental never costs more</td></tr><tr><td>Monthly rate</td><td>The price for 30 days. A 7 to 29 day rental never costs more</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol" start="5"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Lead-time pricing for this car, below the rates: <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> (the tiers there), <b class="gd-ui">Off for this car</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Its own tiers</b> (a table like the one in Program settings). Press <b class="gd-ui">Save</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Price limits</b>, beside them: the lowest and highest daily rate the owner accepts. <b class="gd-ui">This car</b> sets the car&#39;s own; the owner&#39;s line sets them for every car of that owner (a car&#39;s own come first, field by field). Empty is no limit. Press <b class="gd-ui">Save price limits</b>. Owners set the same limits in their portal.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Price limits hold the rental a day (after lead-time pricing, the non-refundable discount, a discount, a promo code or a price typed by hand; never fees, add-ons or tax) between the minimum and the maximum: one line, &quot;Minimum daily rate for this car&quot; or &quot;Maximum daily rate for this car&quot;, brings it back. Never on an Owner Booking or a booking billed to an insurer. To price one request outside them, open its review screen, <b class="gd-ui">More options</b>, tick <b class="gd-ui">Allow a price outside the car&#39;s price limits (Admin only)</b> and say why: it is kept on the booking and in the audit log. Untick it and the limits apply again.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>A problem shows on its own field, in words, as you type. When similar cars have rates, a line suggests them with Use these; it is only a hint. The same fields are on <b class="gd-ui">Add a car</b>, so a car can be added with its rates in one pass.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-fleet-tracking" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Fleet tracking</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Vehicles</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Fleet tracking</b> tab. Fleet staff have the same map as <b class="gd-ui">Fleet map</b> in their menu; customer service, Sales and Finance open it from <b class="gd-ui">Find a car</b> (<b class="gd-ui">Car map</b>) and field staff under <b class="gd-ui">Map</b>, read only: every staff member sees where the cars are, and only Admins and fleet staff mark alerts as seen. Every car on the same map as the Live map, with who has it. A car&#39;s page and a booking&#39;s page show <b class="gd-ui">Where the car is</b> (or <b class="gd-ui">No tracker yet</b>). Each owner sees the location and trips of their own cars in the owner portal, never the renter or the booking.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The four numbers: cars on rent, moving, parked, and open alerts.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The map shows each car as its photo in a ring: green moving (the arrow is its heading), yellow engine on, blue parked, orange not reporting. The list beside it has every car with its renter, booking, when it is due back (late in red) and its state.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press a car on the map or in the list for its card: last report, odometer, fuel, tracker battery, whether the tracker has the car&#39;s power, and the trip under way.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Alerts</b>: speeding, left Ontario, left your zone, still driving after the return time, low tracker battery, unplugged and not reporting. Each also comes to the bell and, with phone alerts on, under Urgent alerts. Press <b class="gd-ui">Show</b> to see where, <b class="gd-ui">Seen</b> when it is handled, or <b class="gd-ui">Mark all as seen</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Trips by booking</b>: each booking&#39;s trips, kilometres and top speed (red at the speeding level). Press the last trip to draw its route on the map.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-pair-a-tracker-with-a-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Pair a tracker with a car</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A new tracker that reports shows under <b class="gd-ui">Trackers</b>, &quot;Reporting, not on a car yet&quot;. Press <b class="gd-ui">Pair</b>, choose the car and the install date.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Or press <b class="gd-ui">Pair a tracker</b> and type its device ID (the IMEI or serial number on the tracker).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The install date starts the Tracker Fee on the owner&#39;s invoice when the car has none yet. A replacement tracker keeps the car&#39;s first date; the old tracker is taken off by itself.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> takes a tracker off a car (tick &quot;faulty&quot; for a broken one). The Tracker Fee is not changed.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-tracking-settings" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Tracking settings</h2><p class="gd-p">Below the trackers: the speeding level (140 km/h), the minutes of grace after the return time (15), the low battery level (20%), the hours before &quot;not reporting&quot; (6), the Ontario alert, and one optional zone (a name, its centre and a radius in km). History keeps a moving car&#39;s position once a minute for 90 days, trips and alerts for 365 days (at most 365: the privacy policy keeps tracker data 12 months).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Demo mode (off): simulated cars drive the GTA&#39;s highways here and on the Live map, for a demonstration. Nothing is saved. Turn it off before the trackers go live.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Make the ingest key</b>: the relay or tracker service signs every batch of positions with it. It is shown once; making a new one stops the old one at once.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>The Live map shows the same cars with its Fleet layer (tick Fleet).</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-tracker-events-evidence-and-pound-flags-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Tracker events, evidence and pound flags (release 48)</h2><p class="gd-p">Below the map on <b class="gd-ui">Cars &gt; Fleet tracking</b>. It is off until the trackers are installed: an Admin turns on <b class="gd-ui">Tracker events</b> under <b class="gd-ui">Tracker event settings</b>.</p><p class="gd-p">On, each event makes one alert per car, kind and 30 minutes (never a flood), an evidence record, and a notice to the renter and to the car&#39;s owner:</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">Speeding over 180, 220 or 300 km/h</b>: a record per limit, with the speeding charge of Settings &gt; Program ($500, $1,000 and $2,500 plus HST by default). The renter is told what the Tracker recorded, the charge and the clause (rental agreement 10.5).</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Over the speeding alert level</b> (140 km/h) and <b class="gd-ui">harsh driving</b>: a friendly heads-up to the renter, no charge.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Left Ontario</b>, <b class="gd-ui">driving after the return time</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Tracker unplugged or tampered with</b>: a notice with the clause. No set charge.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Driving at night</b> (off unless you turn it on): staff and the owner only. The agreement sets no curfew.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">At a pound</b>: see Pound flags below.</li></ul><p class="gd-p">The <b class="gd-ui">Tracker events</b> table shows each record: when, the car and booking, the speed and the map point, where it came from, how many readings it keeps, its seal (a SHA-256), the charge and the clause, and who was told.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">To bill a speeding record, press <b class="gd-ui">Charge</b> on its row (an Admin or Finance). The charge is added to the booking with the evidence record attached, and it is taken from the deposit first.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The record goes into the dispute pack by itself, with the notice the renter got.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Pound flags</b>: a car whose tracker parks inside a pound lot&#39;s radius for 20 minutes is flagged. Fleet gets an urgent To do and alert, Fleet and Admins an email, and the renter is told to call.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Call the lot (its phone and hours are on the flag), then the renter. Keep the receipts.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Record the path</b>: the non-return charge ($1,000) or the theft recovery charge ($1,500) with the tow, impound and storage costs, <b class="gd-ui">Recovered, nothing to charge</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Not a pound</b>. Write what happened.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A charge still waits for its other evidence (the final late notice, the receipt) like every fee.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Pound lots</b>: the known Ontario lots, with name, address, phone and hours. It starts with the lots the Toronto and Peel police publish.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Find the pins from the addresses</b> once; a lot with no pin cannot flag a car.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Edit</b> a lot to add its hours, fix its details or type its pin, and tick <b class="gd-ui">I checked these details with the lot</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Add a lot</b> for any other pound you know of.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Note</span><div>The renter&#39;s notice about a charge is always sent. The renter can mute the heads-up, and the owner can mute their alerts, in their own notification settings.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-the-listing-pipeline" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The listing pipeline</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b>. A draft waiting for review shows Needs review.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each row shows the car, plate, state, photos and the work done on it so far.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Start a listing</b> to begin one for a car that has none.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Open a car to review it.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/listings</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/560"><img src="/guides/img/admin-09-listings-desktop-970819b6.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="560"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:53.5%;top:37%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:87.2%;top:21.1%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:32.6%;top:37%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-review-a-listing" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Review a listing</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Steps to go live shows four numbered steps: <b class="gd-ui">1 Photos</b> (how many of the required photos are in, 14 for most cars, 13 for a two-seater with no rear seats), <b class="gd-ui">2 Cover plates</b>, <b class="gd-ui">3 Review</b> and <b class="gd-ui">4 Live on the site</b>. Each says what it needs and has one button to where it is done; the step to do now is in red. A step that stopped (a photo edit or the copy) shows under them with <b class="gd-ui">Retry</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Similar cars on file lists possible duplicates. Press <b class="gd-ui">Not a duplicate</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Same car</b>. An open flag does not keep the car off the site; only Same car does.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The copy is written by itself from the car&#39;s facts and published when it passes the checks: nothing to type. To change a line, press Change; that field is then locked and kept by every new version.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Under Photos, each public photo shows its plate state: Plate not checked, Plate covered or No plate visible.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/listings/704abf3d-8905-443d-a157-d52769cf7449</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/1100"><img src="/guides/img/admin-10-listing-review-desktop-352745fd.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="1100"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:20.6%;top:16.6%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:86.1%;top:47.5%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:19.9%;top:100%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:74.9%;top:100%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-cover-the-licence-plate" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Cover the licence plate</h2><p class="gd-p">The plates are checked by themselves. Every photo is looked at by the vision model within the day&#39;s free AI share: a plate it finds is blurred so no character can be read (the photo shows Covered automatically, with how sure it was), a photo with no plate is marked No plate visible (No plate seen automatically), and a photo it is not sure of stays Plate not checked for you. While photos wait, the Photos card says how many. A wrong decision: press <b class="gd-ui">Undo</b> on the photo (the photo as it was comes back, Plate not checked), or <b class="gd-ui">Not a plate: no plate visible</b> on a cover put where there is no plate.</p><p class="gd-p">To cover a plate yourself, press <b class="gd-ui">Cover the plate</b> on the photo. The editor opens right under it.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Check the box over the plate, or press <b class="gd-ui">Suggest the plate</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Drag over a plate to draw a box. Drag a box to move it, or its corner to resize it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The plate is blurred so no character can be read, only over the plate itself, with rounded corners and a soft edge. Nothing is drawn on a plate. A car with no front plate gets no box there. The studio photos Gemini makes have no plate at all: it is taken off cleanly, and a bumper without a plate is left as it is.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the covered photo</b>. <b class="gd-ui">Clear the boxes</b> starts over.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">No plate in the shot? Press <b class="gd-ui">No plate visible on this photo</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/listings/704abf3d-8905-443d-a157-d52769cf7449</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:690/703"><img src="/guides/img/admin-11-plate-editor-desktop-4219ad93.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="690" height="703"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:42.5%;top:83.8%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:49.6%;top:29.9%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:4.3%;top:77.4%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:15.5%;top:83.8%" aria-hidden="true">4</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:18.1%;top:91.2%" aria-hidden="true">5</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>The covered photo replaces the public one; the original is kept privately. Keyboard: N adds a box, the arrows move it, Shift and the arrows resize it, Delete removes it.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-publish" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Publish</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A real car that is not on the site is a line on To do: press <b class="gd-ui">Set rates and publish</b>. The daily rate is filled in (the car&#39;s own, or the suggested rate from similar cars or the class); change it if you like and press <b class="gd-ui">Publish now</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">On the car itself, the Listing tab has <b class="gd-ui">Publish now</b>; each open item of its checklist has a button to where it is done.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">From a listing review: press <b class="gd-ui">Approve and publish</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Approve, publish later</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Send back</b> with what to fix.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>The plate check never holds a car back: a real photo whose plate is not checked stays private (the other photos, or the sample photos, show instead) and goes public by itself once its plate is covered or marked not visible. Listings already live show &quot;Plate not checked&quot; on such photos.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-photos-filed-under-the-wrong-shot-and-interior-windows" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Photos filed under the wrong shot, and interior windows</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On the Photos card, each shot lists its photos. A photo filed under the wrong shot: press <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> under it, then <b class="gd-ui">Remove it</b>. The shot is free again: take or pick the right photo. The removed photo is kept privately and the removal is in the history. A live listing&#39;s photos change in the review instead (Reject).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Dashboard and seat photos: what shows through the windows is replaced by the studio background when the cut is clean (a quality check: some but not most of the frame seen through, high in the frame, a few clean regions, sharp edges). Otherwise the windows are blurred, and the photo is marked windows blurred. Nothing to do.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A car with 2 seats or fewer needs no Rear seats photo.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-a-listing-without-photos-yet-sample-photos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A listing without photos yet: sample photos</h2><p class="gd-p">A car can be listed before its photos are taken. Until then the site shows a sample photo.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Submit the listing without photos. The listing copy is still written for you from the car&#39;s details.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The car page and the car&#39;s card show a sample photo, captioned &quot;Sample photo&quot;, so renters know it is not this car. Staff see &quot;Using sample photos&quot; on the car and in Listings.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Publishing does not wait for a plate check: a sample photo has no plate.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Add the real photos when they are taken. Once real photos are approved they replace the sample at once; nothing else to do.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-sample-photos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Sample photos</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Sample photos</b>. The pictures a car shows until its real photos are in.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Every body type has a built-in picture (sedan, SUV, truck, van, coupe, hatchback, electric car).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Add your own: choose the Body type, and a Make and Model if the photo is of that exact model, pick the Photo, and press <b class="gd-ui">Add the photo</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The most specific photo wins: make and model, then make and body type, then body type. <b class="gd-ui">Turn off</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Delete</b> a photo you no longer want.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Cars using sample photos lists the cars still waiting for real photos. Each real car showing sample photos is also a line on To do, with <b class="gd-ui">Add photos</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/settings/sample-photos</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/812"><img src="/guides/img/admin-36-sample-photos-desktop-55c64070.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="812"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:26.8%;top:28.9%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-publish-now-and-new-cars-published-by-themselves" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Publish now, and new cars published by themselves</h2><p class="gd-p">Nothing between a new car and the site has to be finished first: the car goes on the site, and what is still open shows on its checklist.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Publish new cars automatically</b> (on by default): a new real car goes on the site by itself as soon as it has its year, make and model and its rates, when it is added with rates, when its rates are saved, when it is added for an owner, or when an owner&#39;s application is approved.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Otherwise open the car: its Listing tab says why it is not on the site and has <b class="gd-ui">Publish now</b>. A car with no rates yet is published with the suggested rates (similar cars, else the class defaults in Program settings); change them later on the Rates tab.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Every real car has its listing from the moment it is added, as a draft. It shows in Listings and in Not on the site yet until it is published.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">An owner&#39;s own application waits for your decision before its car is published by itself; Publish now still works.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">A car taken off the site by staff, or scheduled for a later date, is never published by itself: press <b class="gd-ui">Publish now</b>.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-the-checklist-what-is-still-open-on-a-listed-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The checklist: what is still open on a listed car</h2><p class="gd-p">Open items never stop publishing. They show as warnings on the car&#39;s Listing tab and after Publish now.</p><div class="gd-tablewrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Table"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Item</th><th scope="col">What it means</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Paperwork</td><td>Ownership permit, registry forms, agreements signed, Forms C and D, upfront payment, registry visit, tracker, safety certificate</td></tr><tr><td>Insurance</td><td>Not on the fleet insurance policy yet: the car can be booked, but not handed over</td></tr><tr><td>Details</td><td>Colour, body, seats, gearbox: the car page leaves out what is missing</td></tr><tr><td>Photos</td><td>No real photos: sample photos stand in. A photo whose plate is not checked stays private until it is</td></tr><tr><td>No VIN yet</td><td>A car added by its plate alone: add the VIN when you have it</td></tr><tr><td>Possible duplicate</td><td>An open flag in Similar cars. Only Same car keeps the car off the site</td></tr><tr><td>Owner terms</td><td>The management fee (Revenue Share) and fees not set: a request uses the owner&#39;s terms or the standard grid</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-the-fleet-policy-rule-at-handover" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The fleet policy rule at handover</h2><p class="gd-p">A program owner&#39;s car is listed and can be requested, offered and paid for while its paperwork is open. It is never handed over until the insurer confirms in writing that it is on the fleet insurance policy.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Staff see a warning on a request and an offer for a car not on the policy yet.</li><li>The handover refuses the car until the insurer&#39;s confirmation is recorded (Owners and onboarding). The field app says so on the job.</li><li>Only real states keep a car off the site: retired, left the program, out of service, Turo only, bookings turned off, a self-managed owner in arrears, or a paused listing.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-cars-on-sample-photos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Cars on sample photos</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b> ends with <b class="gd-ui">Cars on sample photos</b>: each real car whose page still shows sample photos, with its newest handover photos (the check-in and check-out photos field staff take).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Where a handover photographed the car, press <b class="gd-ui">Use the handover photos</b>. They go into the car&#39;s listing as if taken on the capture screen.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">When every required shot is there, the listing is submitted: Gemini makes each photo from the original, then the listing waits for your review like any other.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A car with no handover photos yet gets them at its next handover, or press <b class="gd-ui">Start a listing</b> and take them.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>The listing photos use no Cloudflare image processing: Gemini makes every photo and the site makes the sizes.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-a-car-s-registration-and-documents" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A car&#39;s registration and documents</h2><p class="gd-p">Open the car, then <b class="gd-ui">Owner &amp; documents</b>. The <b class="gd-ui">Registration</b> card:</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Correct the <b class="gd-ui">VIN</b> (it is checked: 17 characters, the check digit, not on another car; decoded again for the body style and trim), the <b class="gd-ui">Year</b> and the <b class="gd-ui">Body style</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Type the <b class="gd-ui">Ontario permit number</b> and the date the <b class="gd-ui">Plate sticker expires</b>. Fleet gets a task 30 days and 7 days before; save the new date after the renewal and the task closes.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Under <b class="gd-ui">Documents</b>, choose the kind (<b class="gd-ui">Ownership permit</b>, Safety Standards Certificate, owner&#39;s insurance, other), pick the photo or PDF and press <b class="gd-ui">Upload</b>. The ownership permit clears that item of the owner&#39;s checklist.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">For the <b class="gd-ui">Safety Standards Certificate</b>, also type its number, the date it was issued and the date it expires. Fleet gets a task 30 days and 7 days before it expires; upload the new certificate with its dates and the task closes. It is a document on the car, not a service record, and nothing is billed to the owner.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Add a car</b> takes the ownership permit and the Safety Standards Certificate too, under <b class="gd-ui">Documents (optional)</b>.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-a-car-added-under-the-wrong-owner" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A car added under the wrong owner</h2><p class="gd-p">Open the car, Overview, <b class="gd-ui">Who supplies the car</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Move to another owner</b>. Choose the owner, or <b class="gd-ui">CarmaCars (owner not known yet)</b>: the car becomes a company car, with no owner schedule or terms.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>The car&#39;s unsigned owner application and vehicle schedule are withdrawn (kept in the history), and its draft owner invoices are deleted. Nobody is notified.</li><li>It is refused once anything for the car is signed, issued, paid or on a statement.</li></ul><h3 class="gd-h3">The VIN from the car, not typed</h3><p class="gd-p">Every VIN field (Add a car, Add a car for an owner, the car&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Registration</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Start a listing</b>) has <b class="gd-ui">Scan the barcode</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Photo of the VIN</b>. Scan the barcode in the driver&#39;s door frame or at the bottom of the windshield: the phone&#39;s camera reads it by itself. Or take a photo of the VIN plate or sticker: the barcode in it is read first, else the photo is read for the printed VIN. The VIN is checked (17 characters, the check digit; I, O and Q become 1 and 0) and decoded as when you type it. Check it against the car before saving.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">Photos in any order</h3><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Add photos</b> on the listing takes any number of photos at once from the camera roll. Each is sorted to its shot by itself (front three-quarter, sides, rear, dashboard, seats and the rest); a shot that already has its photo sends the new one to the extra photos, so nothing is replaced by accident. The shots are a guide, not a rule: a listing is complete with 10 photos that can go on the site and one outside photo for the cover. Outside photos get the studio background: the car is cropped to its edges and placed big in the frame with its wheels on the floor and a soft shadow under the tyres, and any corner watermark or caption beside the car is left out. Inside and detail photos are kept as taken; when one has a watermark, a logo or caption text on it, the edge with the mark is cut off by itself, and a photo whose mark cannot be cut off (one in the middle) stays off the site until you replace it. <b class="gd-ui">Cover the plate</b> opens on every outside photo with the plate box suggested; check it and save.</p><p class="gd-p">Outside photos made before the newest framing (the car small in the frame, or without the model&#39;s name behind it) are made again with <b class="gd-ui">Frame the outside photos again</b> above the photos of the listing, then <b class="gd-ui">Yes, frame again</b>. The cover and the main outside views get the model&#39;s name lettered behind the car, as on the sample photos (for example CLA, C CLASS, AMG GT). The photos leave the site until their plates are checked again: the plate box is suggested on the new photos; check each and cover it. On a published listing each goes back on the site once its plate is checked.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-showroom-photos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Showroom photos</h2><p class="gd-p">Outside photos go in the CarmaCars showroom by themselves. When a real photographed room is stored (dealership or studio photos licensed for commercial use, fetched once from Wikimedia Commons with their author and licence kept), the car stands in it: about 70% of the width, its wheels on the room&#39;s floor, a soft shadow and a faint reflection under it, its light matched to the room, and no sign or lettering on the real wall. Program settings &gt; Listings has the switch (Photographed showroom rooms, on), the car&#39;s width and the cut-out quality floor: a cut-out that is not clean enough (pieces, a blurry or ragged edge) is never placed in a room, the real photo is used instead (its plate covered as usual) and the photo says so. Without a stored room it is the drawn dark showroom: a simple dark dealership with linear lights in the ceiling, a slatted wood wall between two light strips with a big lit CarmaCars sign, and a polished dark floor with the car&#39;s reflection and a shadow under each tyre. Every angle of a car is in the same room, and the cover has the model&#39;s name in metal letters on the wall under the sign. The image model may relight the car or turn it slightly; a photo that shows another car, model or colour is not used. <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b> has the switch (Showroom photos, on), the image model that makes the photos look photographed, and its daily limit. Past the limit, or when the image model is not available, the site makes the showroom itself for free, and the photo says why under it.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>A car whose photos were made on the black studio: press <b class="gd-ui">Apply showroom to this car</b> above its photos, then <b class="gd-ui">Yes, apply</b>.</li><li>Every car at once: <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Showroom photos</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Apply showroom to every car</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Yes, every car</b>.</li><li>Under a photo in the showroom: <b class="gd-ui">Redo</b> makes it again, <b class="gd-ui">Back to the original</b> puts back the version before the showroom.</li></ul><p class="gd-p">A car that stays where it was keeps its plate check. When the image model made the photo, check the plate again: the photo is off the site until you do. Photos made in the first showroom are made again in the new one with <b class="gd-ui">Apply showroom to this car</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Apply showroom to every car</b>.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-failed-photos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Failed photos</h2><p class="gd-p">The site makes the photo sizes itself: the image service is asked only to cut the car out (<b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b>: the switch to let the image service make every photo step is off). When the image service is busy or over its allowance, the photo still goes on the site from the original and is made again later. A listing marked Failed has <b class="gd-ui">Retry failed photos</b> in its note; <b class="gd-ui">Retry failed photos</b> at the top does every listing. They are made again a few at a time, and the listing leaves Failed when they are done.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-the-primary-photo-is-always-the-front-exterior-release-43" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The primary photo is always the front exterior (release 43)</h2><p class="gd-p">The first photo of every car on the site, in the cards, the feeds and the Marketplace kit is its exterior at the standard angle (front three-quarter, in the dark showroom). An inside photo is never ahead of an outside one, and the cover mark follows by itself whenever photos are added, made again or reordered.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">Primary photo is not exterior</b> is a flag and a filter in <b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Vehicles</b>: it marks a car whose first photo is an inside one because its best outside photo is not on the site yet, or it has none. Add or approve an outside photo and the flag clears by itself.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Redo photos with Gemini</b> on the car page makes every photo of the car again from its original with Gemini, and generates its missing angles. A photo Gemini cannot make well stays off the site, flagged. It needs the image model switched on in Program settings, Listings.</li><li>The same press checks the car&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Other detail</b> photos again: an outside view filed there is moved to the outside photos (the front three-quarter becomes the first photo) and made in the showroom. This is what clears the flag on a car that showed nothing to redo.</li><li>Every outside photo has the same room behind it: Gemini replaces the whole background from the original photo.</li><li>Every plate is blurred; nothing is drawn on it and there is no text anywhere else. Inside photos stay sharp from front to back.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Redo every car with Gemini</b> (Listings, Showroom photos; Admin and Fleet) is the same as <b class="gd-ui">Redo every car</b> on the Photo standard card.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-the-photo-standard-every-photo-made-by-gemini-release-45" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The photo standard: every photo made by Gemini (release 45)</h2><p class="gd-p">Every listing photo is made by Gemini from the original photo, never from a cut-out. Outside photos get their whole background replaced by the CarmaCars showroom, with nothing of the place they were taken in left. Inside photos are cleaned up (no clutter) and sharp from front to back. Every plate is blurred so no character can be read; no plate is drawn and there is no text anywhere else on the photo.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">The check.</b> A second Gemini look compares each new photo with the original and refuses it when the old background shows, the car is warped, another colour or model, has parts added or missing, a plate can be read, or there is text anywhere. The site also checks the edges are the dark showroom. A refused photo is made again, twice; then it stays off the site and is counted as flagged.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Missing angles.</b> Every car shows the standard set: front three-quarter, front, side profile, rear three-quarter, rear, dashboard, front seats, rear seats and trunk. An angle the car has no photo of is generated by Gemini from the car&#39;s own photos, in the same showroom, and marked <b class="gd-ui">AI generated</b> on the listing (staff only). A real photo of that angle replaces it by itself.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">The order.</b> The front three-quarter is always first, then the other outside photos, then the inside ones. A car whose first photo would be an inside one shows no photos and cannot be published until it has an outside one; its front three-quarter is generated first.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">By itself.</b> Every 5 minutes the job brings the next cars to the standard, newest listed cars first, until every car is done (about a day for the whole fleet). A photo already at the standard is never made again unless you ask. <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b>: the daily Gemini limit (2000 calls), the calls kept for new uploads (50) and the switch.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Listings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Photo standard</b> (Admin and Fleet) shows each car: photos at the standard out of all, AI angles, flagged photos and the last run. <b class="gd-ui">Redo this car now</b> makes all of its photos again at once; <b class="gd-ui">Redo every car</b> makes every photo of every car again. <b class="gd-ui">Redo photos with Gemini</b> on a car page does the same as Redo this car now.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-the-first-photo-plain-with-a-model-or-a-flyer" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The first photo: plain, with a model, or a flyer</h2><p class="gd-p">On a listing, under <b class="gd-ui">First photo</b>, choose what shows first on the site and in the Marketplace kit. Switch any time; the other photos stay as they are.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">Plain car</b>: the cover photo as it is (the default).</li><li><b class="gd-ui">With a model</b>: a car-show photo made by the image model, with a fully clothed adult model beside the car. It needs the image model; until it is made (or when the image model is not there) the plain cover shows, and the listing says why.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Flyer</b>: the cover photo with a band like a printed flyer: the car, the price a day from its live rates, the call to action, a badge and the logo. When the price, the words or the cover photo change, it is made again by itself within 10 minutes; the plain cover shows meanwhile.</li></ul><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Make it again</b> makes the chosen one again. The words of the flyer and the description of the model are in <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b> (First photo &quot;flyer&quot; and First photo &quot;with a model&quot;); {car}, {price}, {weekly} and {monthly} are filled for each car.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-marketing-photos-in-other-scenes" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Marketing photos in other scenes</h2><p class="gd-p">For Marketplace and social posts, a car&#39;s outside photos can be made again in other scenes. The website keeps its own photos in the dark showroom: a marketing set never replaces them.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On a listing, under <b class="gd-ui">Marketing photos</b>, choose a scene, or <b class="gd-ui">Mix: a different scene on each photo</b>, and press <b class="gd-ui">Make the marketing set</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The copies show as they are made. The dark showroom and the plain white studio are made by the site when the image model is not there; the photographic scenes (a bright showroom, a city street at night, the Toronto waterfront, a parking garage, Highway, a scenic road, Brick building) need the image model, and say so on the copy when it is not there.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Download (ZIP)</b> takes the set; the Marketplace kit&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">With scenes (ZIP)</b> takes the same set.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Marketing scenes</b> lists the scenes. A scene made in a real place has a photo of that place: Brick building picks its photo by itself: the widest outside photo, as taken, of the shareholders&#39; own cars. To use another, press <b class="gd-ui">Change the reference photo</b> and pick one (the shareholders&#39; cars&#39; photos come first), or upload one. The scenes&#39; names and words are in the <b class="gd-ui">Marketing scenes</b> setting.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-extra-photos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Extra photos</h2><p class="gd-p">A photo that fits no shot is an extra photo. Under the shots, <b class="gd-ui">Extra outside photos</b> (put on the studio background) and <b class="gd-ui">Extra inside and detail photos</b> (touched up) each take any number at once. They count toward the 10 photos, get the same plate check, and come after the standard shots on the car&#39;s page.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">In the review, <b class="gd-ui">Extra photos, in their order on the car page</b> lists them.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Drag a photo by its handle (⋮⋮), or press <b class="gd-ui">Earlier</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Later</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the order</b>.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-fix-a-cut-out" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Fix a cut-out</h2><p class="gd-p">When the background removal cuts badly (a mirror or a wheel missing, background left beside the car), press <b class="gd-ui">Edit the cut-out</b> under the outside photo.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Cut-out</b> shows the car over the photo as taken, shown faintly. Choose <b class="gd-ui">Erase</b> and brush over what should go, or <b class="gd-ui">Restore</b> and brush over what the cut-out took off. Set <b class="gd-ui">Brush size</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Zoom</b>; when zoomed, <b class="gd-ui">Move the view</b> pans. <b class="gd-ui">Undo</b> takes back the last stroke.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">On the studio</b> shows the car on the studio background. Drag the car to move it and use <b class="gd-ui">Size</b> to make it larger or smaller. <b class="gd-ui">Centre and full size</b> puts it back.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save as a new version</b>. The photo is made again in about a minute; the version before and the photo as taken are kept. <b class="gd-ui">Reset to the automatic cut-out</b> starts again from the automatic one.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>If the car did not move, the plate check carries over: a photo marked no plate visible stays so, and a covered plate is covered again on the new photo when the review is open. If the car moved, check the plate again. A photo made before cut-outs were kept shows <b class="gd-ui">Make the cut-out</b> first; the editor opens by itself when it is ready.</div></aside><p class="gd-p">Every photo also gets a light touch-up by itself (exposure, levels, a little contrast and colour, mild sharpening), never enough to change the paint colour or hide a scratch. Turn it off for one photo with <b class="gd-ui">Use original colours</b> under it (the photo is made again; approve it again), or for every photo in Admin &gt; Settings &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> (Listings) with <b class="gd-ui">Auto-enhance listing photos</b>. The photo as uploaded is always kept.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-import-photos-from-a-google-drive-link" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Import photos from a Google Drive link</h2><p class="gd-p">The owner often hands over a car&#39;s photos as a public Google Drive folder, or one big folder with a folder per make and then per car. You do not download them: paste the link.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">One car.</b> On the car&#39;s listing, under the capture, <b class="gd-ui">Import photos from a Google Drive link</b>. Paste the folder link (shared with Anyone with the link) and press <b class="gd-ui">Import the photos</b>. Every photo in the folder, and in the folders inside it, is added to this car as if you had pressed Add photos: each is sorted to its shot (else filed as an extra photo, in file-name order), put on the studio background and checked for its plate. The box under the link, <b class="gd-ui">Submit the listing for processing when its photos are in</b>, is on by default.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Many cars.</b> <b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Import photos from Drive</b> (a button on Vehicles). Paste the top folder&#39;s link and press <b class="gd-ui">Read the folder</b>. The page walks every folder and proposes a car for each folder that holds photos, from the year, make, model, colour and plate in the folder names (the make folder above counts; 01 Motors partner cars come first). Check the table: tick or untick <b class="gd-ui">Import</b>, change the car in the list (the likely cars come first), leave out a folder with <b class="gd-ui">Do not import this folder</b>. A line marked <b class="gd-ui">Check this one</b> matched two alike cars. Then press <b class="gd-ui">Import N photos from M folders</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The page follows the import by itself. You can leave it and come back: it runs in the background.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The end shows the summary: imported, skipped and failed, and why for each (a file over 15 MB, a file that is not a photo, the same photo already on the car, a folder not shared).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Try the failed photos again</b> takes only the ones that failed. Pressing Import on the same link again never adds a photo twice: a Drive file already on the car is skipped, and so is the same picture under another name. A photo you took off the car can be imported again.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>JPG, PNG, HEIC and WebP only (HEIC and WebP are made JPEG first). At most 15 MB a photo, 600 photos, 400 folders and 4 GB in one import. Drive is asked politely, one photo at a time; a big import takes a while.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Without a key, Drive shows only the first 50 files of a folder on its public page; a folder with more is read in full when Drive allows it. In <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Photo import from Google Drive</b> box takes a Google API key with the Drive API on (after it is saved only its last 4 characters are shown, and it is never written to the change log): with it, folders of any size are read and photos download without Drive&#39;s warning pages.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-test-bookings-and-deleting-a-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Test bookings and deleting a car</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On a booking made only to try the site, press <b class="gd-ui">Mark as a test booking</b> (Admins only; the reason is optional). <b class="gd-ui">Make it a real booking again</b> undoes it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">A car whose bookings are all test bookings can be deleted: the test bookings and their test payments go with it, and a copy is kept in the archive of deleted requests.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A car with a real booking cannot be deleted.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-pickup-from-owner-and-return-to-owner-release-28" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Pickup from owner and return to owner (release 28)</h2><p class="gd-p">On a car&#39;s page, <b class="gd-ui">Pickup from owner and return to owner</b> records the car&#39;s condition when CarmaCars picks it up from its owner or gives it back: the date and time, km, fuel, many photos at once with the suggested angles, and notes. <b class="gd-ui">Add photos</b> adds more to a record later. The owner sees these records read only on the car&#39;s page in their portal. They are the baseline condition for any dispute.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-incident-cards-release-34" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Incident cards (release 34)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Vehicles</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Incident cards</b> prints the card for each car: what to do in an accident or a breakdown, the support number from Settings, a roadside number when there is one, a QR code to report it in the app, and the fleet insurance slip. Open a car and press <b class="gd-ui">Incident card</b> to print only that car; on the list, <b class="gd-ui">Print all cars</b> prints them all, two cards to a Letter page with crop marks, ready to laminate. Under Fleet insurance policy press <b class="gd-ui">Add the policy</b> (the insurer, the policy number, the dates, the named insured, the roadside number on the slip) and choose the uploaded slip if you have one: it is printed as it is, otherwise the fields are. The card never shows a premium. Fleet staff print the same cards from their portal.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-field-jobs-shifts-and-who-gets-a-job" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Field jobs, shifts and who gets a job</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Field jobs</b>, is the board Fleet uses, with every action Fleet has. Shifts are published by themselves from the shift template in Program settings (one shift of 10:00 to 17:00 every second day by default, 14 days ahead, only forward from the latest shift), with a shift of its own for any handover or return no shift covers; <b class="gd-ui">Publish shifts</b> adds more by hand, and a shift you cancel is not published again. Field staff take them. <b class="gd-ui">Missing check-in and check-out</b>, on the same page, lists every past rental without its photos and readings, with <b class="gd-ui">Give to field staff</b>. Jobs go on shifts, not on people: each job is put on the shift covering its time (or that day&#39;s), whoever holds the shift does it (several people share the jobs, least busy first), a shift nobody holds keeps its jobs for whoever claims it, and work lands only on days with shifts (work due on a day without shifts moves to the day before, or to the next day with shifts when it comes in on the day; the booking&#39;s own times never change). A booking whose handover or return falls on a day with no shifts shows a warning on the board and on the booking. <b class="gd-ui">To a shift</b> moves a job to another shift. You can give a job to a field person on a shift that day or to an Admin, take it off with <b class="gd-ui">Unassign</b> (tick <b class="gd-ui">Tell them</b> to let them know), and an Admin who holds a job opens it on the field portal. A person who has not passed the academy cannot be given a job or take a shift. A shift with jobs and nobody on it within 24 hours alerts Fleet and the Admins once.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-every-view-generated-from-the-car-s-photos-release-47" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Every view generated from the car&#39;s photos (release 47)</h2><p class="gd-p">Every car shows nine generated views: front three-quarter (always first), front, side profile, rear three-quarter, rear, dashboard, front seats, rear seats and trunk. Gemini makes each one from references, so the car is the real car and the room looks like a real showroom.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">What Gemini is sent.</b> The car&#39;s own photos (its exact colour, trim and wheels); when it has fewer than three, or none of that side, its newest check-in and check-out photos as well (only as references: they are never shown on the site). Then the sample view of that angle (for the camera position only), the stock photo of the model, and for an outside view the showroom background plate. The words describe each angle: camera height, lens, crop, the car centred, 45 degrees for a three-quarter. Plates blurred, no text, no logos added.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">The check.</b> A second Gemini look compares the result with the real photos (same car, colour, wheels and trim, nothing warped, not a render) and with the angle. A refused view is made again, twice, told what was wrong; still refused, it is flagged and the car&#39;s real photo of that angle stays on the site.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">The real photos.</b> They stay in the car&#39;s record and on the Admin car page, marked as they were; the site shows the generated view of an angle in place of the real one only once it has passed. Generated views are marked <b class="gd-ui">AI generated</b> for staff only.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">By itself.</b> Every 5 minutes the job takes the front three-quarter of every car first (newest listed first), then the other angles, within the daily Gemini limit (about a day for the whole fleet). <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b>: the switch for the generated views.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Listings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Photo standard</b> shows each car&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Generated set</b> (views made out of nine, being made, flagged, and &quot;from check-in photos&quot; when those were used). <b class="gd-ui">Redo this car now</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Redo every car</b> make the generated views again too; the views on the site stay until the new ones pass.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Showroom background plates</b> (<b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b>, Admin): the room for front, side and rear views. Gemini made them once and a second look confirmed each looks like a real photo. Upload a real photo of a showroom (empty floor in the middle, no people, cars, signs or logos) to replace one or all three; <b class="gd-ui">Make a new one</b> has Gemini make it again.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-the-studio-set-every-car-photographed-the-same-way-release-4" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The studio set: every car photographed the same way (release 48)</h2><p class="gd-p">Every car gets the same nine views, as if all were photographed in one studio on one day: the same angle, camera height, lens and framing for each view, the car facing the same way as the sample covers (the front three-quarter and the side with the nose to the left), plates taken off cleanly, the car itself unchanged.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>The scene: every car stands in the same scene so the covers line up as you scroll: the dark dealership with the CarmaCars sign on the wall by default, with the model&#39;s name on the wall behind the car on the first photo. <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b>: the scene for every car. On a car, <b class="gd-ui">Studio photos</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Scene</b> picks another for that car only (highway, brick building and the other marketing scenes).</li><li>No photo of an angle? Gemini makes it from the car&#39;s other photos. A car with no photo at all gets its outside views from the stock photo of its model, in its own colour.</li><li>One set everywhere: once a car&#39;s front three-quarter is made, the site shows only its made views, in the standard order, the front three-quarter first: the same photo on the home page, the search cards, the car page, the partner feeds and in the sitemap. The real photos stay in the car&#39;s record.</li><li>The check: Gemini checks each view against the car&#39;s own photos: the same car (model, colour, wheels), the right angle, the nose the right way, the old background gone (the site also measures it), no readable plate. Smaller doubts (framing, a part the photos do not show) stop only the first two tries.</li><li>On a car, <b class="gd-ui">Studio photos</b> shows each view beside the car&#39;s own photos of that angle, marked <b class="gd-ui">AI</b>. <b class="gd-ui">Make again</b> makes one view again; <b class="gd-ui">Take off the site</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Put on the site</b>.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Listings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Photo standard</b> shows the fleet&#39;s progress: views made out of all, cars with their studio cover, and about how many days are left at Gemini&#39;s daily limit.</li><li>Marketing set: <b class="gd-ui">Make the marketing set</b> uses the studio views (the same angle and cover as the site) in the scene you choose, plus up to three lifestyle shots: an adult model with the car, styled like a luxury car advert, always fully dressed and tasteful. Each is marked <b class="gd-ui">AI</b>; tick <b class="gd-ui">In the ZIP</b> for the photos you want in a post. A lifestyle shot Gemini declines is skipped.</li><li>Background plates (<b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b>, Admin): one set per scene. Choose the scene, then upload a real photo of the place to replace one or all three.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-studio-renders-first-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Studio renders first (release 48)</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Every car gets the full studio set made from its own photos: same colour, wheels and trim, the same framing for every car.</li><li>On the site the renders come first, in this order: side profile (the nose to the left, the cover), front three-quarter, front, rear three-quarter, rear, dashboard, front seats, rear seats, trunk. The car&#39;s own photos follow, on the same branded background. They are never hidden.</li><li>A render goes live as soon as it passes the photo check. There is no approval step. To change one, open the car, <b class="gd-ui">Studio photos</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Make again</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Take off the site</b>. Taking the side profile off makes the next render the cover.</li><li>The car page says <b class="gd-ui">Rendered photos</b> above the gallery, with <b class="gd-ui">See its real photos</b>.</li><li>New cars get their renders by themselves. To do every published car now: <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Photo standard</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Render every published car</b>. The line beside it shows how many cars are done. It works within the image model&#39;s daily limit.</li><li>When a car&#39;s set is live, the owner gets an email and an alert (&quot;Your car has new studio photos&quot;), and Fleet gets &quot;Studio photos live&quot; in the next digest. Look the photos over.</li><li>The Cars filter lists one model per family (for example CLA-Class or 3 Series). The trim shows on the car. A car whose model family is not recognised is listed in <b class="gd-ui">Data health</b>: fix the typo, or ask for the family to be added.</li></ul></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'owners-and-onboarding', 'chapter', 'chauffeur-service', 'Owners apply on the site with List your car. Every application waits for you in one place, Applications: approve it, ask the owner for something, or decline it. Approved owners sign and pay in their portal.

## Applications

**People** > **Applications**. Every owner application, newest first.

1. The chips filter by status: New, Waiting on owner, Approved, Declined, or All. New applications also show on To do.
2. Each row shows the application number, the owner, the car, how many of the four checks are done, and when they applied.
3. Open an application to decide.

![](/guides/img/admin-33-applications-desktop-152f9e34.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 640; address: carmacars.ca/admin/applications; pins: 1 36.8 39.7, 2 48.6 53.1, 3 19.8 53.1")

## Decide on an application

One page holds everything: the owner, the car, the uploads, the four checks and the notes.

1. Check the driver''s licence, the ownership, the insurance and the lender or lessor. Mark each one Checked, fine, Problem or Not needed.
2. Press **Approve**. The step "Terms and first invoice" opens for each car, filled in with the owner''s negotiated terms (or the standard grid): Insurance Fee, Tracker Fee, management fee (Revenue Share), Install Fee and the first and last month amount (2 x the Insurance Fee unless you type an exact amount). Change any of them to the cent; with several cars, **Use these terms for every car** copies the first car''s numbers to the others.
3. Choose the invoices: First and last month, Registration fee (any exact amount), Tracker install (only once trackers are available) and Another invoice. For each one choose Send now, Save as draft or Already paid. Already paid asks how (e-Transfer, cash, cheque, bank transfer or other), the date and the reference: it is recorded like Record payment and the owner gets no email (no invoice, no receipt) unless you tick the receipt.
4. Press **Approve** at the bottom of the step. Nothing is set or sent before that. The owner becomes active, the documents open for one signature in their portal, only the invoices you chose are made, and the owner gets one email.
5. Missing something? Press **Ask for something**, tick what you need (for example the ownership permit or the insurance slip), add a message if you like, and press **Send to the owner**. The owner gets an email and a task in their portal; the application shows Waiting on owner until they answer.
6. Not a fit? Press **Decline**, write the Reason the owner reads, and press **Decline the application**. The owner is emailed for each car.

![](/guides/img/admin-34-application-desktop-98b64f92.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 812; address: carmacars.ca/admin/applications/c324ef8d-ad00-4bcc-bf04-ca68628a26b4; pins: 1 72.9 67.1, 2 73.9 42.9, 3 84.7 42.9, 4 72.9 49.6")

The application has an Invoices tab: every invoice of its cars, drafts and voids included. An application staff entered for the owner says "Entered by staff" and who; approving it sends the owner the set-up email (review the details and sign) instead of the approval email.

> Tip: Notes on the page are for staff only: **Add note** keeps a line on the record. When the owner answers a request, their answer is in the notes and the application is New again.

## Add a car for an owner

**People** > **Owners**, the **Add a car** tab, or **Add another car** on an owner''s page. The owner never has to fill in the application.

1. The owner: find them by name, email or phone, or choose New owner and enter the name, email, phone and address.
2. The car: press **Take a photo** (or **Choose a photo**) under Fill this from the ownership permit, and the plate, VIN, colour, permit number and plate sticker expiry fill in, with the year, make, model code and body read for you to check. Each detail shows Checked, Check this (for example a VIN that fails its check digit, a plate not in the usual format, or a sticker already expired) or Type it; the photo is attached as the ownership permit. Or type the VIN. The car is looked up at once and shown in one line (Edit if something is wrong); no VIN at hand, add it by its plate with the year, make and model from the lists. Tap the colour, check the class, then the odometer, insurer and whether it is owned, financed or leased. Photos are optional: the listing shows sample photos until real ones are added. Upload the ownership permit, the insurance slip and the lender''s information if you have them.
3. Terms and first invoice: the same fields as Approve. For another car of the same owner they start from that owner''s terms, or their other car''s; change them for this car.
4. Who sourced the owner: Entered for CarmaCars, or I sourced this owner (only then are you recorded as the one who brought the owner). The owner signs in the owner portal after one email (no paper signature).
5. Press **Add the car and set it up**. The owner gets one email: review the details, correct anything, and sign. An owner with no sign-in gets the link to choose a password in that same email.

Customer service and fleet assistants add cars the same way from their portal; theirs wait in Applications for you, with the terms and invoices they proposed already filled in. On an approved application staff entered, **Send the set-up email again** sends the owner the email with a fresh link.

## Owners

**People** > **Owners**. Every owner, with their cars and where onboarding stands.

1. Each owner shows their application, how many cars, and where onboarding stands.
2. **View as (owner portal)** shows their portal. **Send password link** helps them sign in.
3. Invite an owner on file: fill in Name and Email under Invite an owner, then press **Send invitation**.

![](/guides/img/admin-12-owners-desktop-3a54d505.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 560; address: carmacars.ca/admin/owners; pins: 1 41.0 42.9, 2 37.4 49.3, 3 77.4 82.5")

The owner signs everything at once in their portal (Check and sign: the agreements, schedules and Forms A and B; the official registry forms are printed and signed in ink). The confirmations to tick, then one signature: CarmaCars countersigns at the same moment, under the signing officer''s standing authorization. A car with a second owner on the ownership waits for that owner too: they get their own link by email and sign the same documents.

## Mark a car insured (Insurer confirmed)

A program owner''s car is handed over to a renter only once the insurer confirms in writing that it is on the fleet policy. Requests, offers and payment never wait for it.

1. Each car waiting for the insurer is a line on To do: "Insurer has not confirmed : mark it insured". It says Now when a booking picks the car up soon.
2. When the insurer''s email arrives, press **Mark insured**. The date is today; change it to the date of the insurer''s email if it was earlier. Add its subject as the Reference if you like, and press **Insurer confirmed**.
3. One email for several cars? Press **Mark several insured** on the line " cars wait for the insurer". Every waiting car is ticked: untick any car the insurer did not name, check the date, and confirm them all at once.
4. The same button is on the car: Overview (**Insurer confirmed**) and the Listing tab''s checklist, item "Not on the fleet insurance policy yet".

The car is then on the fleet policy from that date: it can be handed over, its Enrollment Date is that date, its fee terms start, and the owner gets the email "Written confirmation: your car is on the fleet policy". Its paperwork (agreements, registry visit, tracker) stays on its checklist until done. A car already listed and Available stays Available.

## Owners who paid another way, and the terms you agreed

Two lines on To do keep an owner''s money right without opening their page.

1. "Record the first and last month paid by ": their first and last month invoice was voided and nothing paid is recorded. Press **Record what they paid**, type the amount for each car (tax included), or one total for several cars, how and when it was paid and the reference. A draft first and last month invoice is kept or voided, your choice. Each car''s invoice is then marked paid and the two prepaid months count; the owner gets no email unless you tick **Email the owner a receipt**. Never for a shareholder.
2. "Enter the terms agreed with ": their cars still use the standard grid. Press **Enter the terms**: the Management fee (Revenue Share), the Insurance Fee, the Tracker Fee, the Install Fee and the first and last month are filled in from the grid. Type what you agreed for the owner, and open a car to give it its own. A car whose schedule is signed gets an updated schedule for the owner to sign.
3. Nothing to change? Press **Not needed** or **These are correct**: the line does not come back.

## A shareholder''s own car

On the owner''s page, each car has **Shareholder’s own car**.

1. A shareholder''s own car is split 90/10 (the share in Program settings) and pays no Insurance Fee, Tracker Fee, first and last month or tracker install.
2. Press **Shareholder’s own car**, say why (it is kept in the audit log) and confirm. Press it again to undo. Bookings already made keep their split.
3. A first and last month or a tracker install invoice is refused for such a car, from any screen.

## Cancellation refunds

**Settings** > **Program**: the refund for each cancellation tier.

| When the renter cancels | Refund (default) |
| --- | --- |
| Within 24 hours of booking, 48 hours or more before the start | 95% |
| 48 hours or more before the start | 75% |
| 24 to 48 hours before the start | 50% |
| Under 24 hours, or after the start | 0% |

## An owner''s page

Open an owner from Owners. Three tabs: Overview, Terms and Invoices. **Add another car** and **New invoice** sit under the name.

1. The **Onboarding checklist**, at the top: per car still onboarding, each step done, to do (with who it waits on: the owner, us, an Admin or the registry), blocked (with why) or not needed, and one button for the next thing to do. The owner and customer service see the same checklist.
2. Cars and terms: each car''s Insurance Fee, Tracker Fee, management fee (Revenue Share), Install Fee and mode, with **Edit** and History (see An owner''s terms, car by car).
3. **Onboarding photos**: the ownership permit, insurance slip and lender''s permission of each car. **Replace**, **Remove** (with a reason), **Approve** or **Not accepted** (the owner reads why). A replaced photo that was approved is checked again. Every change is in the audit log.
4. **Government forms**: the ServiceOntario forms each car needs, made by themselves when the terms are approved and again when a value changes, each with its status, what it misses, when it was made and its download. **Make again** makes a car''s forms anew now (a form signed in ink is kept); the values changed by hand stay, unless you tick **Discard the values changed by hand**. Open a form and press **Change a value** to correct one box of the official form before it is signed: choose the box, type the value and the reason. The form is made again as a new version; the earlier versions stay under **Versions**, each with its download, and every change is in the audit log. **Back to the records** puts a box''s value from the records again. The owner always sees the current version only. Fleet can do the same. The owner signs each form on screen during onboarding. Beside the form, **Owner''s signature** shows the drawn signature (or typed name), who signed, when, from which IP address and device, and the version signed; the signature is never on the official form, and **Download the print-ready form** has no signature. If you change a value after the owner signed, the form shows **Changed since signed** with the boxes that changed, the owner gets one To do (the government forms step opens again) and one reminder email, and the earlier signature stays under **Every signature**. The step is done when every form is signed.
5. **Add cars from a list of VINs**: paste or upload the VINs, **Preview**, then **Add**; a typo, a duplicate or a car already with us is reported, not added.
6. Upfront invoices: issue the first and last month amount agreed on each car''s terms, for each car whose terms are set.
7. Owner: address, sign-in and agreements; statements and payouts for this owner.
8. Further down: **View as (owner portal)**, **Send password link** and **Send a sign-in link to the owner portal**.

A car''s page has the same Government forms box (Owner & documents).

![](/guides/img/admin-13-owner-desktop-819a9f8b.jpg "desktop; size: 410 1030; address: carmacars.ca/admin/owners/50a834dc-270a-4c26-b79e-6396fa7bf2e1; pins: 1 24.6 4.4, 2 16.1 32.9, 3 31.5 73.2, 4 21.2 98.1")

## An owner''s terms, car by car

The table Cars and terms, at the top of an owner''s page and its Terms tab: each car''s Insurance Fee and Tracker Fee a month, management fee (Revenue Share), Install Fee and Management Mode, and since when they apply.

1. Press **Edit** on a car''s row. The row becomes fields: type the exact amounts (to the cent; the management fee in %). Before the Vehicle Schedule is signed you can also change the Install Fee, the Management Mode and the Onboarding Method.
2. Press **Review**. It lists each value before and after, and what happens to each one. Nothing is saved yet.
3. Not signed yet (or not approved yet): **Save** applies the numbers at once. An unsigned Vehicle Schedule is made again with them, so the owner signs these numbers; a car not approved yet keeps them for the Approve step.
4. Signed: a lower amount is in force from today, or the date you choose under Lower amounts from. No notice period is needed because it only lowers what the owner pays. A lower management fee does this while Settings > Program, Lower management % without owner signature, is on (the default); off, the owner signs an updated Vehicle Schedule first.
5. Signed: a higher Insurance Fee or Tracker Fee needs 30 days'' written notice (Enrollment Agreement 4.8). Choose the date under Higher amounts from (30 days ahead at the earliest) and write the Reason: the owner reads it.
6. Signed: a higher management fee (Revenue Share) needs the same notice and the owner''s signature. The owner is emailed the notice and an updated Vehicle Schedule to sign; it applies from the date once signed, or from the day they sign if that is later. Higher fees in the same change apply from the date by the notice either way.
7. Press **Confirm**. The owner is emailed the written notice, which is also a PDF in their portal and in the car''s History.

History, under each car, lists every period of terms (from, to, the amounts, and why: the Vehicle Schedule, a written notice, lowered) and every change with its notice. A change that has not started yet has Cancel (give the reason): the terms before it run on. An updated schedule waiting for the owner has Withdraw it; the owner signs it in the owner portal (never on paper). One change at a time: cancel or finish the one waiting before making the next.

The same editor is on the car''s page (Records tab, Owner terms). The owner''s default terms (for cars whose terms are set later) and the first and last month invoice stay on the Terms tab.

> Good to know: Invoices follow the dates: a month whose Insurance Fee or Tracker Fee changes part way is billed per day at each rate. The Revenue Share of a rental is the one in force on the day it is booked.

## Pay an owner a flat monthly amount

Some owners want the same amount every month for a car instead of a revenue share and fees. An Admin only, car by car.

1. Open the owner''s Cars and terms table (or the car''s page) and press **Pay** on the car''s row.
2. Choose **Flat monthly payment**, type the **Amount a month** (for example 900.00), the date under **From** and, if it ends, the **Last day**. Write the Reason (kept in the history).
3. Press **Review**: it says what happens and lists any monthly invoice already issued for those days. Then press **Confirm**.
4. From that date the owner''s statement pays the amount every month (a part month by the day), with no revenue share and no Insurance Fee or Tracker Fee. Rentals ending on those days stay with CarmaCars, in the company figures.
5. Back to revenue share: press **Pay**, choose Revenue share and the date. The flat period ends the day before; every period stays in the list.

> Good to know: A month already on an approved owner statement never changes: a new date starts after it. A monthly invoice already issued for flat days stays: void or credit it. A booking expense on a flat car is CarmaCars'' own unless you press **Charge to the owner** beside it on the booking (an Admin only): it is then an owner cost on their statement. Owner costs recorded on the owner''s account (tickets, tolls, damage of their own use) are charged as before.

## Change a signed car''s Management Mode

Managed, Self-Managed or Turo-Only, from a date, for a car whose Vehicle Schedule is signed. An Admin only.

1. Open the owner''s Cars and terms table (or the car''s page) and press **Change mode** on the car''s row.
2. Choose the **New Management Mode** and its Onboarding Method (the options that fit how the car is held), the date under **From**, and write the Reason: the owner reads it. Tick **The owner asked for this** only when it is their own request.
3. Press **Review**: it lists each value before and after (a Self-Managed car has no management fee; a Turo-Only car has no Fees and leaves the fleet insurance policy) and says whether the owner has to sign. Nothing is saved yet.
4. The owner asked and no amount goes up: no signature and no notice period. From today (or the date you chose) the car has the new mode, an updated Vehicle Schedule is issued with CarmaCars'' signature and the owner is emailed the notice.
5. Anything else (CarmaCars'' own decision, or a higher fee): the owner is emailed the notice and an updated Vehicle Schedule to sign, the date is at least 30 days away and the car stays as it is until it is signed. The owner signs it in the owner portal; in History, **Withdraw it** if needed.
6. A change dated ahead applies by itself on its date: the schedule is issued and the car moves. **Cancel** in History (give the reason) stops it and emails the owner that their terms stay as they are. The same email goes when a notice of a higher fee is cancelled.

> Good to know: A shareholder-owned car has fixed terms. A car whose schedule is not signed yet changes its mode in the terms editor, where it applies at once.

## Paid and signed

**People** > **Owners**, the **Paid and signed** tab. What each owner still has to pay or sign, and how each item was done.

1. Each owner shows how many items are open and how many are done. Owners with nothing left are hidden; press Show every owner to see them.
2. Open **Checklist and quick actions**. Each line says Signed in the portal, Signed on paper (before November 2026), Paid by e-Transfer, Not signed, and so on.
3. Paid by e-Transfer, cheque, cash or bank transfer? Press **Record payment**. Choose Paid by, the Date received and the Reference (the cheque number for a cheque). Leave Amount empty for the full balance, or type less for a partial payment. Add a photo of the cheque or a screenshot if you have one.
4. Every agreement is signed in the owner portal: a signature on paper is not recorded. Only an official ServiceOntario form signed in ink is: press **Record an official form signed in ink**, choose the form, check Signed by and Date signed, and upload the scan.
5. The same checklist sits at the top of each owner''s page.
6. You rarely need to come here: an upfront or overdue owner invoice is a line on To do with **Record payment**, and an owner whose documents were sent two days ago or more and are not signed is a line with **Waiting to sign** (open the owner to send the link again). Both pop-ups are the same forms, filled in.

A recorded payment marks the invoice paid (or partly paid), stops the automatic debit for that amount, sends the owner a receipt, and shows "Paid by e-Transfer on " in their portal. An official form recorded as signed in ink counts as signed everywhere: the checklist, onboarding and the owner portal. The scan is kept privately with the owner''s documents.

> Watch out: Recorded the wrong thing, or a cheque bounced? Press **Void** beside it and give the reason. The invoice owes that amount again and the owner is told; a voided signature makes the item open again. Only an Admin can void.

## Forms C and D

**People** > **Owner forms**. Forms C and D are signed on screen in the owner portal, with the witnesses on the same screen (one for Form C, two for Form D), and approved at once; Part 2 of Form D is signed for CarmaCars from the stored signatures (the signing officer, and the second signing officer of Program settings as CarmaCars'' witness). This queue holds only photos of paper copies sent before November 2026.

1. Each row shows the owner, the form, the witnesses and when it was uploaded.
2. Press Open to read the photo or scan. Check each marked spot is signed or initialled.
3. Press **Approve**, or **Send back** with What to fix (the owner reads this).

![](/guides/img/admin-22-owner-forms-desktop-c20ad300.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 470; address: carmacars.ca/admin/owner-forms; pins: 1 29.2 52.3, 2 57.6 52.3, 3 76.7 52.3")

## The earnings calculator on List your car

People who think of listing their car see what it could earn, near the top of List your car and, smaller, at the start of the application. They pick the year, make and model (or type the VIN), the days rented a month (5 to 28, 18 at first) and their share (60% to 90%, 70% at first, "set in your agreement"). The page shows the month and the year: the daily rate of cars like theirs on the site (the same make and model, else the class average, else the class''s starting rate in Program settings) times the days, their share of it, less the monthly fees. "Just cheaper insurance" shows the fleet policy''s fee and what they would keep at only 5 days a month.

1. **Settings** > **Program**: **Earnings calculator on List your car: the monthly insurance fee shown** and **the monthly tracker fee shown**, in dollars a month.
2. Leave either one empty and the page says "Insurance and tracker fees: quoted in your agreement" and shows the earnings "before fees". No amount is ever made up.
3. Set both and the page takes them off the month and the year. Each owner''s real fees stay the ones in their agreement.

## Agreements: who still needs to sign

**Owners and partners** > **Owners** > **Agreements**. Every owner with the agreements their deal needs, and where each one stands.

1. Each owner shows their deal (revenue split, flat monthly or fleet lease) and one line per agreement: the Vehicle Enrollment Agreement, the Flat-Rate Vehicle Enrollment Agreement or the Fleet Supplier Lease Agreement, the Title-Holding and Lease Agreement, an Additional Vehicle Schedule for a car added later, the Partner agreement, and a Referral Override Agreement for each owner they referred.
2. Each line says **Signed**, **Sent, not signed**, **Not sent** or **Missing**. Missing means there is nothing to sign yet: set the terms of a car first, and the agreement is made from them.
3. Press **Send** (or **Send again**). The owner gets one email with the link to read and sign in their portal. An owner with no sign-in yet shows "invite first": press Invite on the Owners list.
4. Owners whose agreements are all signed are hidden; press Show every owner to see them. The same lines are at the top of each owner''s Terms tab.

> Good to know: "Awaiting lawyer OK" marks the Referral Override Agreement until the lawyer approves its text (Program settings). The Fleet Supplier Lease Agreement is approved. Owners can sign either way.

## A fleet supplier: the fleet lease

For a supplier''s corporation that leases many cars to CarmaCars. Open the owner, **Terms** tab, **Fleet lease**.

1. A supplier who signs up on the website as a fleet supplier (or whom staff add on the fleet supplier route) gets the default lease terms of Program settings and the default Upkeep Table at once: the card shows **Fleet supplier route**. To agree other numbers, press **Change the lease terms**.
2. A supplier on file without the route: press **Enter the lease terms** and type what you agreed: the Regular Rate and the Troubled Rate (the lease a month for each car of that tier), the Claim Profit Share, the Early Write-Off Share, the Write-Off Period in months, the Later Write-Off Share and the Notice Period in days.
3. Check the **Upkeep Table**: for each cost (engine, transmission, shocks, rustproofing, refurbishment, tires, brakes, oil changes, ball joints) the supplier or CarmaCars.
4. Add each car with **Add another car** on the owner''s page. The **Fleet lease** step asks for the tier (Regular or Troubled) and the delivery date: the tier is required and set once. No fee or invoice step: the supplier pays CarmaCars nothing, and no owner invoice or debit is ever made for these cars.
5. A car already on file: press **Put on the lease** beside it, with the delivery date and the tier.
6. The tier never changes. Typed the wrong one? Only an Admin can press **Correct the tier**, with what was entered by mistake. It is corrected from the delivery (or from the day after the last approved statement) and kept in the audit log.
7. The lease is paid in arrears on the 10th with the owner payouts: a car''s first payment is on the first 10th at least one full month after its delivery and covers every month up to then. Part months are paid by the day; the statement line shows the calculation (rate, days, total).
8. A claim on a leased car: settling it pays the supplier its Claim Profit Share of any profit, on its next statement. A write-off pays any lien first, then the supplier''s Early or Later Write-Off Share of the balance by the months in service.
9. An upkeep cost: **Record an upkeep cost**. A cost the Upkeep Table gives the supplier comes off its next lease payment; one CarmaCars pays is not billed.

> Watch out: New lease terms after the supplier signed wait for the supplier to sign the new agreement (it opens for signature at once). The cars keep the signed rates until then.

## Approve a fleet supplier''s cars

A supplier who signed up on the website: his application is in **Applications** like any other, with each car''s VIN, plate and the tier he chose.

1. Open the application. Check the ownership copy of each car (he uploads it in his portal), the tier and who the car is registered to now. Its ServiceOntario forms were filled in when he added it: the lease (SR-LV-006 with his corporation as the registrant, SR-LV-012 with CarmaCars holding the plates) and, for a car not yet in his corporation, the transfer (ON00453 when the corporation has no RIN; 013-0169 and 013-1155 when an officer moves his own car in). A form still missing a value (a RIN, the odometer) shows what is missing, as on the other routes.
2. A tier chosen by mistake: open the owner, **Terms** tab, **Fleet lease**, and press **Correct the tier** beside the car, with what was chosen by mistake. Only an Admin can, and only before approval; it is kept in the audit log.
3. Approve: there are no terms or invoices to set. Check **Delivered on** (the lease starts that day) and press **Approve**. Each car goes on the lease at its tier.
4. He signs in the owner portal only: the Fleet Supplier Lease Agreement and the Title-Holding and Lease Agreement, and Form B on screen, with the full e-signature and its audit trail. Paper signatures cannot be recorded for him. Form D is in his packet and signed on screen with two witnesses; Form C is not asked.

> Good to know: The Fleet Supplier Lease Agreement is final: the lawyer approved it, so it no longer shows "Awaiting lawyer OK". The default lease terms are in **Settings** > **Program settings** (Fleet supplier route); a change there applies to suppliers who sign up later.

> Good to know: Owners > **Add an owner** offers the same route: choose **A corporation**, then **Fleet supplier: leases the cars to CarmaCars**. So does **Add a car for an owner** for a new owner.
', 'Owners and onboarding', 'Applications, the terms and first invoice, adding a car for an owner, an owner''s terms and invoices, paid and signed, and Forms C and D.',
  'Owners apply on the site with List your car. Every application waits for you in one place, Applications: approve it, ask the owner for something, or decline it. Approved owners sign and pay in their portal.

## Applications

**People** > **Applications**. Every owner application, newest first.

1. The chips filter by status: New, Waiting on owner, Approved, Declined, or All. New applications also show on To do.
2. Each row shows the application number, the owner, the car, how many of the four checks are done, and when they applied.
3. Open an application to decide.

![](/guides/img/admin-33-applications-desktop-152f9e34.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 640; address: carmacars.ca/admin/applications; pins: 1 36.8 39.7, 2 48.6 53.1, 3 19.8 53.1")

## Decide on an application

One page holds everything: the owner, the car, the uploads, the four checks and the notes.

1. Check the driver''s licence, the ownership, the insurance and the lender or lessor. Mark each one Checked, fine, Problem or Not needed.
2. Press **Approve**. The step "Terms and first invoice" opens for each car, filled in with the owner''s negotiated terms (or the standard grid): Insurance Fee, Tracker Fee, management fee (Revenue Share), Install Fee and the first and last month amount (2 x the Insurance Fee unless you type an exact amount). Change any of them to the cent; with several cars, **Use these terms for every car** copies the first car''s numbers to the others.
3. Choose the invoices: First and last month, Registration fee (any exact amount), Tracker install (only once trackers are available) and Another invoice. For each one choose Send now, Save as draft or Already paid. Already paid asks how (e-Transfer, cash, cheque, bank transfer or other), the date and the reference: it is recorded like Record payment and the owner gets no email (no invoice, no receipt) unless you tick the receipt.
4. Press **Approve** at the bottom of the step. Nothing is set or sent before that. The owner becomes active, the documents open for one signature in their portal, only the invoices you chose are made, and the owner gets one email.
5. Missing something? Press **Ask for something**, tick what you need (for example the ownership permit or the insurance slip), add a message if you like, and press **Send to the owner**. The owner gets an email and a task in their portal; the application shows Waiting on owner until they answer.
6. Not a fit? Press **Decline**, write the Reason the owner reads, and press **Decline the application**. The owner is emailed for each car.

![](/guides/img/admin-34-application-desktop-98b64f92.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 812; address: carmacars.ca/admin/applications/c324ef8d-ad00-4bcc-bf04-ca68628a26b4; pins: 1 72.9 67.1, 2 73.9 42.9, 3 84.7 42.9, 4 72.9 49.6")

The application has an Invoices tab: every invoice of its cars, drafts and voids included. An application staff entered for the owner says "Entered by staff" and who; approving it sends the owner the set-up email (review the details and sign) instead of the approval email.

> Tip: Notes on the page are for staff only: **Add note** keeps a line on the record. When the owner answers a request, their answer is in the notes and the application is New again.

## Add a car for an owner

**People** > **Owners**, the **Add a car** tab, or **Add another car** on an owner''s page. The owner never has to fill in the application.

1. The owner: find them by name, email or phone, or choose New owner and enter the name, email, phone and address.
2. The car: press **Take a photo** (or **Choose a photo**) under Fill this from the ownership permit, and the plate, VIN, colour, permit number and plate sticker expiry fill in, with the year, make, model code and body read for you to check. Each detail shows Checked, Check this (for example a VIN that fails its check digit, a plate not in the usual format, or a sticker already expired) or Type it; the photo is attached as the ownership permit. Or type the VIN. The car is looked up at once and shown in one line (Edit if something is wrong); no VIN at hand, add it by its plate with the year, make and model from the lists. Tap the colour, check the class, then the odometer, insurer and whether it is owned, financed or leased. Photos are optional: the listing shows sample photos until real ones are added. Upload the ownership permit, the insurance slip and the lender''s information if you have them.
3. Terms and first invoice: the same fields as Approve. For another car of the same owner they start from that owner''s terms, or their other car''s; change them for this car.
4. Who sourced the owner: Entered for CarmaCars, or I sourced this owner (only then are you recorded as the one who brought the owner). The owner signs in the owner portal after one email (no paper signature).
5. Press **Add the car and set it up**. The owner gets one email: review the details, correct anything, and sign. An owner with no sign-in gets the link to choose a password in that same email.

Customer service and fleet assistants add cars the same way from their portal; theirs wait in Applications for you, with the terms and invoices they proposed already filled in. On an approved application staff entered, **Send the set-up email again** sends the owner the email with a fresh link.

## Owners

**People** > **Owners**. Every owner, with their cars and where onboarding stands.

1. Each owner shows their application, how many cars, and where onboarding stands.
2. **View as (owner portal)** shows their portal. **Send password link** helps them sign in.
3. Invite an owner on file: fill in Name and Email under Invite an owner, then press **Send invitation**.

![](/guides/img/admin-12-owners-desktop-3a54d505.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 560; address: carmacars.ca/admin/owners; pins: 1 41.0 42.9, 2 37.4 49.3, 3 77.4 82.5")

The owner signs everything at once in their portal (Check and sign: the agreements, schedules and Forms A and B; the official registry forms are printed and signed in ink). The confirmations to tick, then one signature: CarmaCars countersigns at the same moment, under the signing officer''s standing authorization. A car with a second owner on the ownership waits for that owner too: they get their own link by email and sign the same documents.

## Mark a car insured (Insurer confirmed)

A program owner''s car is handed over to a renter only once the insurer confirms in writing that it is on the fleet policy. Requests, offers and payment never wait for it.

1. Each car waiting for the insurer is a line on To do: "Insurer has not confirmed : mark it insured". It says Now when a booking picks the car up soon.
2. When the insurer''s email arrives, press **Mark insured**. The date is today; change it to the date of the insurer''s email if it was earlier. Add its subject as the Reference if you like, and press **Insurer confirmed**.
3. One email for several cars? Press **Mark several insured** on the line " cars wait for the insurer". Every waiting car is ticked: untick any car the insurer did not name, check the date, and confirm them all at once.
4. The same button is on the car: Overview (**Insurer confirmed**) and the Listing tab''s checklist, item "Not on the fleet insurance policy yet".

The car is then on the fleet policy from that date: it can be handed over, its Enrollment Date is that date, its fee terms start, and the owner gets the email "Written confirmation: your car is on the fleet policy". Its paperwork (agreements, registry visit, tracker) stays on its checklist until done. A car already listed and Available stays Available.

## Owners who paid another way, and the terms you agreed

Two lines on To do keep an owner''s money right without opening their page.

1. "Record the first and last month paid by ": their first and last month invoice was voided and nothing paid is recorded. Press **Record what they paid**, type the amount for each car (tax included), or one total for several cars, how and when it was paid and the reference. A draft first and last month invoice is kept or voided, your choice. Each car''s invoice is then marked paid and the two prepaid months count; the owner gets no email unless you tick **Email the owner a receipt**. Never for a shareholder.
2. "Enter the terms agreed with ": their cars still use the standard grid. Press **Enter the terms**: the Management fee (Revenue Share), the Insurance Fee, the Tracker Fee, the Install Fee and the first and last month are filled in from the grid. Type what you agreed for the owner, and open a car to give it its own. A car whose schedule is signed gets an updated schedule for the owner to sign.
3. Nothing to change? Press **Not needed** or **These are correct**: the line does not come back.

## A shareholder''s own car

On the owner''s page, each car has **Shareholder’s own car**.

1. A shareholder''s own car is split 90/10 (the share in Program settings) and pays no Insurance Fee, Tracker Fee, first and last month or tracker install.
2. Press **Shareholder’s own car**, say why (it is kept in the audit log) and confirm. Press it again to undo. Bookings already made keep their split.
3. A first and last month or a tracker install invoice is refused for such a car, from any screen.

## Cancellation refunds

**Settings** > **Program**: the refund for each cancellation tier.

| When the renter cancels | Refund (default) |
| --- | --- |
| Within 24 hours of booking, 48 hours or more before the start | 95% |
| 48 hours or more before the start | 75% |
| 24 to 48 hours before the start | 50% |
| Under 24 hours, or after the start | 0% |

## An owner''s page

Open an owner from Owners. Three tabs: Overview, Terms and Invoices. **Add another car** and **New invoice** sit under the name.

1. The **Onboarding checklist**, at the top: per car still onboarding, each step done, to do (with who it waits on: the owner, us, an Admin or the registry), blocked (with why) or not needed, and one button for the next thing to do. The owner and customer service see the same checklist.
2. Cars and terms: each car''s Insurance Fee, Tracker Fee, management fee (Revenue Share), Install Fee and mode, with **Edit** and History (see An owner''s terms, car by car).
3. **Onboarding photos**: the ownership permit, insurance slip and lender''s permission of each car. **Replace**, **Remove** (with a reason), **Approve** or **Not accepted** (the owner reads why). A replaced photo that was approved is checked again. Every change is in the audit log.
4. **Government forms**: the ServiceOntario forms each car needs, made by themselves when the terms are approved and again when a value changes, each with its status, what it misses, when it was made and its download. **Make again** makes a car''s forms anew now (a form signed in ink is kept); the values changed by hand stay, unless you tick **Discard the values changed by hand**. Open a form and press **Change a value** to correct one box of the official form before it is signed: choose the box, type the value and the reason. The form is made again as a new version; the earlier versions stay under **Versions**, each with its download, and every change is in the audit log. **Back to the records** puts a box''s value from the records again. The owner always sees the current version only. Fleet can do the same. The owner signs each form on screen during onboarding. Beside the form, **Owner''s signature** shows the drawn signature (or typed name), who signed, when, from which IP address and device, and the version signed; the signature is never on the official form, and **Download the print-ready form** has no signature. If you change a value after the owner signed, the form shows **Changed since signed** with the boxes that changed, the owner gets one To do (the government forms step opens again) and one reminder email, and the earlier signature stays under **Every signature**. The step is done when every form is signed.
5. **Add cars from a list of VINs**: paste or upload the VINs, **Preview**, then **Add**; a typo, a duplicate or a car already with us is reported, not added.
6. Upfront invoices: issue the first and last month amount agreed on each car''s terms, for each car whose terms are set.
7. Owner: address, sign-in and agreements; statements and payouts for this owner.
8. Further down: **View as (owner portal)**, **Send password link** and **Send a sign-in link to the owner portal**.

A car''s page has the same Government forms box (Owner & documents).

![](/guides/img/admin-13-owner-desktop-819a9f8b.jpg "desktop; size: 410 1030; address: carmacars.ca/admin/owners/50a834dc-270a-4c26-b79e-6396fa7bf2e1; pins: 1 24.6 4.4, 2 16.1 32.9, 3 31.5 73.2, 4 21.2 98.1")

## An owner''s terms, car by car

The table Cars and terms, at the top of an owner''s page and its Terms tab: each car''s Insurance Fee and Tracker Fee a month, management fee (Revenue Share), Install Fee and Management Mode, and since when they apply.

1. Press **Edit** on a car''s row. The row becomes fields: type the exact amounts (to the cent; the management fee in %). Before the Vehicle Schedule is signed you can also change the Install Fee, the Management Mode and the Onboarding Method.
2. Press **Review**. It lists each value before and after, and what happens to each one. Nothing is saved yet.
3. Not signed yet (or not approved yet): **Save** applies the numbers at once. An unsigned Vehicle Schedule is made again with them, so the owner signs these numbers; a car not approved yet keeps them for the Approve step.
4. Signed: a lower amount is in force from today, or the date you choose under Lower amounts from. No notice period is needed because it only lowers what the owner pays. A lower management fee does this while Settings > Program, Lower management % without owner signature, is on (the default); off, the owner signs an updated Vehicle Schedule first.
5. Signed: a higher Insurance Fee or Tracker Fee needs 30 days'' written notice (Enrollment Agreement 4.8). Choose the date under Higher amounts from (30 days ahead at the earliest) and write the Reason: the owner reads it.
6. Signed: a higher management fee (Revenue Share) needs the same notice and the owner''s signature. The owner is emailed the notice and an updated Vehicle Schedule to sign; it applies from the date once signed, or from the day they sign if that is later. Higher fees in the same change apply from the date by the notice either way.
7. Press **Confirm**. The owner is emailed the written notice, which is also a PDF in their portal and in the car''s History.

History, under each car, lists every period of terms (from, to, the amounts, and why: the Vehicle Schedule, a written notice, lowered) and every change with its notice. A change that has not started yet has Cancel (give the reason): the terms before it run on. An updated schedule waiting for the owner has Withdraw it; the owner signs it in the owner portal (never on paper). One change at a time: cancel or finish the one waiting before making the next.

The same editor is on the car''s page (Records tab, Owner terms). The owner''s default terms (for cars whose terms are set later) and the first and last month invoice stay on the Terms tab.

> Good to know: Invoices follow the dates: a month whose Insurance Fee or Tracker Fee changes part way is billed per day at each rate. The Revenue Share of a rental is the one in force on the day it is booked.

## Pay an owner a flat monthly amount

Some owners want the same amount every month for a car instead of a revenue share and fees. An Admin only, car by car.

1. Open the owner''s Cars and terms table (or the car''s page) and press **Pay** on the car''s row.
2. Choose **Flat monthly payment**, type the **Amount a month** (for example 900.00), the date under **From** and, if it ends, the **Last day**. Write the Reason (kept in the history).
3. Press **Review**: it says what happens and lists any monthly invoice already issued for those days. Then press **Confirm**.
4. From that date the owner''s statement pays the amount every month (a part month by the day), with no revenue share and no Insurance Fee or Tracker Fee. Rentals ending on those days stay with CarmaCars, in the company figures.
5. Back to revenue share: press **Pay**, choose Revenue share and the date. The flat period ends the day before; every period stays in the list.

> Good to know: A month already on an approved owner statement never changes: a new date starts after it. A monthly invoice already issued for flat days stays: void or credit it. A booking expense on a flat car is CarmaCars'' own unless you press **Charge to the owner** beside it on the booking (an Admin only): it is then an owner cost on their statement. Owner costs recorded on the owner''s account (tickets, tolls, damage of their own use) are charged as before.

## Change a signed car''s Management Mode

Managed, Self-Managed or Turo-Only, from a date, for a car whose Vehicle Schedule is signed. An Admin only.

1. Open the owner''s Cars and terms table (or the car''s page) and press **Change mode** on the car''s row.
2. Choose the **New Management Mode** and its Onboarding Method (the options that fit how the car is held), the date under **From**, and write the Reason: the owner reads it. Tick **The owner asked for this** only when it is their own request.
3. Press **Review**: it lists each value before and after (a Self-Managed car has no management fee; a Turo-Only car has no Fees and leaves the fleet insurance policy) and says whether the owner has to sign. Nothing is saved yet.
4. The owner asked and no amount goes up: no signature and no notice period. From today (or the date you chose) the car has the new mode, an updated Vehicle Schedule is issued with CarmaCars'' signature and the owner is emailed the notice.
5. Anything else (CarmaCars'' own decision, or a higher fee): the owner is emailed the notice and an updated Vehicle Schedule to sign, the date is at least 30 days away and the car stays as it is until it is signed. The owner signs it in the owner portal; in History, **Withdraw it** if needed.
6. A change dated ahead applies by itself on its date: the schedule is issued and the car moves. **Cancel** in History (give the reason) stops it and emails the owner that their terms stay as they are. The same email goes when a notice of a higher fee is cancelled.

> Good to know: A shareholder-owned car has fixed terms. A car whose schedule is not signed yet changes its mode in the terms editor, where it applies at once.

## Paid and signed

**People** > **Owners**, the **Paid and signed** tab. What each owner still has to pay or sign, and how each item was done.

1. Each owner shows how many items are open and how many are done. Owners with nothing left are hidden; press Show every owner to see them.
2. Open **Checklist and quick actions**. Each line says Signed in the portal, Signed on paper (before November 2026), Paid by e-Transfer, Not signed, and so on.
3. Paid by e-Transfer, cheque, cash or bank transfer? Press **Record payment**. Choose Paid by, the Date received and the Reference (the cheque number for a cheque). Leave Amount empty for the full balance, or type less for a partial payment. Add a photo of the cheque or a screenshot if you have one.
4. Every agreement is signed in the owner portal: a signature on paper is not recorded. Only an official ServiceOntario form signed in ink is: press **Record an official form signed in ink**, choose the form, check Signed by and Date signed, and upload the scan.
5. The same checklist sits at the top of each owner''s page.
6. You rarely need to come here: an upfront or overdue owner invoice is a line on To do with **Record payment**, and an owner whose documents were sent two days ago or more and are not signed is a line with **Waiting to sign** (open the owner to send the link again). Both pop-ups are the same forms, filled in.

A recorded payment marks the invoice paid (or partly paid), stops the automatic debit for that amount, sends the owner a receipt, and shows "Paid by e-Transfer on " in their portal. An official form recorded as signed in ink counts as signed everywhere: the checklist, onboarding and the owner portal. The scan is kept privately with the owner''s documents.

> Watch out: Recorded the wrong thing, or a cheque bounced? Press **Void** beside it and give the reason. The invoice owes that amount again and the owner is told; a voided signature makes the item open again. Only an Admin can void.

## Forms C and D

**People** > **Owner forms**. Forms C and D are signed on screen in the owner portal, with the witnesses on the same screen (one for Form C, two for Form D), and approved at once; Part 2 of Form D is signed for CarmaCars from the stored signatures (the signing officer, and the second signing officer of Program settings as CarmaCars'' witness). This queue holds only photos of paper copies sent before November 2026.

1. Each row shows the owner, the form, the witnesses and when it was uploaded.
2. Press Open to read the photo or scan. Check each marked spot is signed or initialled.
3. Press **Approve**, or **Send back** with What to fix (the owner reads this).

![](/guides/img/admin-22-owner-forms-desktop-c20ad300.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 470; address: carmacars.ca/admin/owner-forms; pins: 1 29.2 52.3, 2 57.6 52.3, 3 76.7 52.3")

## The earnings calculator on List your car

People who think of listing their car see what it could earn, near the top of List your car and, smaller, at the start of the application. Since release 48 the numbers are conservative and follow the season, and the result says plainly it is a rough estimate, not a promise.

They pick the year, make and model (or type the VIN), the **days rented in an average month** (4 to 22, 12 at first) and their share (60% to 90%, 70% at first, "set in your agreement"). The page then works a whole year, month by month:

- A month''s rented days are the days chosen times that month''s factor: summer runs above the average, winter under it, and the shoulder months (spring and fall) are the slowest.
- A rented day earns the daily rate of cars like theirs on the site (the same make and model, else the class average, else the class''s starting rate in Program settings) less a typical discount for weekly rates and offers.
- Their share of that, less the monthly fees.

It shows the average month, the year (the twelve months added up, never twelve of the best month), the range from the slowest month to the busiest, the rented days of each month as bars, and how many months the share would not cover the fees. "Just cheaper insurance" shows the fleet policy''s fee and what they would keep in their slowest month.

1. **Settings** > **Program**: **Earnings calculator on List your car: the monthly insurance fee shown** and **the monthly tracker fee shown**, in dollars a month.
2. Leave either one empty and the page says "Insurance and tracker fees: quoted in your agreement" and shows the earnings "before fees". No amount is ever made up.
3. Set both and the page takes them off every month and the year. Each owner''s real fees stay the ones in their agreement.
4. **Earnings calculator on List your car: the rented days of an average month it starts from** (12): keep it low, a new car takes months to fill.
5. **The percent that comes off the listed daily rate on a rented day** (15).
6. **The factor of each month** (jan to dec) against an average month (1.00): by default June 1.10, July and August 1.30, December 0.85, January and February 0.75, May and September 0.85, March and October 0.70, April and November 0.65. Every month must be there.

## Agreements: who still needs to sign

**Owners and partners** > **Owners** > **Agreements**. Every owner with the agreements their deal needs, and where each one stands.

1. Each owner shows their deal (revenue split, flat monthly or fleet lease) and one line per agreement: the Vehicle Enrollment Agreement, the Flat-Rate Vehicle Enrollment Agreement or the Fleet Supplier Lease Agreement, the Title-Holding and Lease Agreement, an Additional Vehicle Schedule for a car added later, the Partner agreement, and a Referral Override Agreement for each owner they referred.
2. Each line says **Signed**, **Sent, not signed**, **Not sent** or **Missing**. Missing means there is nothing to sign yet: set the terms of a car first, and the agreement is made from them.
3. Press **Send** (or **Send again**). The owner gets one email with the link to read and sign in their portal. An owner with no sign-in yet shows "invite first": press Invite on the Owners list.
4. Owners whose agreements are all signed are hidden; press Show every owner to see them. The same lines are at the top of each owner''s Terms tab.

> Good to know: "Awaiting lawyer OK" marks the Referral Override Agreement until the lawyer approves its text (Program settings). The Fleet Supplier Lease Agreement is approved. Owners can sign either way.

## A fleet supplier: the fleet lease

For a supplier''s corporation that leases many cars to CarmaCars. Open the owner, **Terms** tab, **Fleet lease**.

1. A supplier who signs up on the website as a fleet supplier (or whom staff add on the fleet supplier route) gets the default lease terms of Program settings and the default Upkeep Table at once: the card shows **Fleet supplier route**. To agree other numbers, press **Change the lease terms**.
2. A supplier on file without the route: press **Enter the lease terms** and type what you agreed: the Regular Rate and the Troubled Rate (the lease a month for each car of that tier), the Claim Profit Share, the Early Write-Off Share, the Write-Off Period in months, the Later Write-Off Share and the Notice Period in days.
3. Check the **Upkeep Table**: for each cost (engine, transmission, shocks, rustproofing, refurbishment, tires, brakes, oil changes, ball joints) the supplier or CarmaCars.
4. Add each car with **Add another car** on the owner''s page. The **Fleet lease** step asks for the tier (Regular or Troubled) and the delivery date: the tier is required and set once. No fee or invoice step: the supplier pays CarmaCars nothing, and no owner invoice or debit is ever made for these cars.
5. A car already on file: press **Put on the lease** beside it, with the delivery date and the tier.
6. The tier never changes. Typed the wrong one? Only an Admin can press **Correct the tier**, with what was entered by mistake. It is corrected from the delivery (or from the day after the last approved statement) and kept in the audit log.
7. The lease is paid in arrears on the 10th with the owner payouts: a car''s first payment is on the first 10th at least one full month after its delivery and covers every month up to then. Part months are paid by the day; the statement line shows the calculation (rate, days, total).
8. A claim on a leased car: settling it pays the supplier its Claim Profit Share of any profit, on its next statement. A write-off pays any lien first, then the supplier''s Early or Later Write-Off Share of the balance by the months in service.
9. An upkeep cost: **Record an upkeep cost**. A cost the Upkeep Table gives the supplier comes off its next lease payment; one CarmaCars pays is not billed.

> Watch out: New lease terms after the supplier signed wait for the supplier to sign the new agreement (it opens for signature at once). The cars keep the signed rates until then.

## Approve a fleet supplier''s cars

A supplier who signed up on the website: his application is in **Applications** like any other, with each car''s VIN, plate and the tier he chose.

1. Open the application. Check the ownership copy of each car (he uploads it in his portal), the tier and who the car is registered to now. Its ServiceOntario forms were filled in when he added it: the lease (SR-LV-006 with his corporation as the registrant, SR-LV-012 with CarmaCars holding the plates) and, for a car not yet in his corporation, the transfer (ON00453 when the corporation has no RIN; 013-0169 and 013-1155 when an officer moves his own car in). A form still missing a value (a RIN, the odometer) shows what is missing, as on the other routes.
2. A tier chosen by mistake: open the owner, **Terms** tab, **Fleet lease**, and press **Correct the tier** beside the car, with what was chosen by mistake. Only an Admin can, and only before approval; it is kept in the audit log.
3. Approve: there are no terms or invoices to set. Check **Delivered on** (the lease starts that day) and press **Approve**. Each car goes on the lease at its tier.
4. He signs in the owner portal only: the Fleet Supplier Lease Agreement and the Title-Holding and Lease Agreement, and Form B on screen, with the full e-signature and its audit trail. Paper signatures cannot be recorded for him. Form D is in his packet and signed on screen with two witnesses; Form C is not asked.

> Good to know: The Fleet Supplier Lease Agreement is final: the lawyer approved it, so it no longer shows "Awaiting lawyer OK". The default lease terms are in **Settings** > **Program settings** (Fleet supplier route); a change there applies to suppliers who sign up later.

> Good to know: Owners > **Add an owner** offers the same route: choose **A corporation**, then **Fleet supplier: leases the cars to CarmaCars**. So does **Add a car for an owner** for a new owner.
',
  '<p class="gd-p">Owners apply on the site with List your car. Every application waits for you in one place, Applications: approve it, ask the owner for something, or decline it. Approved owners sign and pay in their portal.</p><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-applications" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Applications</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Applications</b>. Every owner application, newest first.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The chips filter by status: New, Waiting on owner, Approved, Declined, or All. New applications also show on To do.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Each row shows the application number, the owner, the car, how many of the four checks are done, and when they applied.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Open an application to decide.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/applications</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/640"><img src="/guides/img/admin-33-applications-desktop-152f9e34.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="640"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:36.8%;top:39.7%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:48.6%;top:53.1%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:19.8%;top:53.1%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-decide-on-an-application" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Decide on an application</h2><p class="gd-p">One page holds everything: the owner, the car, the uploads, the four checks and the notes.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Check the driver&#39;s licence, the ownership, the insurance and the lender or lessor. Mark each one Checked, fine, Problem or Not needed.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b>. The step &quot;Terms and first invoice&quot; opens for each car, filled in with the owner&#39;s negotiated terms (or the standard grid): Insurance Fee, Tracker Fee, management fee (Revenue Share), Install Fee and the first and last month amount (2 x the Insurance Fee unless you type an exact amount). Change any of them to the cent; with several cars, <b class="gd-ui">Use these terms for every car</b> copies the first car&#39;s numbers to the others.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Choose the invoices: First and last month, Registration fee (any exact amount), Tracker install (only once trackers are available) and Another invoice. For each one choose Send now, Save as draft or Already paid. Already paid asks how (e-Transfer, cash, cheque, bank transfer or other), the date and the reference: it is recorded like Record payment and the owner gets no email (no invoice, no receipt) unless you tick the receipt.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b> at the bottom of the step. Nothing is set or sent before that. The owner becomes active, the documents open for one signature in their portal, only the invoices you chose are made, and the owner gets one email.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Missing something? Press <b class="gd-ui">Ask for something</b>, tick what you need (for example the ownership permit or the insurance slip), add a message if you like, and press <b class="gd-ui">Send to the owner</b>. The owner gets an email and a task in their portal; the application shows Waiting on owner until they answer.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Not a fit? Press <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b>, write the Reason the owner reads, and press <b class="gd-ui">Decline the application</b>. The owner is emailed for each car.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/applications/c324ef8d-ad00-4bcc-bf04-ca68628a26b4</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/812"><img src="/guides/img/admin-34-application-desktop-98b64f92.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="812"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:72.9%;top:67.1%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:73.9%;top:42.9%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:84.7%;top:42.9%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:72.9%;top:49.6%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div><p class="gd-p">The application has an Invoices tab: every invoice of its cars, drafts and voids included. An application staff entered for the owner says &quot;Entered by staff&quot; and who; approving it sends the owner the set-up email (review the details and sign) instead of the approval email.</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Notes on the page are for staff only: <b class="gd-ui">Add note</b> keeps a line on the record. When the owner answers a request, their answer is in the notes and the application is New again.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-add-a-car-for-an-owner" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Add a car for an owner</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Owners</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Add a car</b> tab, or <b class="gd-ui">Add another car</b> on an owner&#39;s page. The owner never has to fill in the application.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The owner: find them by name, email or phone, or choose New owner and enter the name, email, phone and address.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The car: press <b class="gd-ui">Take a photo</b> (or <b class="gd-ui">Choose a photo</b>) under Fill this from the ownership permit, and the plate, VIN, colour, permit number and plate sticker expiry fill in, with the year, make, model code and body read for you to check. Each detail shows Checked, Check this (for example a VIN that fails its check digit, a plate not in the usual format, or a sticker already expired) or Type it; the photo is attached as the ownership permit. Or type the VIN. The car is looked up at once and shown in one line (Edit if something is wrong); no VIN at hand, add it by its plate with the year, make and model from the lists. Tap the colour, check the class, then the odometer, insurer and whether it is owned, financed or leased. Photos are optional: the listing shows sample photos until real ones are added. Upload the ownership permit, the insurance slip and the lender&#39;s information if you have them.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Terms and first invoice: the same fields as Approve. For another car of the same owner they start from that owner&#39;s terms, or their other car&#39;s; change them for this car.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Who sourced the owner: Entered for CarmaCars, or I sourced this owner (only then are you recorded as the one who brought the owner). The owner signs in the owner portal after one email (no paper signature).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Add the car and set it up</b>. The owner gets one email: review the details, correct anything, and sign. An owner with no sign-in gets the link to choose a password in that same email.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">Customer service and fleet assistants add cars the same way from their portal; theirs wait in Applications for you, with the terms and invoices they proposed already filled in. On an approved application staff entered, <b class="gd-ui">Send the set-up email again</b> sends the owner the email with a fresh link.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-owners" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Owners</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Owners</b>. Every owner, with their cars and where onboarding stands.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each owner shows their application, how many cars, and where onboarding stands.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">View as (owner portal)</b> shows their portal. <b class="gd-ui">Send password link</b> helps them sign in.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Invite an owner on file: fill in Name and Email under Invite an owner, then press <b class="gd-ui">Send invitation</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/owners</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/560"><img src="/guides/img/admin-12-owners-desktop-3a54d505.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="560"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:41%;top:42.9%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:37.4%;top:49.3%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:77.4%;top:82.5%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div><p class="gd-p">The owner signs everything at once in their portal (Check and sign: the agreements, schedules and Forms A and B; the official registry forms are printed and signed in ink). The confirmations to tick, then one signature: CarmaCars countersigns at the same moment, under the signing officer&#39;s standing authorization. A car with a second owner on the ownership waits for that owner too: they get their own link by email and sign the same documents.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-mark-a-car-insured-insurer-confirmed" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Mark a car insured (Insurer confirmed)</h2><p class="gd-p">A program owner&#39;s car is handed over to a renter only once the insurer confirms in writing that it is on the fleet policy. Requests, offers and payment never wait for it.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each car waiting for the insurer is a line on To do: &quot;Insurer has not confirmed : mark it insured&quot;. It says Now when a booking picks the car up soon.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">When the insurer&#39;s email arrives, press <b class="gd-ui">Mark insured</b>. The date is today; change it to the date of the insurer&#39;s email if it was earlier. Add its subject as the Reference if you like, and press <b class="gd-ui">Insurer confirmed</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">One email for several cars? Press <b class="gd-ui">Mark several insured</b> on the line &quot; cars wait for the insurer&quot;. Every waiting car is ticked: untick any car the insurer did not name, check the date, and confirm them all at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The same button is on the car: Overview (<b class="gd-ui">Insurer confirmed</b>) and the Listing tab&#39;s checklist, item &quot;Not on the fleet insurance policy yet&quot;.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">The car is then on the fleet policy from that date: it can be handed over, its Enrollment Date is that date, its fee terms start, and the owner gets the email &quot;Written confirmation: your car is on the fleet policy&quot;. Its paperwork (agreements, registry visit, tracker) stays on its checklist until done. A car already listed and Available stays Available.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-owners-who-paid-another-way-and-the-terms-you-agreed" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Owners who paid another way, and the terms you agreed</h2><p class="gd-p">Two lines on To do keep an owner&#39;s money right without opening their page.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">&quot;Record the first and last month paid by &quot;: their first and last month invoice was voided and nothing paid is recorded. Press <b class="gd-ui">Record what they paid</b>, type the amount for each car (tax included), or one total for several cars, how and when it was paid and the reference. A draft first and last month invoice is kept or voided, your choice. Each car&#39;s invoice is then marked paid and the two prepaid months count; the owner gets no email unless you tick <b class="gd-ui">Email the owner a receipt</b>. Never for a shareholder.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">&quot;Enter the terms agreed with &quot;: their cars still use the standard grid. Press <b class="gd-ui">Enter the terms</b>: the Management fee (Revenue Share), the Insurance Fee, the Tracker Fee, the Install Fee and the first and last month are filled in from the grid. Type what you agreed for the owner, and open a car to give it its own. A car whose schedule is signed gets an updated schedule for the owner to sign.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Nothing to change? Press <b class="gd-ui">Not needed</b> or <b class="gd-ui">These are correct</b>: the line does not come back.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-a-shareholder-s-own-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A shareholder&#39;s own car</h2><p class="gd-p">On the owner&#39;s page, each car has <b class="gd-ui">Shareholder’s own car</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A shareholder&#39;s own car is split 90/10 (the share in Program settings) and pays no Insurance Fee, Tracker Fee, first and last month or tracker install.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Shareholder’s own car</b>, say why (it is kept in the audit log) and confirm. Press it again to undo. Bookings already made keep their split.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A first and last month or a tracker install invoice is refused for such a car, from any screen.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-cancellation-refunds" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Cancellation refunds</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b>: the refund for each cancellation tier.</p><div class="gd-tablewrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Table"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">When the renter cancels</th><th scope="col">Refund (default)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Within 24 hours of booking, 48 hours or more before the start</td><td>95%</td></tr><tr><td>48 hours or more before the start</td><td>75%</td></tr><tr><td>24 to 48 hours before the start</td><td>50%</td></tr><tr><td>Under 24 hours, or after the start</td><td>0%</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-an-owner-s-page" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">An owner&#39;s page</h2><p class="gd-p">Open an owner from Owners. Three tabs: Overview, Terms and Invoices. <b class="gd-ui">Add another car</b> and <b class="gd-ui">New invoice</b> sit under the name.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The <b class="gd-ui">Onboarding checklist</b>, at the top: per car still onboarding, each step done, to do (with who it waits on: the owner, us, an Admin or the registry), blocked (with why) or not needed, and one button for the next thing to do. The owner and customer service see the same checklist.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Cars and terms: each car&#39;s Insurance Fee, Tracker Fee, management fee (Revenue Share), Install Fee and mode, with <b class="gd-ui">Edit</b> and History (see An owner&#39;s terms, car by car).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Onboarding photos</b>: the ownership permit, insurance slip and lender&#39;s permission of each car. <b class="gd-ui">Replace</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> (with a reason), <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Not accepted</b> (the owner reads why). A replaced photo that was approved is checked again. Every change is in the audit log.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Government forms</b>: the ServiceOntario forms each car needs, made by themselves when the terms are approved and again when a value changes, each with its status, what it misses, when it was made and its download. <b class="gd-ui">Make again</b> makes a car&#39;s forms anew now (a form signed in ink is kept); the values changed by hand stay, unless you tick <b class="gd-ui">Discard the values changed by hand</b>. Open a form and press <b class="gd-ui">Change a value</b> to correct one box of the official form before it is signed: choose the box, type the value and the reason. The form is made again as a new version; the earlier versions stay under <b class="gd-ui">Versions</b>, each with its download, and every change is in the audit log. <b class="gd-ui">Back to the records</b> puts a box&#39;s value from the records again. The owner always sees the current version only. Fleet can do the same. The owner signs each form on screen during onboarding. Beside the form, <b class="gd-ui">Owner&#39;s signature</b> shows the drawn signature (or typed name), who signed, when, from which IP address and device, and the version signed; the signature is never on the official form, and <b class="gd-ui">Download the print-ready form</b> has no signature. If you change a value after the owner signed, the form shows <b class="gd-ui">Changed since signed</b> with the boxes that changed, the owner gets one To do (the government forms step opens again) and one reminder email, and the earlier signature stays under <b class="gd-ui">Every signature</b>. The step is done when every form is signed.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Add cars from a list of VINs</b>: paste or upload the VINs, <b class="gd-ui">Preview</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Add</b>; a typo, a duplicate or a car already with us is reported, not added.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Upfront invoices: issue the first and last month amount agreed on each car&#39;s terms, for each car whose terms are set.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">Owner: address, sign-in and agreements; statements and payouts for this owner.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">8</span><div class="gd-t">Further down: <b class="gd-ui">View as (owner portal)</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Send password link</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Send a sign-in link to the owner portal</b>.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">A car&#39;s page has the same Government forms box (Owner &amp; documents).</p><div class="gd-figblock"><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/owners/50a834dc-270a-4c26-b79e-6396fa7bf2e1</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:410/1030"><img src="/guides/img/admin-13-owner-desktop-819a9f8b.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="410" height="1030"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:24.6%;top:4.4%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:16.1%;top:32.9%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:31.5%;top:73.2%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:21.2%;top:98.1%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-an-owner-s-terms-car-by-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">An owner&#39;s terms, car by car</h2><p class="gd-p">The table Cars and terms, at the top of an owner&#39;s page and its Terms tab: each car&#39;s Insurance Fee and Tracker Fee a month, management fee (Revenue Share), Install Fee and Management Mode, and since when they apply.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Edit</b> on a car&#39;s row. The row becomes fields: type the exact amounts (to the cent; the management fee in %). Before the Vehicle Schedule is signed you can also change the Install Fee, the Management Mode and the Onboarding Method.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Review</b>. It lists each value before and after, and what happens to each one. Nothing is saved yet.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Not signed yet (or not approved yet): <b class="gd-ui">Save</b> applies the numbers at once. An unsigned Vehicle Schedule is made again with them, so the owner signs these numbers; a car not approved yet keeps them for the Approve step.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Signed: a lower amount is in force from today, or the date you choose under Lower amounts from. No notice period is needed because it only lowers what the owner pays. A lower management fee does this while Settings &gt; Program, Lower management % without owner signature, is on (the default); off, the owner signs an updated Vehicle Schedule first.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Signed: a higher Insurance Fee or Tracker Fee needs 30 days&#39; written notice (Enrollment Agreement 4.8). Choose the date under Higher amounts from (30 days ahead at the earliest) and write the Reason: the owner reads it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Signed: a higher management fee (Revenue Share) needs the same notice and the owner&#39;s signature. The owner is emailed the notice and an updated Vehicle Schedule to sign; it applies from the date once signed, or from the day they sign if that is later. Higher fees in the same change apply from the date by the notice either way.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Confirm</b>. The owner is emailed the written notice, which is also a PDF in their portal and in the car&#39;s History.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">History, under each car, lists every period of terms (from, to, the amounts, and why: the Vehicle Schedule, a written notice, lowered) and every change with its notice. A change that has not started yet has Cancel (give the reason): the terms before it run on. An updated schedule waiting for the owner has Withdraw it; the owner signs it in the owner portal (never on paper). One change at a time: cancel or finish the one waiting before making the next.</p><p class="gd-p">The same editor is on the car&#39;s page (Records tab, Owner terms). The owner&#39;s default terms (for cars whose terms are set later) and the first and last month invoice stay on the Terms tab.</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Invoices follow the dates: a month whose Insurance Fee or Tracker Fee changes part way is billed per day at each rate. The Revenue Share of a rental is the one in force on the day it is booked.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-pay-an-owner-a-flat-monthly-amount" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Pay an owner a flat monthly amount</h2><p class="gd-p">Some owners want the same amount every month for a car instead of a revenue share and fees. An Admin only, car by car.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open the owner&#39;s Cars and terms table (or the car&#39;s page) and press <b class="gd-ui">Pay</b> on the car&#39;s row.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose <b class="gd-ui">Flat monthly payment</b>, type the <b class="gd-ui">Amount a month</b> (for example 900.00), the date under <b class="gd-ui">From</b> and, if it ends, the <b class="gd-ui">Last day</b>. Write the Reason (kept in the history).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Review</b>: it says what happens and lists any monthly invoice already issued for those days. Then press <b class="gd-ui">Confirm</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">From that date the owner&#39;s statement pays the amount every month (a part month by the day), with no revenue share and no Insurance Fee or Tracker Fee. Rentals ending on those days stay with CarmaCars, in the company figures.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Back to revenue share: press <b class="gd-ui">Pay</b>, choose Revenue share and the date. The flat period ends the day before; every period stays in the list.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A month already on an approved owner statement never changes: a new date starts after it. A monthly invoice already issued for flat days stays: void or credit it. A booking expense on a flat car is CarmaCars&#39; own unless you press <b class="gd-ui">Charge to the owner</b> beside it on the booking (an Admin only): it is then an owner cost on their statement. Owner costs recorded on the owner&#39;s account (tickets, tolls, damage of their own use) are charged as before.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-change-a-signed-car-s-management-mode" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Change a signed car&#39;s Management Mode</h2><p class="gd-p">Managed, Self-Managed or Turo-Only, from a date, for a car whose Vehicle Schedule is signed. An Admin only.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open the owner&#39;s Cars and terms table (or the car&#39;s page) and press <b class="gd-ui">Change mode</b> on the car&#39;s row.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose the <b class="gd-ui">New Management Mode</b> and its Onboarding Method (the options that fit how the car is held), the date under <b class="gd-ui">From</b>, and write the Reason: the owner reads it. Tick <b class="gd-ui">The owner asked for this</b> only when it is their own request.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Review</b>: it lists each value before and after (a Self-Managed car has no management fee; a Turo-Only car has no Fees and leaves the fleet insurance policy) and says whether the owner has to sign. Nothing is saved yet.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The owner asked and no amount goes up: no signature and no notice period. From today (or the date you chose) the car has the new mode, an updated Vehicle Schedule is issued with CarmaCars&#39; signature and the owner is emailed the notice.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Anything else (CarmaCars&#39; own decision, or a higher fee): the owner is emailed the notice and an updated Vehicle Schedule to sign, the date is at least 30 days away and the car stays as it is until it is signed. The owner signs it in the owner portal; in History, <b class="gd-ui">Withdraw it</b> if needed.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">A change dated ahead applies by itself on its date: the schedule is issued and the car moves. <b class="gd-ui">Cancel</b> in History (give the reason) stops it and emails the owner that their terms stay as they are. The same email goes when a notice of a higher fee is cancelled.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A shareholder-owned car has fixed terms. A car whose schedule is not signed yet changes its mode in the terms editor, where it applies at once.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-paid-and-signed" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Paid and signed</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Owners</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Paid and signed</b> tab. What each owner still has to pay or sign, and how each item was done.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each owner shows how many items are open and how many are done. Owners with nothing left are hidden; press Show every owner to see them.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Checklist and quick actions</b>. Each line says Signed in the portal, Signed on paper (before November 2026), Paid by e-Transfer, Not signed, and so on.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Paid by e-Transfer, cheque, cash or bank transfer? Press <b class="gd-ui">Record payment</b>. Choose Paid by, the Date received and the Reference (the cheque number for a cheque). Leave Amount empty for the full balance, or type less for a partial payment. Add a photo of the cheque or a screenshot if you have one.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Every agreement is signed in the owner portal: a signature on paper is not recorded. Only an official ServiceOntario form signed in ink is: press <b class="gd-ui">Record an official form signed in ink</b>, choose the form, check Signed by and Date signed, and upload the scan.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The same checklist sits at the top of each owner&#39;s page.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">You rarely need to come here: an upfront or overdue owner invoice is a line on To do with <b class="gd-ui">Record payment</b>, and an owner whose documents were sent two days ago or more and are not signed is a line with <b class="gd-ui">Waiting to sign</b> (open the owner to send the link again). Both pop-ups are the same forms, filled in.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">A recorded payment marks the invoice paid (or partly paid), stops the automatic debit for that amount, sends the owner a receipt, and shows &quot;Paid by e-Transfer on &quot; in their portal. An official form recorded as signed in ink counts as signed everywhere: the checklist, onboarding and the owner portal. The scan is kept privately with the owner&#39;s documents.</p><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>Recorded the wrong thing, or a cheque bounced? Press <b class="gd-ui">Void</b> beside it and give the reason. The invoice owes that amount again and the owner is told; a voided signature makes the item open again. Only an Admin can void.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-forms-c-and-d" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Forms C and D</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Owner forms</b>. Forms C and D are signed on screen in the owner portal, with the witnesses on the same screen (one for Form C, two for Form D), and approved at once; Part 2 of Form D is signed for CarmaCars from the stored signatures (the signing officer, and the second signing officer of Program settings as CarmaCars&#39; witness). This queue holds only photos of paper copies sent before November 2026.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each row shows the owner, the form, the witnesses and when it was uploaded.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press Open to read the photo or scan. Check each marked spot is signed or initialled.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Send back</b> with What to fix (the owner reads this).</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/owner-forms</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/470"><img src="/guides/img/admin-22-owner-forms-desktop-c20ad300.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="470"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:29.2%;top:52.3%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:57.6%;top:52.3%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:76.7%;top:52.3%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-the-earnings-calculator-on-list-your-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The earnings calculator on List your car</h2><p class="gd-p">People who think of listing their car see what it could earn, near the top of List your car and, smaller, at the start of the application. Since release 48 the numbers are conservative and follow the season, and the result says plainly it is a rough estimate, not a promise.</p><p class="gd-p">They pick the year, make and model (or type the VIN), the <b class="gd-ui">days rented in an average month</b> (4 to 22, 12 at first) and their share (60% to 90%, 70% at first, &quot;set in your agreement&quot;). The page then works a whole year, month by month:</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>A month&#39;s rented days are the days chosen times that month&#39;s factor: summer runs above the average, winter under it, and the shoulder months (spring and fall) are the slowest.</li><li>A rented day earns the daily rate of cars like theirs on the site (the same make and model, else the class average, else the class&#39;s starting rate in Program settings) less a typical discount for weekly rates and offers.</li><li>Their share of that, less the monthly fees.</li></ul><p class="gd-p">It shows the average month, the year (the twelve months added up, never twelve of the best month), the range from the slowest month to the busiest, the rented days of each month as bars, and how many months the share would not cover the fees. &quot;Just cheaper insurance&quot; shows the fleet policy&#39;s fee and what they would keep in their slowest month.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b>: <b class="gd-ui">Earnings calculator on List your car: the monthly insurance fee shown</b> and <b class="gd-ui">the monthly tracker fee shown</b>, in dollars a month.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Leave either one empty and the page says &quot;Insurance and tracker fees: quoted in your agreement&quot; and shows the earnings &quot;before fees&quot;. No amount is ever made up.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Set both and the page takes them off every month and the year. Each owner&#39;s real fees stay the ones in their agreement.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Earnings calculator on List your car: the rented days of an average month it starts from</b> (12): keep it low, a new car takes months to fill.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">The percent that comes off the listed daily rate on a rented day</b> (15).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">The factor of each month</b> (jan to dec) against an average month (1.00): by default June 1.10, July and August 1.30, December 0.85, January and February 0.75, May and September 0.85, March and October 0.70, April and November 0.65. Every month must be there.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-agreements-who-still-needs-to-sign" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Agreements: who still needs to sign</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Owners and partners</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Owners</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Agreements</b>. Every owner with the agreements their deal needs, and where each one stands.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each owner shows their deal (revenue split, flat monthly or fleet lease) and one line per agreement: the Vehicle Enrollment Agreement, the Flat-Rate Vehicle Enrollment Agreement or the Fleet Supplier Lease Agreement, the Title-Holding and Lease Agreement, an Additional Vehicle Schedule for a car added later, the Partner agreement, and a Referral Override Agreement for each owner they referred.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Each line says <b class="gd-ui">Signed</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Sent, not signed</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Not sent</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Missing</b>. Missing means there is nothing to sign yet: set the terms of a car first, and the agreement is made from them.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Send</b> (or <b class="gd-ui">Send again</b>). The owner gets one email with the link to read and sign in their portal. An owner with no sign-in yet shows &quot;invite first&quot;: press Invite on the Owners list.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Owners whose agreements are all signed are hidden; press Show every owner to see them. The same lines are at the top of each owner&#39;s Terms tab.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>&quot;Awaiting lawyer OK&quot; marks the Referral Override Agreement until the lawyer approves its text (Program settings). The Fleet Supplier Lease Agreement is approved. Owners can sign either way.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-a-fleet-supplier-the-fleet-lease" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A fleet supplier: the fleet lease</h2><p class="gd-p">For a supplier&#39;s corporation that leases many cars to CarmaCars. Open the owner, <b class="gd-ui">Terms</b> tab, <b class="gd-ui">Fleet lease</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A supplier who signs up on the website as a fleet supplier (or whom staff add on the fleet supplier route) gets the default lease terms of Program settings and the default Upkeep Table at once: the card shows <b class="gd-ui">Fleet supplier route</b>. To agree other numbers, press <b class="gd-ui">Change the lease terms</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">A supplier on file without the route: press <b class="gd-ui">Enter the lease terms</b> and type what you agreed: the Regular Rate and the Troubled Rate (the lease a month for each car of that tier), the Claim Profit Share, the Early Write-Off Share, the Write-Off Period in months, the Later Write-Off Share and the Notice Period in days.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Check the <b class="gd-ui">Upkeep Table</b>: for each cost (engine, transmission, shocks, rustproofing, refurbishment, tires, brakes, oil changes, ball joints) the supplier or CarmaCars.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Add each car with <b class="gd-ui">Add another car</b> on the owner&#39;s page. The <b class="gd-ui">Fleet lease</b> step asks for the tier (Regular or Troubled) and the delivery date: the tier is required and set once. No fee or invoice step: the supplier pays CarmaCars nothing, and no owner invoice or debit is ever made for these cars.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">A car already on file: press <b class="gd-ui">Put on the lease</b> beside it, with the delivery date and the tier.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">The tier never changes. Typed the wrong one? Only an Admin can press <b class="gd-ui">Correct the tier</b>, with what was entered by mistake. It is corrected from the delivery (or from the day after the last approved statement) and kept in the audit log.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">The lease is paid in arrears on the 10th with the owner payouts: a car&#39;s first payment is on the first 10th at least one full month after its delivery and covers every month up to then. Part months are paid by the day; the statement line shows the calculation (rate, days, total).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">8</span><div class="gd-t">A claim on a leased car: settling it pays the supplier its Claim Profit Share of any profit, on its next statement. A write-off pays any lien first, then the supplier&#39;s Early or Later Write-Off Share of the balance by the months in service.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">9</span><div class="gd-t">An upkeep cost: <b class="gd-ui">Record an upkeep cost</b>. A cost the Upkeep Table gives the supplier comes off its next lease payment; one CarmaCars pays is not billed.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>New lease terms after the supplier signed wait for the supplier to sign the new agreement (it opens for signature at once). The cars keep the signed rates until then.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owners-and-onboarding-approve-a-fleet-supplier-s-cars" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Approve a fleet supplier&#39;s cars</h2><p class="gd-p">A supplier who signed up on the website: his application is in <b class="gd-ui">Applications</b> like any other, with each car&#39;s VIN, plate and the tier he chose.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open the application. Check the ownership copy of each car (he uploads it in his portal), the tier and who the car is registered to now. Its ServiceOntario forms were filled in when he added it: the lease (SR-LV-006 with his corporation as the registrant, SR-LV-012 with CarmaCars holding the plates) and, for a car not yet in his corporation, the transfer (ON00453 when the corporation has no RIN; 013-0169 and 013-1155 when an officer moves his own car in). A form still missing a value (a RIN, the odometer) shows what is missing, as on the other routes.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">A tier chosen by mistake: open the owner, <b class="gd-ui">Terms</b> tab, <b class="gd-ui">Fleet lease</b>, and press <b class="gd-ui">Correct the tier</b> beside the car, with what was chosen by mistake. Only an Admin can, and only before approval; it is kept in the audit log.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Approve: there are no terms or invoices to set. Check <b class="gd-ui">Delivered on</b> (the lease starts that day) and press <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b>. Each car goes on the lease at its tier.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">He signs in the owner portal only: the Fleet Supplier Lease Agreement and the Title-Holding and Lease Agreement, and Form B on screen, with the full e-signature and its audit trail. Paper signatures cannot be recorded for him. Form D is in his packet and signed on screen with two witnesses; Form C is not asked.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>The Fleet Supplier Lease Agreement is final: the lawyer approved it, so it no longer shows &quot;Awaiting lawyer OK&quot;. The default lease terms are in <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> (Fleet supplier route); a change there applies to suppliers who sign up later.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Owners &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Add an owner</b> offers the same route: choose <b class="gd-ui">A corporation</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Fleet supplier: leases the cars to CarmaCars</b>. So does <b class="gd-ui">Add a car for an owner</b> for a new owner.</div></aside></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'leads-and-sales-claims', 'chapter', 'text-alerts-email-text-or-both', 'Every lead in one place: people who are not renters or owners yet, from every source, with who is working on each one. Open **People** > **Renters** > **All leads**. An alert for a new lead (in the app, on the phone, or by email) opens that lead''s own page.

## What is in the list

- **Renter leads**: the contact form, live chat, the phone number box, discount game claims, offers that expired, booking requests typed and not sent, calls missed from a number with no booking (they arrive by themselves within 15 minutes), and Live visitors who turned Hot and left an email.
- **Owner leads**: owner program enquiries, owner applications started and not finished, owner form contacts and earnings calculator contacts. They are also under **People** > **Owners** > **Leads**, and each New owner program enquiry task opens its lead.
- **Partner leads**: fleet suppliers, dealers, rental businesses and insurers.

Each card shows the name, phone, email, the source in plain words (a live chat lead says Live chat), how old it is, and the start of what they wrote. New and hot leads come first. Open a lead for everything they wrote, the live chat transcript, their calls, every contact logged and the claim history.

## Work a lead

1. Press **Claim** on a card, or **Next lead** for the oldest hot lead nobody holds. It is yours for 15 minutes; nobody else can work on it meanwhile.
2. Press **Call**, **Text** or **Email**. Your phone or mail app opens and the contact is logged on the lead. Each call, text, email or **Note** adds another 15 minutes to your claim, up to 60 minutes from when you claimed it.
3. Press **Outcome** and choose Contacted, Call booked, Applied, Won (with the booking number when there is one) or Lost (say why). Won and lost close the lead.
4. Nothing more to do? Press **Mark handled**. Done with it for now? Press **Unclaim**: it goes back to the pool at once.

A claim that runs out returns the lead to the pool for everyone. One person holds at most 25 leads at a time. When a renter lead''s person books and the booking is confirmed, the lead closes as Won by itself, for the Sales person on the booking.

## As an Admin

- **Reassign** gives a lead to a person (their claim, and the lead is assigned to them). **Release** ends someone''s claim.
- **Sales team** shows each person''s leads claimed, won, close rate (won out of claimed), contacted, time to first contact and claims that ran out, today, this week or this month, best first.
- **Settings** > **Sales** sets how long a claim holds for renter, owner and partner leads (10 to 15 minutes suggested), the most a claim can be extended to, how many leads one person may hold, and how long a lead counts as hot.

> Good to know: Filters narrow the list by type, source, status, age, person and your own leads; the search finds a name, phone number, email or words they wrote.

## Rebooking, intent and leads (release 35)

- A returning renter''s new request goes straight to the salesperson of their last booking, with the usual claim time.
- Every renter and lead has an intent score (hot, warm or cold) with what they said they want: budget, car class, length, dates, urgency, delivery and coverage, read from calls (with their transcripts), texts, emails, the site chat and their visits.
- Leads are never given out by themselves: onboarded Sales claim them, one every 5 minutes, up to 3 open at once plus one for every 5 won in the last 30 days (at most 10).

## Leads handled on a call by customer service or Fleet (release 37)

A lead that customer service or Fleet handle on a call (they answer or place the call, add a note, or create the lead from the call) is held for them for **Customer service and Fleet: a lead they handle on a call is held for** minutes in **Settings** > **Sales** (empty: the Sales claim minutes of its type). Each new handled call adds the time. Sales see **Being handled by** and cannot work it; **Next lead** skips it. **Release hold** on the lead ends it at once; it returns to the salesperson who had a claim on it or brought it, else the open list. Your own reassign also ends it. A booking made from the lead keeps the usual credit; the hold is not a claim, so customer service is never credited. Every step is in the lead''s history (hold, another call handled, hold ended).

## The person behind the lead, and assigning leads in bulk (release 40)

**The person.** Open a lead, or press **The person** on its card, to see everything we know about whoever sent it, matched by their renter record, email and phone: their name and the name they go by, phone and email, whether they have an account and whether their licence is verified (yes or no; the number is never shown), every booking (car, dates, status, total and any open balance), what they owe and their deposit, open requests and offers sent, their earlier leads, their messages, calls and texts, notes, reviews, incidents and claims, and who has handled them (Helped by, and who claimed, held or was assigned their leads).

**Signals.** The intent score and the **Signals** timeline are for the whole person, not one lead: calls (in, out, missed, with their length), texts both ways, WhatsApp, Messenger and Instagram messages, the site chat, emails they wrote, links they opened in our emails, visits and cars looked at, offers, quotes and payment pages opened, bookings, rentals, cancellations and reviews. Newest first.

**Assign in bulk.** On **Leads**, tick cards (or **Select all on this page**), or choose **Everything the filter matches** to take every open lead the filters show (status, type, source, age, person, words). Choose a Sales person in **Assign to**, or **Return to the pool**, and press **Assign**: you see how many leads match and confirm first. **Assign every unassigned lead older than today** takes every open lead nobody has (no person, no claim, no hold) that came in before today, after the same confirm. Up to 500 leads go per press; when more match, it says how many are left: press again.

- Only active, fully onboarded Sales staff can be chosen. Customer service, Fleet and Finance take no sales credit, so they are not in the list.
- A bulk assignment is your assignment, not a claim: it does not run out, nobody else can claim the lead, and **Next lead** skips it for everyone else. The person''s claims on their assigned leads do not count against their limits.
- A customer service or Fleet call can still hold the lead while they handle it; when the hold ends, the lead goes back to the assigned person.
- **Reassign** on one lead still gives a timed claim, as before. **Return to the pool** ends the assignment and any claim.
- Every lead moved shows **Assigned by an Admin to** in its history, and each press is one entry in the audit log.

## Requests that did not go through (release 42)

When a customer presses **Send request** and the request is refused or fails, nothing is lost. The form keeps everything they typed, tells them the exact reason beside the field to change, and Sales gets a To-do.

1. On **All leads** you see **Requests that did not go through** with a count, when there is one. Open it for the reasons and the people: name, email, phone, the car, the dates, the reason they were shown, how many times they tried and when.
2. Each person is listed once per car and day, however many times they tried. The newest reason is shown.
3. Sales has a **Request did not go through** To-do for each one, with the same details. Call or text the person and help them finish, or make the offer yourself with **New quote**.
4. When that person''s request goes through, they leave the list and the To-do closes by itself.

The reasons a customer can see, and what each asks them to change:

- **Dates**: the pickup is too soon, the return is before the pickup, the booking is longer than one booking covers, or the car is taken or leaves the fleet first.
- **Car**: the car cannot be booked online right now.
- **Place**: a delivery address or an airport is missing, or the car is not handed over at its owner''s location.
- **Driver**: the email, the phone, the date of birth or the age for this car, the licence class, or an additional driver''s details.
- **Coverage**: no card picked, a card that does not cover this car, or a box not ticked.
- **Limits**: 3 requests already open for that person, or more than 30 requests in an hour from one internet connection.
- **Our system could not take the request**: the customer is told we kept the request and will contact them. The To-do is urgent and shows what the system said. Tell the developer if you see the same one twice.

> Good to know: An add-on that cannot be added online never stops a request. The request arrives without the add-ons and its note starts with "Add-ons asked for, not added online": confirm them with the renter in the offer.

## Show a lead''s phone to a salesperson (release 46)

Sales see customer numbers with most digits hidden. To give one salesperson the full number of one lead:

1. On the lead (its page, its card, or its row under Expired offers on the Leads tab of Renters), press **Show the phone to** and the salesperson''s name: the lead''s salesperson, or the person holding its claim. On the lead''s page you can choose another Sales person and type a reason.
2. That person gets an alert that opens the lead, and now sees the full number on that lead only, with a call link and **Copy**. Every other lead stays hidden for them, except the same number where it belongs to the same person (their renter record or another lead with that phone), and nobody else gets it.
3. **Hide it again** beside their name hides it. Reassigning the lead hides it by itself: the new salesperson sees it only once you show it to them.
4. A salesperson can press **Ask an Admin to show the number**: you get a To do on the lead with **Show the phone**, which shows it to the one who asked and closes the To do.

> Good to know: each show and hide is in the audit log with who, when, for whom and the reason.', 'Leads and Sales claims', 'Every lead in one place, claims, outcomes and the Sales team''s numbers.',
  'Every lead in one place: people who are not renters or owners yet, from every source, with who is working on each one. Open **People** > **Renters** > **All leads**. An alert for a new lead (in the app, on the phone, or by email) opens that lead''s own page.

## What is in the list

- **Renter leads**: the contact form, live chat, the phone number box, discount game claims, offers that expired, booking requests typed and not sent, calls missed from a number with no booking (they arrive by themselves within 15 minutes), and Live visitors who turned Hot and left an email.
- **Owner leads**: owner program enquiries, owner applications started and not finished, owner form contacts and earnings calculator contacts. They are also under **People** > **Owners** > **Leads**, and each New owner program enquiry task opens its lead.
- **Partner leads**: fleet suppliers, dealers, rental businesses and insurers.

Each card shows the name, phone, email, the source in plain words (a live chat lead says Live chat), how old it is, and the start of what they wrote. New and hot leads come first. Open a lead for everything they wrote, the live chat transcript, their calls, every contact logged and the claim history.

## Work a lead

1. Press **Claim** on a card, or **Next lead** for the oldest hot lead nobody holds. It is yours for 15 minutes; nobody else can work on it meanwhile.
2. Press **Call**, **Text** or **Email**. Your phone or mail app opens and the contact is logged on the lead. Each call, text, email or **Note** adds another 15 minutes to your claim, up to 60 minutes from when you claimed it.
3. Press **Outcome** and choose Contacted, Call booked, Applied, Won (with the booking number when there is one) or Lost (say why). Won and lost close the lead.
4. Nothing more to do? Press **Mark handled**. Done with it for now? Press **Unclaim**: it goes back to the pool at once.

A claim that runs out returns the lead to the pool for everyone. One person holds at most 25 leads at a time. When a renter lead''s person books and the booking is confirmed, the lead closes as Won by itself, for the Sales person on the booking.

