 (car hire), sale (financing), detailing (ceramic coating) and body shop (bumper repair), at carmacars.ca/t/term/...</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Pages: how many pages each level and each tier has, the total, and how many are in search. Every page is in search by default; nothing needs setting up.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">One switch per tier takes it out of search at once: <b class="gd-ui">Index the place pages</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Index the colour pages</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Index the search term pages</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Index the /buy pages</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Index the detailing pages</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Index the body shop pages</b>. Off, those pages stay visible but leave the sitemaps and search.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The places are the place list of the local search release (every city, town and neighbourhood, with GTA and country levels); until it is filled, the area landing pages. The search terms are edited with them.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Oldest model year with vehicle pages</b> (2005): cars from that year on. An older model year has no page in any tree (it answers not found) and is in no sitemap or list of years; a model with only older years has no page either.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Financing disclaimer</b>: the text on financing and leasing pages. CarmaCars never says it lends or leases.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Database: its size against the cap the catalog and places imports keep under: the cap of the Database plan (Pro, 6,144 MB, by default; Free, 450 MB). IndexNow: the addresses sent today, where the sweep is, and any back-off; nothing to do.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">Each page is built from data: the EPA fuel-use ratings in litres per 100 km, the cost to drive 100 km at the gas or electricity price set here, what changed from the year before, how a trim differs from the others, similar models, and the rental questions from the program settings.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">8</span><div class="gd-t">Below the facts: our cars of that exact year, model and trim, then the same model in other years, then similar cars free now, and Request it, which sends an enquiry to People &gt; Renters, the Leads tab.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">9</span><div class="gd-t">Settings: every page is in search; the switch per tier above is the only way to take a tier out.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">10</span><div class="gd-t">Canadian trims: open a model and type one line per run of years, entry trim first: 2020-2021: Comfortline, Highline, Sportline, Execline. Your lines are kept by every import; empty them to go back to the CarmaCars list. <b class="gd-ui">Add trims for another model</b> adds a model that has none.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">11</span><div class="gd-t">Catalog import: the last import and its counts. <b class="gd-ui">Import now</b> asks for a new one; it runs at the next daily check, at 07:17 UTC.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A car joins its pages by itself once it is on the site: its make, model, year and trim are read from the car. A trim that names several (S / SE / R-Line) leaves the car on the year page only; set the car&#39;s trim to one Canadian name to put it on the trim page.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides-stock-photos-on-the-vehicle-pages" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Stock photos on the vehicle pages</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Vehicle pages</b>, card Stock photos. The vehicle pages show a real photo of the make, model and generation at the top (a 2015 Camry page shows a Camry of the 2012 to 2017 generation), with the credit always under it: &quot;Photo: author, licence, Wikimedia Commons&quot;. The place pages and the detailing and body shop pages show a photo of a road, a car being detailed or a body shop. Our own cars always show their own photos.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Nothing to set up: the photos come by themselves every day, our fleet&#39;s models and the popular models first. Only free licences are used (public domain, CC0, CC BY, CC BY-SA), from Wikimedia Commons, or Openverse when Commons has none. A year without a photo of its own generation shows the nearest photo of the model, marked &quot;not the exact year&quot;; a model with no photo keeps the studio drawing.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The card shows how many models and model years have a photo, the popular models still without one, and the last run.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Open a make to see its photos. A wrong car, a poor photo or a photo you do not want: press <b class="gd-ui">Hide</b>. The page goes back to the studio drawing at once, and that photo is never picked again.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Pick again</b> asks for the next best photo; <b class="gd-ui">Replace</b> takes a photo you found on Wikimedia Commons: paste its address (https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:...). Either is done at the next daily run, after its licence is checked. A photo whose licence is not allowed is refused, with the reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Show stock photos</b> in the settings above turns every stock photo off at once (on by default).</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Never upload or use a photo from Google, a dealer or a manufacturer&#39;s site here: only Wikimedia Commons files, with the credit the page shows.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides-a-car-for-sale" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A car for sale</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Vehicles</b>, then the car. On the For sale card, tick <b class="gd-ui">For sale</b>, enter the Asking price and press <b class="gd-ui">Save</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The car then shows at the top of its /buy pages (its make, model, year and trim) with the asking price, the only time a page says a car is for sale.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Untick it when the car is sold or no longer for sale: the pages say so at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">&quot;Find me this car&quot; on the /buy pages sends a buyer lead to Sales (staff portal: <b class="gd-ui">Owner leads</b>, Buyer leads), with a To do line.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides-search-engines-and-business-listings" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Search engines and business listings</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, then Site settings.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Search engines: paste the Google Search Console value (HTML tag) or the file name (HTML file), and the Bing value. The steps are on the card.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Business name, address and phone: the exact text for every listing, and the description and categories.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Business listings: press <b class="gd-ui">Copy</b> beside each line and paste it into Google Business Profile, Bing Places, Apple Business Connect, Yelp, Yellow Pages and Facebook. Tick each one when it is done.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Changed pages are sent to IndexNow (Bing and the other engines that use it) by themselves. Google reads the sitemap: submit carmacars.ca/sitemap.xml once in Search Console.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides-place-pages" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Place pages</h2><p class="gd-p">Every place we have, from a country down to a neighbourhood, gets a page for every term people search with: renting (car hire, SUV rental, monthly car rental ...), buying help (used cars, car financing ...), detailing (ceramic coating, window tint ...) and body work (collision repair, dent repair ...). Each page is written from real data only: the distance from us, the delivery price within our reach, the nearest airport, the landmarks near it, our live cars and the places around it. A place far from Toronto says we serve the Toronto area and takes a request instead. <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, then Search.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Place pages: four switches, one for each family, put the pages in search and in the sitemaps. All four are on.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Every place page is in search and filled with its own data; there is no quality gate.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Delivery reach: places within this distance of our location are offered delivery. Database size cap: the places import stops before the database passes it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Regions and places: Ontario is on, every city, town and neighbourhood in it; every other province, state and territory is off (kept, not deleted): its place pages answer not found and are in no sitemap. Tick a region to put its pages back.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Terms and services: change a term&#39;s title or what is true about it, point a synonym to another term, switch a term off, or add one. Give a service a starting price, or leave it empty for &quot;price on request&quot;.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">One page per service: terms people search with the same meaning are one group (car hire, cars for hire and vehicle rental are car rental; auto body repair is collision repair; auto detailing is car detailing). A synonym&#39;s pages, by place and by car, send the visitor to its group&#39;s page, which lists them (&quot;Also searched as: ...&quot;); only the group&#39;s pages are in the sitemaps. Different services keep their own pages: interior and exterior detailing, ceramic coating, window tint, PPF, financing, leasing, lease takeover, insurance replacement rental and each mechanical service.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A region has pages once the places workflow has loaded it: GitHub, Actions, places, Run workflow, with the regions or all. The run loads Ontario first and names any region it skipped because of the size cap.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides-alternative-searches" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Alternative searches</h2><p class="gd-p">People also search for an alternative to another service. Turo alternative, RideAlike alternative and Luup alternative for rideshare drivers have their place pages like every way of renting (&quot;Turo Alternative in Mississauga&quot;), in the sitemaps. Each page says plainly that CarmaCars is not affiliated with the company named and says nothing about that company. Nothing to set up.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides-requests-from-the-place-pages" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Requests from the place pages</h2><p class="gd-p">The buying help, detailing and body shop pages, and the pages of places beyond our reach, have a request form. Each request is a lead with a task in <b class="gd-ui">To do</b>: detailing and body shop requests are due within an hour of opening and show in Today. Buying help pages offer to rent the model first and help find the car; the notice at the top is set under Place pages.</p><p class="gd-p">Mechanical work has pages too, under the body shop pages and listed apart as &quot;Auto services we arrange&quot;: a mechanic, oil changes, brakes, tires and winter tires, towing, batteries and boosts, alignment, transmission and engine repair, diagnostics, inspections and the Ontario safety certificate, emissions, AC, exhaust and suspension. The pages say a trusted shop does the work, which CarmaCars arranges: each takes a request (a &quot;Mechanical work to arrange&quot; task, due within an hour of opening) and offers a rental while the car is in. They have no questions of their own; their per car pages (for each make, model, year and trim) say the same and take the same request.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides-one-name-address-and-phone" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">One name, address and phone</h2><p class="gd-p">The footer, the contact page, the structured data and every business listing show the business address of Site settings. Keep it the address renters come to, and change it there only.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides-what-search-engines-may-read" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">What search engines may read</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Vehicle pages</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Search scope</b> says what search engines are invited to read:</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">Full (every page)</b>, the default: every vehicle, place, colour, search term and for-sale page is in the sitemaps and open to crawlers. It costs more of the website&#39;s CPU time as crawlers read them.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Core (about 23,000 pages)</b>: the fixed pages, the fleet&#39;s cars, the landing pages, the guides and the vehicle pages down to the trim. The other pages stay up for people, but robots.txt keeps crawlers out and they are in no sitemap.</li></ul><p class="gd-p">The change takes effect within minutes, with no deploy. In either scope, from 70% of the month&#39;s included CPU time crawlers get no catalog page at all (&quot;try again tomorrow&quot;) until the month resets. People always get every page.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides-indexnow" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">IndexNow</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Search</b>, Today shows IndexNow in two lines. Changed pages: a car, a landing page or a guide that changed, sent first and on their own, 100 at a time; a refusal waits an hour, then longer, and a server error 10 minutes, doubling up to 6 hours. Sweep: the priority list once a week, 1,000 addresses a request (Program settings); a refusal from Bing waits until the next day, a day longer for each refusal in a row, and a server error 10 minutes, doubling up to 6 hours, then the sweep goes on from where it was.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">Index coverage</h3><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Index coverage (Search Console sample)</b> shows, by day, how many of the addresses the gsc workflow inspected Google knows, how many of those are indexed (the share Search Console itself counts), the priority pages indexed, the crawled and discovered but not indexed, and apart the addresses still unknown to Google (most of the long tail). A car page is sent to IndexNow again whenever its copy, prices or photos change, and each place page now names its drive time, the landmarks and places near it and the real cars with their prices.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">Longer pages from real data</h3><p class="gd-p">Every place page, landing page, car page and vehicle page has sections written from its own data: the cars and their daily, weekly and 30-day prices and deposits (or the nearest similar cars when none match), the delivery fee, the distance and drive time from us, the nearest airport and GO station, the highways and the 407 ETR&#39;s tolls, the city&#39;s parking rule, the age, licence, coverage and deposit rules, the fee schedule, the car&#39;s figures and the cost to drive 100 km, and questions answered from those facts. Nothing to set up: the stops, hotels and specs come from the seo-data workflow every week, each with its source shown on the page.</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>After a release that changes these pages, press Validate fix in Search Console on &quot;Crawled - currently not indexed&quot; (Indexing &gt; Pages). Google has no way to press it for you.</div></aside><h3 class="gd-h3">Release 36: more pages, more data, every page positive</h3><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">Positive pages</b>: a search page never says what we lack. A page whose own list is empty shows the cars ready to book now and <b class="gd-ui">Request this exact car</b>; the checks refuse copy that says &quot;not available&quot;, &quot;we don&#39;t have&quot; or &quot;we don&#39;t offer&quot;.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Popular cars</b>: a car with more than its share of the requests (Program settings, Demand steering: 25% by default) is placed lower in Trending (no higher than 6th), its page says <b class="gd-ui">Popular</b> with similar cars first, and the search pages list it after the others. A pin still leads.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Car figures</b>: every car and vehicle page shows what the free sources give, each with its source: the manufacturer&#39;s price, production years and plants (Wikidata), dimensions (NHTSA vPIC, Canada), recall campaigns (NHTSA and Transport Canada), the parts owners complain about most (NHTSA), charging, equipment, and ratings out of 10 with how each is worked out (fuel economy, performance, space, crash safety, recall record, parkability). The seo-data workflow loads them weekly; a curated CSV adds the manufacturer&#39;s colours, prices and equipment.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Parking</b>: place, event and airport pages list the parking lots, garages and streets with parking nearby (OpenStreetMap).</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Events</b>: <b class="gd-ui">Marketing</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Event pages</b> lists the Toronto and GTA events with a &quot;Rent a car for&quot; page. Add an event, or set its dates once the organiser announces them; until then the page says the months it is usually held. Sales sees the same list on its Marketing page.</li><li>Pages for Turo searches: five landing pages for people searching Turo cancellations, deposits, fees, damage and missed handovers. They describe our own process and say CarmaCars is not affiliated with Turo.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">GPS tracker</b>: its page (/gps-tracker) and a short section on the search pages, from Program settings (name, prices, features, details; off hides both).</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Airports</b>: a page for Pearson and Billy Bishop: the car delivered to the terminal at the standard delivery price.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Renting vs owning</b>: a page per popular model year (and the nearest cities) with the monthly cost of owning, line by line with sources, against our monthly rate. The financing rate and term, kilometres, depreciation and cleaning are Program settings; insurance and parking figures are added with their source.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Languages</b>: the landing, event and airport pages in 18 languages (French, Punjabi, Mandarin, Cantonese, Arabic, Urdu, Tagalog, Spanish, Portuguese, Italian, Tamil, Farsi, Korean, Russian, Hindi, Gujarati, Vietnamese, Polish) at carmacars.ca/fr/... The seo-i18n workflow translates the templates once; a language is in search and named to Google only once 90% of its text is translated (Program settings).</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Reviews</b>: real reviews show on every car page and search page with their source. <b class="gd-ui">Reviews</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Add a customer review</b> enters one that came another way (Turo, an earlier platform, a text, a call, email, in person, Google): the first name and last initial, the source, the date, the rating, the customer&#39;s words exactly as received, and a screenshot if you have one. Never write or change a review for a customer. Hide one only for cause.</li><li>Sitemaps: two more files, the new page families and the language versions (with each page&#39;s languages), each with its own dates.</li></ul><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>The Cantonese pages are translated by a person (the translation model has no Cantonese): until then they stay out of search.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides-search-footprint-and-the-clicks-goal-releases-35-and-36" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Search footprint and the clicks goal (releases 35 and 36)</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>The search pages are in 18 languages spoken across the GTA, with page families for places, landing needs, cars and models, events, airports, comparisons with other rental companies and renting vs owning.</li><li>Real reviews show on every car and search page, each with where it was received. Staff add a review that came by text, call, email or another platform exactly as received, with a screenshot.</li><li>The SEO page in the Admin portal follows Search Console: clicks and impressions by week, pages indexed, and the progress to the goal of 5 million clicks, with the page families that bring the most.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides-the-tracker-pages-every-service-on-every-page-and-the-new-pa" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The tracker pages, every service on every page, and the new page design (release 48)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">The GPS tracker and kill switch</b> has its own pages now:</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li><span class="gd-url">/trackers</span>: the product page, with the price by number of cars, what it does, a comparison table, questions and the form. <span class="gd-url">/gps-tracker</span> sends people there.</li><li><span class="gd-url">/trackers/kill-switch-for-car</span>, <span class="gd-url">starter-interrupt-device</span>, <span class="gd-url">gps-tracker-for-rental-car</span>, <span class="gd-url">anti-theft-tracker-toronto</span>, <span class="gd-url">fleet-tracking</span>, <span class="gd-url">turo-host-gps-tracker</span> and <span class="gd-url">toll-and-ticket-billing</span>: one page for each way people search.</li><li><span class="gd-url">/trackers/install</span> and <span class="gd-url">/trackers/install/</span> followed by the place: &quot;tracker install near me&quot;, one page per Ontario place, with the same gate as the place pages.</li></ul><p class="gd-p">Every price on those pages comes from <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> (the tracker tiers and the install price). While &quot;Trackers can be installed&quot; is off, every page says <b class="gd-ui">Join the waitlist</b> with the words of &quot;GPS tracker product: the words beside Join the waitlist&quot; (&quot;Shipping soon&quot;) and never says a tracker is in stock. Turn &quot;Trackers can be installed&quot; on when trackers can be installed: the same pages then take orders.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Someone joins the waitlist or pre-orders: a lead appears in <b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Renters</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">All leads</b> with the source &quot;GPS tracker waitlist&quot; or &quot;GPS tracker pre-order&quot;, the number of cars and the price quoted, with its To do and the usual new-lead alert.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The person gets the email &quot;You are on the waitlist&quot; with their price. Nothing is charged.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Every service on every page.</b> Each search page (landing pages, place pages, vehicle pages, the car page, events, airports) ends with the module <b class="gd-ui">More from CarmaCars</b>: the tracker, List your car, chauffeur, delivery, coverage, monthly rentals, insurance replacement, rideshare, young drivers and the add-ons, each with its price when the database has one. <span class="gd-url">/services</span> lists every service with its pages.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">New landing pages</b>, edited like the others in <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Search</b>: <span class="gd-url">rideshare</span>, <span class="gd-url">g2-licence</span>, <span class="gd-url">with-a-charger</span>, <span class="gd-url">with-flowers</span> and <span class="gd-url">with-child-seat</span>. The add-on pages show the add-on&#39;s own price card from <b class="gd-ui">Add-ons</b>, so change the price there, never in the copy.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">The page design.</b> Long pages are built from blocks: the short answer, the cars, price cards, the copy and the detail as folds (tap a heading to open it), questions, and on a phone a bar at the bottom with one button. The text is all still in the page for search engines.</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>a visitor who follows a Google, Bing, ChatGPT or Perplexity result to a place or vehicle page now gets the page at once. Before, a first visit could show &quot;One moment, loading the page&quot; for a second.</div></aside></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'settings', 'chapter', 'search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides', 'Settings change the public site and the rules of the program at once. Program settings are kept as dated rows, so earlier values stay on record.

## The Settings page

1. Site setup lists what is still missing on the public site, with **Open site settings**.
2. Site settings: contact details, hours, tagline, logo, socials, Google place id and featured cars.
3. Program settings: every timing and policy value.
4. Forms: Blind Spot''s rental agreement for every booking, and the official ServiceOntario PDFs and what goes in each field.
5. Insurers: insurance companies billed for bookings.

![](/guides/img/admin-24-settings-desktop-89b31691.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 900; address: carmacars.ca/admin/settings; pins: 1 32.6 33.0, 2 25.8 40.2, 3 77.4 40.2, 4 25.8 73.2, 5 25.8 84.9")

The other tiles: Site content (headings, FAQs, legal text), Fee defaults, Deposit tiers, Kilometre choices, Vehicle classes, Vehicle class rules, Airports and delivery, Protection Plan prices, Card coverage, Reviews, Quo contacts (everyone with a phone number as a contact in Quo: see Texts and calls), Text alerts, Partners (each partner company''s CRM link: see Partners, company cars and rentals added by hand), Email aliases and reply-to, My profile, Staff and roles, Promo codes, Quick replies and Call helper.

**My profile**: the greeting name of this login. To do greets it whole ("Good morning, Abbas and Mahad" on a login the owners share) and the assistant uses it; empty, the first name of the account. Press **Change the greeting name**, type it and save.

## Program settings

1. Buffer between trips (90 minutes): the time held before and after every trip, in every availability and conflict check (requests, offers, date changes, extensions, the calendar). The cleaning block after a trip is this time; Turnaround between trips is the same number. A booking already closer than this is not changed: the calendar rings it.
1. Late fee and extensions (Booking requests and offers): the late fee per started hour (17.5% of the daily rate, at least $25; new bookings and offers only), the extension discounts (no longer applied since release 35: an extension costs the booking''s all-in price a day) and **Approve a renter''s extension at once when nothing needs a person** (on). A car''s own switch is in Fleet, the car, **Edit details**: **Renters extend themselves**.
1. RentalCover (the Protection Plan): whether quotes price the plan once the key is set (on), the markup (on, 20%, no fixed amount), how long a quote is reused, the car value limit ($50,000) and whether a car with no value may have the plan (off).
2. Settings come in groups such as Company, Booking requests and offers, Owner debits and statement emails, Deposits, Delivery, Owners and fleet, and Tolls and damage. Open one to see its fields.
3. First reply target for customer service and sales (minutes), under Booking requests and offers: 5 by default. New booking requests, enquiries, changes renters ask for and renter messages are due that many minutes after they come in; the scorecard and the staff screens use it. What renters are told (Reply wording, in Site settings) is separate.
4. Staff commissions and prices typed by hand: the commission outside Sales (10%, field staff only: customer service, Fleet and Finance earn none), the three Sales tiers and their days (10%, 15% from 50 days, 20% from 100 days, the month''s target), the price floor a day (empty: none) and the discount from the rate sheet that flags a price (20%). The owner confirmed these values in October 2026. The remote Sales values follow: the three remote tiers (5%, 10%, 15%), the touches a month (400), the drop under it (one tier) and its floor (2.5%), the peak hours a week (20), the reply target (15 minutes) and the peak hours (noon to 6 pm, Thursday to Sunday).
5. Staff agreement defaults by function, at the bottom: pay (a month, an hour or commission only), the rate, the schedule (full time, part time or flexible), days a week and hours a day for Customer service, Fleet, Finance and Sales, the values every assistant shares, and the field staff wage. Sales is commission only: no rate and a flexible schedule. Press **Save the defaults**.
6. Live visitors and live chat: recording visits, the signal thresholds, follow-up tasks, the chat and its assistant, and how long visits and chats are kept.
7. Discount games: the same values as Settings, Discount games (the prize table and the games are easier to change there).
8. Deposits: the toll and ticket window after the return (7 days: settling sooner suggests a hold-back), the longest hold-back (30 days after the return), how long before a card hold lapses it is collected (36 hours), and collecting what is owed after the deposit by itself (the card on file, then a pay link, then a Finance task). A deposit is never released by itself.
9. Field jobs and handovers: field jobs made from each confirmed booking (on) and who gets them (the least busy field staff member, or nobody so Fleet assigns), how field staff may take a deposit at the check-in besides a card (e-Transfer and cash), and whether they may release a car whose tracker is not reporting, with a reason (on; you get an urgent task). Shifts published by themselves (on): the shift template (one shift of 10:00 to 17:00 for one person, every second day from November 23, 2026), how many days ahead (14) and the first day they may be published for; a handover or return no shift covers gets a shift of its own. Field pay: the first day of a pay period (every period is two weeks), the default hourly rate (CA$18.00), whether overtime is paid (off), after how many hours in a week (44) and at what share of the rate (150%), vacation pay added to each statement (off; Ontario 4%) and the longest shift (16 hours).
10. Sign-in by phone: codes by text from the CarmaCars number (on), US numbers (off until the Quo number is registered for US texting, A2P 10DLC), codes per number and per connection an hour, and whether a verified phone confirms an account like a confirmed email. Accepting an offer, signing and paying need a confirmed account; an account made by phone gives its email on the pay page before its first payment.
11. Calendar sync, Turo by email, Booking recovery emails and Site check: how often calendar links are read, the Turo inbound address and who may forward to it, the reminder delays and sending hours, and the site check with the address its alerts go to (rent@carmacars.ca), the minutes before an email, the daily limit and the quiet hours.
12. Change a value and press **Save**. It is saved as a new row from today; the rows before stay as they were.

