  '<p class="gd-p">Every function adds rentals that come in by phone, at the counter, from Turo, a partner, an insurer or someone you know. The rental is confirmed and on the calendar at once.</p><section class="gd-task" id="add-a-rental-by-hand-add-a-rental" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Add a rental</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Bookings</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Add a rental</b> button. Your home address must be in your profile first: until it is, the page asks for it.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">At pickup with the renter? Press <b class="gd-ui">Start at pickup</b>: the renter&#39;s name and phone, the car, the kilometres and the fuel, then <b class="gd-ui">Hold the car and finish later</b>. The car is held for 2 hours and you get a task to finish it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Nothing is required to save: the form is saved as a draft as you type (<b class="gd-ui">Save draft</b> saves at once). A line at the top of this page, <b class="gd-ui">You have an unfinished one</b>, opens your own draft where it was left, on any device. Sales (and Admins) also have <b class="gd-ui">Unfinished rentals</b>, everyone&#39;s, on Today and on Bookings. Tick Hold the car while I finish to keep the car off the calendar while you type.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Choose the car, the dates and the places. The check shows any clash with another booking or with the cleaning time after a trip. You cannot book over a clash: ask an Admin.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The dates decide the case, shown under them. Car already out with the renter? Enter the pickup as when it left: the rental is recorded as on trip, and anything still missing (signature, licence check, coverage proof, deposit) becomes a task. A rental that has already ended is recorded by an Admin.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Find the renter by name, email or phone, or add a new one with their name, email, phone, date of birth and licence. A renter on file shows their licence, home address and the drivers named before (<b class="gd-ui">Add them</b> puts those drivers on the rental), with an expired licence or an old address flagged. Add any other drivers.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">The calendar and the price are checked by themselves once the car and the dates are in. The price comes from the rate sheet. You may add the extras, how damage is covered and an allowed promo code.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">Quick start: <b class="gd-ui">Phone</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Walk-in</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Turo or another platform</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Insurance replacement</b> sets the usual choices.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">8</span><div class="gd-t">A car tagged Listing not finished can be rented too: it stays off the public site. If it has no rates yet, type the rental charge for the whole rental and the reason. An owner&#39;s car not yet on the fleet insurance policy is added by an Admin only.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">9</span><div class="gd-t">Every line of the price can be changed where it stands (customer service and sales, while Program settings allow it): the rental charge for the trip or a rate a day, the young driver fee, the Protection Plan, delivery, each add-on, the kilometres a day; add a fee from the list or a charge of its own. The (i) beside each line says what it is. The rate-sheet price stays on the booking; a price far under it is flagged for an Admin, never refused. Know what the renter paid with tax? Choose After tax (HST included) under Amounts I type and type those amounts (&quot;$270 after tax for the rental, $50 for the Protection Plan&quot;), or type the Total the renter pays (after tax): the rental charge is worked out so the total is exactly that. The total shown is the total saved.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">10</span><div class="gd-t">Any length: past 30 days the monthly rate applies for each 30 days, and the monthly periods are listed. Each later period gets its own agreement, sent to the renter to sign a few days before it starts (Monthly periods on the booking; Send the agreement for the next period now if needed).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">11</span><div class="gd-t">Choose how the rent is paid (e-Transfer or cash received, card on file, payment link, platform payout, insurer billed later; the ways open to you are set by an Admin; paid in parts: Add another payment) and then how the deposit is paid (card hold, cash or e-Transfer with its reference). Before you save sums it all up. The rental agreement is sent to the renter to sign online (never on paper). An insurance replacement with dates not known yet: untick Blocks the car&#39;s calendar and say why. Insurer billed later shows Charges to the insurer: type the rate a day of VLF, LDW, T&amp;LDW, PAP/PEC or Waiver Saver that the insurer authorized (empty: none); each is the rate times the days, plus HST, billed to the insurer.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">12</span><div class="gd-t">Under Who found this client, choose <b class="gd-ui">I sourced this client</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Entered for CarmaCars</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">13</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Add the rental</b>. The renter gets the confirmation email unless you tick <b class="gd-ui">Do not email the renter</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">14</span><div class="gd-t">A rental you add is credited to you and shows in My sales as a rental you added. If you sourced it, its commission shows there too.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>The renter signs the rental agreement in their portal before pickup. With the saved card, nothing is charged when you add the rental: the card is charged when the renter presses Accept and sign. At the counter, they sign on the phone with <b class="gd-ui">Sign now on this device</b>. A payment link keeps the booking waiting for payment.</div></aside></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('va', 'shared-tools', 'chapter', 'car-maintenance', 'Every function has the calendar and Find a renter. Use them to answer questions fast.

## Which cars are free (release 44)

At the top of **Calendar**: choose the **Pickup** and the **Return** the customer wants and you see every car at once.

1. Each car says **Available** (green edge) or **Not available** (red edge), available cars first. A car that is not available says why: Booked, On rent, Booked, payment due, Placeholder (held), Maintenance, Cleaning, Blocked, Out of service or Leaving the fleet, with the booking number and the dates. It also says the **Next free** start for the same length of rental.
2. An offer or a request out on a car does not hold it: it shows as a note, and the car stays Available until the booking is paid.
3. Narrow it with **Class**, **Seats at least** and **Price a day up to**, or tick **Available only**.
4. Customer service and Sales: press **Offer these dates** on an available car. Send an offer opens with the car and the dates filled in; add the customer and send.
5. No customer''s name or number is shown here. The answer is the same check the booking makes, so a car shown Available can be booked for those dates.

## The calendar

1. Every car with its photo, its bookings, requests and blocks, in the colours of the legend above it: on rent, confirmed, request, offer or hold, maintenance, block. The red line is now. Tap a bar for its details; on a phone it opens on the agenda, by day.
2. Use the arrows, Today and the range to move around, or search by plate, booking or name.
3. Fleet and customer service can remove a cleaning block from its side panel (**Remove the block**) when a car is ready sooner.

![](/guides/img/va-cs-09-calendar-desktop-541a6da5.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 800; address: carmacars.ca/va/calendar; pins: 1 60.2 33.8, 2 28.5 17.5")

## Find a car

**Bookings**, the **Find a car** tab. A renter quotes the car code on the car''s page (like CC-7F3A).

1. Type the car code, a plate, a VIN or the name. Each car shows its code, plate, status and its page on the site.
2. In Add a rental, type the car code or plate in the box above Car to choose it.

## Find a renter

1. Search by name, email, phone or booking number.
2. Opening a renter''s private details asks for a reason (**Open with a reason**). It is kept in the access log.
3. The renter''s record has **Add a note** and the **Activity** log: everything about the renter, newest first, with a chip per type (All by default), **Search the activity**, **Older** for the next 50, and **Email**, **Call** and **Text**. Fleet does not see payments in it.

![](/guides/img/va-cs-07-renters-desktop-99cfd0ef.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 240; address: carmacars.ca/va/renters; pins: 1 68.3 34.6")

## Email the renter

Customer service, Sales, Fleet and Finance can all write to the renter from a booking: press **Email the renter**, or open the **Messages & history** section.

The booking page, the car page and the listing review are the same pages an Admin opens. The car page has the Admin''s tabs your function uses: **Overview**, **Rates & fees** and **Maintenance** (Fleet), **Listing** and **Documents**; an old link to a car''s maintenance opens its Maintenance tab. You see the sections and buttons of your function: Finance has the money, the refunds and the deposit; Fleet the field jobs, the handovers and the car''s rates; customer service the review and offer, changes and extensions; Sales the requests and offers.

1. Write a **Subject** and a **Message**, or pick a **Quick reply** to start from.
2. Press **Email the renter**. It goes from CarmaCars and the renter can answer in their account; the answer opens a task for customer service.
3. On a booking an insurer pays you can choose Blind Spot Car Rental (insurance) as the sender, and **Email the adjuster** writes to the adjuster on the booking.

The form is under the booking''s Activity log (release 35), which lists the messages both ways, every email of the booking, the texts, chat, calls, notes and the rest, newest first, with a chip per type and a search. Each email counts against the daily email limit, shown under the form with today''s number.

### Find a booking
**Bookings**: type at least 3 characters of the booking number (CC-1042, 1042), the renter''s or a driver''s name, an email, a phone number, a plate or a car code, then press Enter. **My bookings** lists yours, with your commission. Every search is logged, as Find a renter.

## Phone alerts

Get an alert on your phone or computer for new requests, replies to answer and urgent problems, even with the portal closed.

1. Open **Profile** (top of the menu). Under **Phone alerts**, press **Turn on alerts** and allow notifications. The first page of the portal also offers it once.
2. Under **What to alert me about**: new requests, booking changes and messages are on for staff; payments are off until you tick them.
3. **Send a test alert** checks the device. **Remove** takes an old phone off.

On an iPhone, add CarmaCars to the Home Screen first (Safari, **Share**, **Add to Home Screen**). Use your phone''s own Focus or Do Not Disturb for quiet hours.

### Search

The **Search** button at the top of every page (or press **/** where the page has no search box of its own) finds pages and the records your role may open: bookings and requests by number, renter name, email, phone or plate, renters, owners and cars.

### A VIN from the car

VIN fields have **Scan the barcode** (the barcode in the driver''s door frame or under the windshield) and **Photo of the VIN**. Check what was read against the car before saving.

## Alerts by email

Alerts that are not urgent come together in one email at most once an hour; urgent ones (a payment declined, documents to review for a pickup within 2 hours, the site down) still come on their own. Every alert is in the bell and on your phone at once. Choose on **Profile**, Notifications: alerts by email, **Change how often**: Hourly digest, Daily digest (07:00) or Off.

> Tip: To change the email you sign in with, open Profile, Sign-in and press **Change my email**: type the new address, and we send a confirmation link to it and tell the old address. Your email changes only when the link is opened, and every record of yours follows it.', 'Shared tools', 'The calendar and Find a renter.',
