-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The calendar</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Every car with its photo, its bookings, requests and blocks, in the colours of the legend above it: on rent, confirmed, request, offer or hold, maintenance, block. The red line is now. Tap a bar for its details; on a phone it opens on the agenda, by day.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Use the arrows, Today and the range to move around, or search by car, plate, booking or name.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">With many cars (release 48): filter by <b class="gd-ui">Car status</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Class</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Availability</b> (Fleet and Finance also by owner), and <b class="gd-ui">Group by</b> class, status or availability; press a heading to fold its cars away. The count says how many cars show and how many are free today. <b class="gd-ui">Clear</b> takes the filters off.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A return is a check-out. Under the bars, a trip that ends has two jobs as small chips: <b class="gd-ui">Check-out</b> with its time (once the car is back, the time it actually came back) and <b class="gd-ui">Cleaning</b> (the post-trip cleaning). A tick means done. A booking&#39;s side panel says Pickup (check-in) and Return (check-out).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Fleet and customer service can remove the post-trip cleaning from its side panel (<b class="gd-ui">Remove the block</b>) when a car is ready sooner.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/calendar</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/800"><img src="/guides/img/va-cs-09-calendar-desktop-541a6da5.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="800"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:60.2%;top:33.8%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:28.5%;top:17.5%" aria-hidden="true">2</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="shared-tools-find-a-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Find a car</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Bookings</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Find a car</b> tab. A renter quotes the car code on the car&#39;s page (like CC-7F3A).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Type the car code, a plate, a VIN or the name. Each car shows its code, plate, status and its page on the site.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">In Add a rental, type the car code or plate in the box above Car to choose it.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="shared-tools-find-a-renter" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Find a renter</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Search by name, email, phone or booking number.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Opening a renter&#39;s private details asks for a reason (<b class="gd-ui">Open with a reason</b>). It is kept in the access log.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The renter&#39;s record has <b class="gd-ui">Add a note</b> and the <b class="gd-ui">Activity</b> log: everything about the renter, newest first, with a chip per type (All by default), <b class="gd-ui">Search the activity</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Older</b> for the next 50, and <b class="gd-ui">Email</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Text</b>. Fleet does not see payments in it.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/renters</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/240"><img src="/guides/img/va-cs-07-renters-desktop-99cfd0ef.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="240"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:68.3%;top:34.6%" aria-hidden="true">1</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="shared-tools-email-the-renter" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Email the renter</h2><p class="gd-p">Customer service, Sales, Fleet and Finance can all write to the renter from a booking: press <b class="gd-ui">Email the renter</b>, or open the <b class="gd-ui">Messages &amp; history</b> section.</p><p class="gd-p">The booking page, the car page and the listing review are the same pages an Admin opens. The car page has the Admin&#39;s tabs your function uses: <b class="gd-ui">Overview</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Rates &amp; fees</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Maintenance</b> (Fleet), <b class="gd-ui">Listing</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Documents</b>; an old link to a car&#39;s maintenance opens its Maintenance tab. You see the sections and buttons of your function: Finance has the money, the refunds and the deposit; Fleet the field jobs, the handovers and the car&#39;s rates; customer service the review and offer, changes and extensions; Sales the requests and offers.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Write a <b class="gd-ui">Subject</b> and a <b class="gd-ui">Message</b>, or pick a <b class="gd-ui">Quick reply</b> to start from.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Email the renter</b>. It goes from CarmaCars and the renter can answer in their account; the answer opens a task for customer service.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">On a booking an insurer pays you can choose Blind Spot Car Rental (insurance) as the sender, and <b class="gd-ui">Email the adjuster</b> writes to the adjuster on the booking.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">The form is under the booking&#39;s Activity log (release 35), which lists the messages both ways, every email of the booking, the texts, chat, calls, notes and the rest, newest first, with a chip per type and a search. Each email counts against the daily email limit, shown under the form with today&#39;s number.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">Find a booking</h3><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Bookings</b>: type at least 3 characters of the booking number (CC-1042, 1042), the renter&#39;s or a driver&#39;s name, an email, a phone number, a plate or a car code, then press Enter. <b class="gd-ui">My bookings</b> lists yours, with your commission. Every search is logged, as Find a renter.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="shared-tools-phone-alerts" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Phone alerts</h2><p class="gd-p">Get an alert on your phone or computer for new requests, replies to answer and urgent problems, even with the portal closed.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Profile</b> (top of the menu). Under <b class="gd-ui">Phone alerts</b>, press <b class="gd-ui">Turn on alerts</b> and allow notifications. The first page of the portal also offers it once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Under <b class="gd-ui">What to alert me about</b>: new requests, booking changes and messages are on for staff; payments are off until you tick them.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Send a test alert</b> checks the device. <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> takes an old phone off.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">On an iPhone, add CarmaCars to the Home Screen first (Safari, <b class="gd-ui">Share</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Add to Home Screen</b>). Use your phone&#39;s own Focus or Do Not Disturb for quiet hours.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">Search</h3><p class="gd-p">The <b class="gd-ui">Search</b> button at the top of every page (or press <b class="gd-ui">/</b> where the page has no search box of its own) finds pages and the records your role may open: bookings and requests by number, renter name, email, phone or plate, renters, owners and cars.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">A VIN from the car</h3><p class="gd-p">VIN fields have <b class="gd-ui">Scan the barcode</b> (the barcode in the driver&#39;s door frame or under the windshield) and <b class="gd-ui">Photo of the VIN</b>. Check what was read against the car before saving.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="shared-tools-alerts-by-email" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Alerts by email</h2><p class="gd-p">Alerts that are not urgent come together in one email at most once an hour; urgent ones (a payment declined, documents to review for a pickup within 2 hours, the site down) still come on their own. Every alert is in the bell and on your phone at once. Choose on <b class="gd-ui">Profile</b>, Notifications: alerts by email, <b class="gd-ui">Change how often</b>: Hourly digest, Daily digest (07:00) or Off.</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>To change the email you sign in with, open Profile, Sign-in and press <b class="gd-ui">Change my email</b>: type the new address, and we send a confirmation link to it and tell the old address. Your email changes only when the link is opened, and every record of yours follows it.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="shared-tools-more-than-one-role-one-portal-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">More than one role? One portal (release 48)</h2><p class="gd-p">If your account has more than one role (Sales and Field work, or you also own a car with us), there is no &quot;Choose a portal&quot; stop any more.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Working as</b>, at the top of every page, lists every role you have. The one you are in is black; press another to work in it. Your staff functions are there too, as before.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Pages of your other roles</b>, under it, goes straight to the most used pages of a role you are not in right now.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Signing in opens the role you used last on this device.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">What you may open has not changed: each page still checks your role.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="shared-tools-possible-wrong-person-at-pickup" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Possible wrong person at pickup</h2><p class="gd-p">At a pickup, staff (and a renter checking in alone) can take a photo of the licence the person is holding. It is compared with the licence and selfie on file (name, licence number, expiry and face), and the card shown is compared with the card on file by its last four digits and its name. The card is never photographed.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A mismatch raises an urgent To do, <b class="gd-ui">Possible wrong person at pickup</b>, for Fleet and for Admin (Fleet sees it on To do), with what did not match, and a staff alert. The booking page shows the same mark at the top, with each line of the check.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Review the licence</b> on the booking: the photos taken at the pickup are listed with the licence and selfie on file. Press <b class="gd-ui">View</b> on each to compare them side by side.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Call the staff member at the car if the keys have not been handed over. Finish the To do once you have looked: the mark on the booking goes with it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">On a rental covered by the renter&#39;s credit card, a card that is not in the renter&#39;s own name is also raised as <b class="gd-ui">Coverage problem at pickup</b>.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>The check is optional and never stops a handover by itself. Every check, matched or not, is kept as evidence and goes into the dispute pack.</div></aside></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('field', 'a-handover', 'chapter', 'my-jobs', 'You give the renter the keys only after every check passes. The whole handover is one screen: each part has a green tick once it is done, and the button at the bottom says what is still needed.

> Good to know: The job''s header shows how much of the rental walkthrough the renter has read, for example "Renter''s walkthrough: read 2 of 6 steps". Below 6, walk them through the rest at the car: what to bring, the walk-around, the road rules and the return.

> Watch out: Finish the handover in the app, to the last step. Until the pickup is recorded the renter''s messages and the office''s records are guesses: 30 minutes after the pickup time you get an alert and a text to record it, or to mark a no-show.

## Before you start: the ready check

The first part lists what must be done before the car can go: signed, paid, ID checked, deposit. When everything is ready it is one green line; open **The six checks** to see them.

1. Each line should show a green tick: agreement signed, identity verified, coverage confirmed, additional drivers accepted, the booking holds the calendar, deposit taken.
2. A red line shows what you can do about it right under it (see the next part). Fix it, then press **Check again**.
3. All green? Go on down the screen.
4. Coverage or the calendar not ready? Only the office fixes those: call CarmaCars. Still not ready? Press **Stop: do not release the car**.

![](/guides/img/field-21-handover-01-ready-phone-ecb54c56.jpg "phone; size: 390 410; pins: 1 91.0 63.4")

> Watch out: Never hand over keys if the ready check fails, the renter does not match the photo on file, or they do not have their original licence or the card on file. Stop and call us.

## Fix the ready check on the spot

Most red lines are fixed on your phone, without calling the office. Everything you do is recorded with your name.

1. Agreement not signed: press **Sign now on this device** and hand the phone to the renter. A copy signed on paper is not accepted.
2. Identity not verified: for each driver, press **Take** for the licence front, the back and the selfie. Hold the original licence: tick that the name matches, the photo is the person, it is valid past the return and it is class G2 or G. No expiry on file? Type the licence number and the expiry. Press **The licence checks out**.
3. Deposit not taken: press **Card hold: hand this phone to the renter**. They type their card in Stripe''s secure form; take the phone back and press **Back to the job**.
4. Paid by e-Transfer instead: open **Paid by e-Transfer**, type the reference number from their confirmation and press **Record the e-Transfer**.
5. Paid in cash: open **Paid in cash**, count the amount in front of the renter and press **I received**. Keep the cash apart from your own money and hand it to CarmaCars within 1 business day, as Finance directs: Finance gets a task to collect it from you.
6. Additional driver not accepted: press **Sign now on this device (additional driver)**.

> Tip: An expired licence, a face that does not match or a renter who will not sign: do not fix it. Press Stop and call us.

## The handover, on one screen

With the car already? On the job, **Start the check-in now** acknowledges, starts and opens the screen in one tap.

1. **Renter, licence and card**: three taps. This is the renter named on the booking; you checked the original licence (name, photo, not expired; a photo of a licence is not enough); you saw the physical card with the same last four digits. Something is wrong? Open **Something is wrong** and press what it is: the handover stops and the office is told.
2. **Odometer, fuel and keys**: already filled in when the car reports them (from the Tracker, else from its last report). Check each against the dash and change what differs. Fuel: tap the level on the gauge, in eighths from E to F. Keys: **+** and **−**.
3. **Photos**: 19 photos, one tap each. **Take this photo** always shows the next angle; **All 19 photos** lists them, with **Retake**.
4. **Damage**: nothing new? Leave it. New damage: open it, tap the car diagram where it is, choose Where and Type, press **Add the damage** and take the close-up.
5. **Tracker**: one green line when it reports. If not, **Check again**. The car has to go anyway? Open **The car has to go anyway?**, say why and press **Release without the tracker**: an Admin is told at once.
6. **Review and sign**: the renter reads the summary and signs, then you. **Use this signature** for each.
7. Press **Hand over the keys**. You see "Checked in. The rental has started." The renter gets the photo report by email and in their Documents.

Not everything in yet? The button above it says what is next (for example "Next: Odometer") and takes you there. A note for Fleet (anything missing or not clean) is under **Add a note for Fleet**.

![](/guides/img/field-29-handover-09-photos-phone-767ecd4f.jpg "phone; size: 390 350")

> Good to know: You were interrupted? Open the job again: your answers and photos are where you left them.

> Tip: Photos wait on the phone without a connection and upload by themselves when it returns; the count shows what is still uploading. Each photo keeps its time, and the place when your phone allows location. No signal on a step? It says "Answers kept on this phone" and you can go on: press Try again, or they are sent when the signal returns.

## Sign now on this device

The renter (or an additional driver) has not signed the rental agreement yet? They sign on your phone.

1. On the job, press **Sign now on this device**. It shows who still has to sign and whether their licence is on file.
2. Check the person: the name matches their licence, and you saw the original licence. Tick both. No licence on file? Press **Photograph: Licence, front** (and the back and the selfie).
3. Press **Hand the device to** and their name. They read the agreements (CarmaCars'' and Blind Spot''s), tick the statements and sign with their name or their finger.
4. They hand the phone back: press **Back to the staff view**. The signature record says it was signed in person, collected by you, on your phone.

## The agreements at check-in

Both rental agreements follow the check-in.

1. Signing at pickup? Record the odometer and the fuel on the check-in first, then hand over the device: the agreement then shows the time, kilometres and fuel out, and the signed copy holds them.
2. The signer gets a code on their phone, initials the key terms, ticks the consents and draws their signature.
3. Already signed online? When you complete the check-in, the "as picked up" copy of both agreements is made with your readings and your countersignature, and emailed to the renter.
4. The check-in stops if the agreement is missing something a claim needs (a licence expiry, a VIN). Ask the office to fill it on the booking, or an Admin to override.

## The deposit on your phone

Deposit not taken yet? The ready check shows how to take it under the Deposit line. You never type a card number.

1. Press **Card hold: hand this phone to the renter**. They type their credit card in Stripe''s secure form and press the button with the amount.
2. They see "Hold placed": take the phone back and press **Back to the job**. The ready check shows the deposit taken.
3. A rental longer than the hold limit shows **Save the card on this phone (long rental)** instead: Finance charges the deposit to that card.
4. No credit card? When CarmaCars allows it, the renter pays the deposit by e-Transfer or in cash: record it under the Deposit line.

## Add-ons to put in the car

A booking may come with add-ons: a baby seat, a child or booster seat, flowers, an umbrella, a phone charger or a prepaid full tank.

1. Open the job. Under Put in the car you see each add-on, how many, and what to do (for example "Put the bouquet on the front passenger seat").
2. Put every item in the car before the handover. The screen lists them again under the readings.
3. Prepaid fuel: the renter may return the car at any fuel level. Do not charge for fuel at the return.
4. A chauffeur on the booking: Fleet tells you who drives and when.

> Tip: An item missing? Write it under **Add a note for Fleet** and call the office before the handover.

> Tip: The photo count shows "19 of 19 photos taken · all uploaded" when the set is complete. The first photo must show the plate. Open circles on the damage diagram were recorded before; add only what is new.

## On one screen (release 28)

On the booking page the check-in is one screen: the time, km, fuel, and many photos picked at once from the camera roll, with the suggested angles as a checklist. If the renter checked in themselves, add your photos to theirs. It is under **Check in with photos already taken (from the gallery)**; the button above it opens the one-screen handover described here.

## When a check stops the handover (release 33)
When something stops the pickup or the return (the deposit, a signature, the licence, the car''s status) and the trip must go ahead, the job shows **What stops the pickup now** with each check. Press **Ask an Admin to override the pickup** (or the return), give the actual time, the km and fuel if you know them, and why. An Admin approves in one tap and the handover is recorded with the time you entered; add the photos and readings afterwards on the job, as with any handover recorded now.

## Picked up, deposit pending (release 48)
When the renter cannot place the deposit hold at the pickup (the card is declined, the bank wants a call) and the car must go, you can let it go with the deposit owed. On the job, under the deposit line, open **Let the car go with the deposit owed**, say why, and go on with the check-in. On a booking, **Record the pickup now** has the box **Deposit not taken yet: let the car go owing it, because**, and the check-in panel has **Deposit not taken: let the car go owing it**. The booking then shows **Deposit pending $X** everywhere. Each morning the renter''s saved card is tried once; if that fails, the renter gets the deposit link by text (or email). After 48 hours an Admin gets a To do. You do nothing more: once the deposit is taken the chip changes by itself.', 'A handover', 'The ready check, ID, card, odometer, photos, damage, signatures and the keys.',
